    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:964778/": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer in Crisis preparedness and Civil Defence with a Focus on Social Vulnerability and Critical Perspectives",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer in Crisis preparedness and Civil Defence with a Focus on Social Vulnerability and Critical Perspectives Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Senior Lecturer in Crisis preparedness and Civil Defence with a Focus on Social Vulnerability and Critical Perspectives Login and apply Lund University, LTH, Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Department of Building and Environmental Technology at LTH, Lund University, is recruiting an Senior Lecturer. The Division of Risk Management and Societal Safety, within the Department of Building and Environmental Technology, conducts research and education in the field of societal risk and crisis management. The focus of both our research and teaching is to develop knowledge of how individuals, organizations, and societies prevent, prepare for, manage, recover from, learn from, and adapt to events that may threaten something of value. We also conduct research aimed at developing methods, processes, and other types of artefacts that can be used to better understand and manage risks, crises, and disasters across a wide range of contexts. The division currently employs 23 staff members, and an additional 8 individuals are affiliated with the division, such as adjunct faculty staff and industrial PhD students. The division's academic staff and researchers represent a broad range of backgrounds and expertise, including engineering, psychology, and sociology. This position is intended to strengthen the division's capacity in the field of crisis preparedness and management, and civil defence, with a particular focus on social vulnerability. Crisis preparedness and management in general, and civil defence in particular, are areas experiencing rapid growth in Sweden. We anticipate that substantial research funding will be allocated to these fields in the coming years, creating significant opportunities for research and development . Subject Crisis preparedness and Civil Defence with a Focus on Social Vulnerability and Critical Perspectives Subject description The position of Senior Lecturer primarily involves research and teaching focusing on social vulnerability, power, identity, and critical perspectives on complex crises, both in peacetime and during periods of heightened preparedness. During crises, disasters, and conflicts, different groups in society are affected in different ways depending on their social, economic, and organizational circumstances. Crises often expose and amplify existing inequalities, making it more difficult for some groups to access information, resources, support, and influence over decision-making processes. At the same time, power relations between public authorities, civil society organizations, voluntary initiatives, and individual citizens emerge and evolve, shaping both the distribution of responsibilities and opportunities for different actors to make their voices heard. To understand the societal consequences of crises, it is therefore essential to analyse how different forms of vulnerability are created, reinforced, and managed, as well as how power is exercised, negotiated, and contested during acute events. Such perspectives can contribute to a more nuanced understanding of which groups are at risk of marginalization during crises and which measures are required to create more equitable and inclusive approaches to crisis management and societal resilience. Particular emphasis in this position is placed on qualitative research approaches. The ability to employ qualitative methods to analyse influence, power dynamics, and social relationships is therefore essential. The focus is especially on understanding the factors beyond formal structures and hierarchies that shape how crisis management, emergency preparedness, and civil defence actually function in practice, which may differ considerably from how they have been planned and designed in advance. Furthermore, qualitative research methods are employed in the majority of master's degree projects conducted within the Division of Risk Management and Societal Safety. For this reason, the division seeks to strengthen its competence and capacity in qualitative research methodology. Work duties Work duties include: Research within the subject area. Teaching in the first, second and third cycles of studies. Supervision of degree projects and doctoral students. Actively seeking external research funding. Collaboration with industry and wider society. Administration related to the work duties listed above. Strategic work aimed at establishing and strengthening collaborations between LTH and relevant national and international partners Qualification requirements Appointment to senior lecturer requires that the applicant has: A PhD or corresponding research competence or professional expertise considered important with regard to the subject matter of the post and the work duties it will involve. Demonstrated teaching expertise. Completed five weeks of training in higher education teaching and learning, or acquired equivalent knowledge by other means, unless there are valid reasons. Assessment criteria When assessing the applicants, special importance will be given to research and teaching expertise within the subject, assessing research and teaching expertise equally. The assessment criteria specify the aspects to be taken into account, and the level to be achieved, in order for the assessment criteria to be deemed fulfilled. The following assessment criteria must be fulfilled for appointment to senior lecturer: A good national and international standing as a researcher. The requirement for international experience shall be assessed with consideration to the character and traditions of the subject. Good teaching ability, including a good ability to conduct, develop and lead teaching and other educational activities on different levels and using a variety of teaching methods. An ability to supervise doctoral students to achieve a PhD. An ability to collaborate with wider society and communicate his or her activities. A general ability to lead and develop activities. Additional requirements Very good oral and written proficiency in English. Good oral and written proficiency in Swedish. Experience of teaching, course development, and research using qualitative research methodology. Collaborative skills, initiative and the ability to solve work tasks independently. Other qualifications Significant documented research experience (e.g. from postdoc or doctoral studies) from another university/institute or relevant experience from industry/public sector. Experience of conducting research, both independently and collaboratively, within the fields of crisis preparedness, crisis management, social vulnerability, civil society issues, and critical perspective. The extent to which the applicant, through their experience and skills, may complement and strengthen ongoing research, undergraduate education, departmental innovation, and how they can contribute to the future development of the department will also be taken into consideration. We offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme.  Read more on the University website about being a Lund University employee: https://www.lunduniversity.lu.se/about-university/work-lund-university. Instructions on how to apply Applications shall be written in English. Please draw up the application in accordance with LTH’s Academic qualifications portfolio – see link below. Upload the application as PDF-files in the recruitment system. Read more: http://www.lth.se/english/working-at-lth/to-apply-for-academic-positions-at-lth/ We welcome your application! LTH is Lund University’s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers – many of whom work in world-leading profile areas – publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create – to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time First day of employment As soon as possible Salary Monthly Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 % City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2529 Union representative SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2229364,kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362,st@st.lu.se Published 02.Oct.2026 Last application date 27.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:970914/": {
      "title": "Research Engineer",
      "description": "Research Engineer Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Research Engineer Login and apply Lunds universitet Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the Research Group The research group for Diabetes and Cardiovascular Disease – Genetic Epidemiology conducts clinical/epidemiological research in diet, genes, gut microbiome and their connection to type 2 diabetes and other cardiometabolic diseases. Research has been at the forefront of the field of diet, multifactorial genetics and gut microbiota for several years. The group is led by Professor Marju Orho-Melander and consists of both research and technical staff. The activities are located at the Clinical Research Center (CRC) in Malmö. Within the research group, we care about a good work environment with respect and consideration in our relationships with each other and strive for a workplace that is experienced as developing and stimulating for all employees. We are constantly working to create conditions for job satisfaction, development and participation for all employees. We protect both physical safety and the psychosocial work environment. What We Offer Lund University is a public authority, which means that you are entitled to special benefits, generous annual leave, and a favorable occupational pension. We also have a flextime agreement, which contributes to good conditions for a healthy work–life balance. Read more on the University’s website about being employed at Lund University: Work with us Work duties and areas of responsibility We are looking for a driven research engineer to assist researchers and students in the research group with genetic and bioinformatic analyses of genome wide association data, gut microbiome- and other omics data, and clinical data. Qualifications Requirements for this position: MSc in medical sciences, public health sciences or equivalent. Knowledge and documented experience in epidemiological and genetic/epigenetic analyses and research on type 2 diabetes or related cardiometabolic diseases. Documented programming and statistical analysis skills in both R and Python. Documented experience in analyzing large complex data sets with advanced analysis methods. Experience in working with molecular, clinical, epidemiological and/or lifestyle related data and integrating information from different data sources. Documented experience in summarizing and presenting results in a reproducible report including publication-ready tables and figures, and writing scientific articles. Great importance will be placed on personal qualities. The tasks require that you have good collaboration skills that fit in an interdisciplinary team, that you are self-motivated, flexible and can work independently in a well-documented manner. Other personal qualities required are that you are easy to take initiative, are flexible and have good communication skills. Desirable Qualifications: Experience in scientific data communication of complex quantitative results. Understanding of clinical research questions, experience of patient-facing work and/or clinical education (medical doctor, nurse or other) Additional Information This is a speciall fixed-term employment (SÄVA) for the period 2026-12-01 until 2027-04-30 , at 100 % full-time. How to Apply The position must be applied for through the University’s recruitment system. Your application should include a cover letter describing how you meet the qualification requirements and why you are interested in the position. The application should also include your CV, a copy of your degree certificate, and any other documents you wish to submit in support of your application (such as transcripts, contact details for references, letters of recommendation, etc.). The Faculty of Medicine is a part of Lund University, and is responsible for education and research within medicine and healthcare. Our academic programs are closely linked with the healthcare system and are firmly anchored in the faculty’s strong research tradition. Our research spans a broad field within experimental preclinical research, near-patient clinical research and health sciences research. The Faculty of Medicine, with its 1,800 employees and 2,700 students in Lund and Malmö, is a knowledge-intensive meeting place for students, teachers and researchers from all over the world. The Department of Clinical Sciences, Malmö is one of the six departments at the Faculty of Medicine, Lund University. We have a strong focus on clinical and epidemiological research and also conduct an extensive preclinical laboratory research. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Special fixed-term employment Contract type Full time First day of employment 2026-12-01 Salary Månadslön Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Malmö County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2729 Contact Marju Orho-Melander, Rekryterande chef, +4640391210, marju.orho-melander@med.lu.se Sarah Quist, HR-partner, +4640391055, sarah.quist@med.lu.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 02.Oct.2026 Last application date 17.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:972522/": {
      "title": "Researcher in nanowire solar cell development for space applications",
      "description": "Researcher in nanowire solar cell development for space applications Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Researcher in nanowire solar cell development for space applications Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The position is placed at the Division of Solid-State Physics at the Department of Physics, a division with around 100 employees where extensive research is carried out centered on various aspects of nanophysics, ranging from materials science to bio- and quantum physics to various applications. The division is a central part of NanoLund, Lund University's large interdisciplinary research center on nanoscience and nanotechnology. The research center includes also Lund Nano Lab, a central and shared cleanroom facility for the production of materials and components at the nanoscale. The Division has a strong commitment to undergraduate education, not least in the Master's programme \"Engineering Nanoscience\" at LTH. Work duties In this position, you will be responsible for the development of nanowire solar cells for space applications. The ZEUS project focuses on advancing the development of innovative and radiation-resistant nanowire solar cells with high efficiency. While current space-tested nanowire solar cells offer around 15% efficiency with single-bandgap cells, ZEUS aims to significantly improve this efficiency, potentially up to 47%, by using triple-junction nanowire cells using III-V semiconductor materials. The project aims to achieve scalability by transferring nanowire solar cells to lightweight, flexible substrates. The main objectives include: Increase the efficiency of radiation-resistant nanowire solar cells. Scale up the substrate size to 100 mm^2 and develop modules with a size of 1x1 cm2. Reduce weight and material usage through nanowire peeling and substrate reuse. The project is an EIC pathfinder challenge project, which may require travel for project meetings and collaboration with the other partners within the project. Description of the work duties: The tasks as a researcher mainly include conducting research. The purpose of the position is to develop your independence as a researcher and create conditions for further qualifications. You will work with the synthesis of nanowires, surface passivation and to process these into solar cells for space applications. Characterization of the nanowires and their evaluation with respect to external quantum efficiency (EQE) and current-voltage characterization (IV), also inside a scanning electron microscope, will be part of the project. Qualifications Appointment to a position as a researcher requires that the applicant has a PhD degree. Proof that the eligibility requirement has been met must be received no later than the time the employment decision is made. Required qualifications : a PhD in physics or chemistry very good oral and written proficiency in English. experience in epitaxy, MOVPE and nanowire growth of III-V materials. experience in cleanroom and semiconductor sample processing, like wet chemical etching, photolithography, metal evaporation, etc. strong independence excellent collaboration skills Additional requirements: previous meritorious post doc position, experience of research in a laboratory environment after dissertation. electro-optical characterization of nanowire-based structures (I-V, EQE, PL, EBIC, photocurrent measurements) nano scale device fabrication. material characterisation by use of EDX, SEM, TEM. We Offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. Read more on the University website about being a Lund University employee . Further information The position is a fixed term position for 20270116 – 20271230  at 100 per cent of full time. Researchers are covered by a local collective agreement on annual working hours for researchers and assistant researchers. The planning of annual working hours is done in dialogue between the manager and the employee. How to apply Applications are to be submitted via the University’s recruitment system. The application should include a CV and a personal letter justifying your interest in the position and how it matches your qualifications. The application should also include a degree certificate or equivalent and any other document to which you would like to draw attention (copies of grade transcripts, details of referees, letters of recommendation, etc.)” We welcome your application! LTH is Lund University’s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers – many of whom work in world-leading profile areas – publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create – to benefit the world. The Department of Physics is with a staff of about 400 scientists and educators one of the largest departments within Lund University. There are seven research divisions and a number of research centra within the department. The research activities at the department cover a broad spectrum of modern physics. www.fysik.lu.se/english. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Special fixed-term employment Employment expires 2027-12-31 Contract type Full time First day of employment 2027-01-16 Salary Månadslön Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2777 Contact Magnus Borgström, Professor, +46462221494, magnus.borgstrom@fysik.lu.se Emmy Heidenblad, HR-partner, +46462229294, emmy.heidenblad@lth.lu.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 02.Oct.2026 Last application date 16.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:963933/": {
      "title": "Research Infrastructure Specialist in AI/ML",
      "description": "Research Infrastructure Specialist in AI/ML Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Research Infrastructure Specialist in AI/ML Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace LUNARC is a centre at Lund University providing services in high-performance computing (HPC), visualisation, and data storage. We support researchers across the university with advanced infrastructure, expertise, and training. This position is part of a national investment in AI within the Swedish AI Factory, the Swedish node of the EuroHPC AI Factory initiative. In this role, you will work at the intersection of advanced AI research, research infrastructure, and education, in close collaboration with national and international partners. Work duties As a Research Infrastructure Specialist in AI/ML, you will play a key role in strengthening the use of AI within Swedish research, with a particular focus on education and skills development. Your responsibilities will include: Developing and delivering training activities in AI/ML (courses, workshops, seminars) for LU researchers and users of Swedish AI Factory. Contributing to the development of educational materials and long-term training initiatives in AI Supporting researchers in applying AI methods at Swedish AI Factory resources. Contributing to the development and optimisation of AI workflows on HPC infrastructure Participating in national and international collaborations within Swedish AI Factory and EuroHPC Contributing to outreach and dissemination of knowledge in AI and its applications Qualifications Requirements PhD in a relevant field such as Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Computer Science, Computational Science or other field that the employer finds relevant for the position Documented experience using and developing AI tools and models. Hands-on experience with modern AI frameworks such as PyTorch, TensorFlow, or equivalent Strong programming skills in Python and experience working in Linux/Unix environments Documented experience in teaching, training, or course development Ability to work both independently and collaboratively with researchers and research groups Excellent communication skills in English, both written and spoken Merits Experience in developing and delivering courses or training programmes in AI/ML Experience working with research infrastructure, e.g. HPC, large-scale storage, or distributed systems Experience supporting users or researchers in AI-related projects Experience from international collaborations, e.g. EU or EuroHPC projects Experience collaborating with industry or public sector organisations Experience with generative AI and large language models Further information The position is a permanent poisition full-time (100%). Start date by agreement, at the latest April 2027. The position is based in Lund, Sweden. Application Applications should be submitted through Lund University’s recruitment system and include a CV, a cover letter describing your qualifications and motivation, and relevant supporting documents. LTH is Lund University’s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers – many of whom work in world-leading profile areas – publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create – to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time First day of employment By agreement, at the latest April 2027 Salary Månadslön Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2512 Contact Jonas Lindemann, Avdelningsföreståndare, jonas.lindemann@lunarc.lu.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 01.Oct.2026 Last application date 29.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:969247/": {
      "title": "Utbildningskoordinator",
      "description": "Utbildningskoordinator Logga in och sök jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Utbildningskoordinator Logga in och sök jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas återkommande som ett av världens främsta lärosäten. Här finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malmö. Vi förenas i vår strävan att förstå, förklara och förbättra vår värld och människors villkor. Lunds universitet välkomnar sökande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. Jämställdhet, lika villkor och mångfald är grundläggande principer för alla delar av vår verksamhet. Utbildningskoordinator Är du noggrann, strukturerad och van vid att snabbt sätta dig in i administrativa system? Trivs du i en föränderlig miljö med nära kontakt med studenter och lärare? Vi söker dig som är serviceinriktad och initiativrik, arbetar väl både självständigt och tillsammans med andra samt kan prioritera vid hög arbetsbelastning. Då kan du vara den utbildningskoordinator vi söker till Institutionen för psykologi. Arbetsuppgifter och ansvarsområden Som utbildningskoordinator ansvarar du för att planera, organisera, administrera och samordna olika aspekter av utbildning så som antagningsarbete, studiedokumentation och studieplanering. Du har både ett helhets- och detaljperspektiv. Du samarbetar med kollegor för att bedriva och utveckla utbildning och processer. Arbetet sker i olika administrativa team. Arbetet innebär exempelvis att: •    planera och genomföra antagningsarbete •    ansvara för utbildnings- och studieadministration i universitetets administrativa system •    handlägga studieadministrativa ärenden och utfärda intyg •    ge information, service och stöd till nuvarande och presumtiva studenter •    uppdatera utbildningsinformation på webben •    administrera utbildningsutbud, kurser och kursplaner •    bidra till utveckling av utbildningsadministrativa processer och arbetssätt •    tillämpa regler och riktlinjer inom utbildningsområdet •    hantera dokumentation, informationshantering och diarieföring •    samverka med lärare, studierektorer, program- och kursansvariga samt övriga administrativa funktioner •    delta i relevanta interna nätverk inom Lunds universitet •    ansvara för viss samordning inom ekonomiadministrativa system •    koordinera, administrera och återrapportera anställningsformer samt samordna avtals- och anställningsfrågor med studierektor, kursansvariga, ekonomiansvarig och anställda •    boka resor/hotell. Kvalifikationer Krav: •    Kandidatexamen inom samhällsvetenskapligt ämne, eller annan utbildning/erfarenhet som arbetsgivaren bedömer som likvärdig •    God förmåga att uttrycka dig på svenska och engelska i tal och skrift •    God datorvana och erfarenhet av att arbeta i IT-system och digitala verktyg Meriterande: •    Erfarenhet av administrativa och/eller koordinerande arbetsuppgifter •    Erfarenhet av serviceinriktat arbete •    Personliga egenskaper som initiativtagande, ansvarstagande och att vara utvecklingsorienterad samt god förmåga att snabbt sätta dig in i nya arbetsuppgifter, ta till dig instruktioner och se både helhet och detaljer Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet är en statlig myndighet vilket innebär att du får särskilda förmåner, generös semester och en förmånlig tjänstepension. Institutionen för psykologi är en hybrid arbetsplats där möjlighet att arbeta på distans upp till 2 dagar i veckan finns. Vi har även ett flextidavtal som skapar goda förutsättningar för balans mellan arbete och fritid. Läs mer på universitetets webbplats om att vara anställd vid Lunds universitet: Jobba hos oss. Övrigt Anställningen är en tillsvidaretjänst med tillträde 2027-01-01 eller enligt överenskommelse. Provanställning på 6 månader kan komma att tillämpas . Tjänstens uppgifter kan komma att förändras över tid. Ansökan Anställningen söks via universitetets rekryteringssystem. Samhällsvetenskapliga fakulteten vid Lunds universitet är ett av landets ledande kunskapscentra för forskning och utbildning inom samhälls- och beteendevetenskap. Med verksamhet i både Lund och Helsingborg, över 700 anställda och cirka 5 700 helårsstudenter är fakulteten en av Lunds universitets största. Vi erbjuder en kreativ akademisk miljö med engagerade studenter och medarbetare. Vår huvuduppgift är att utveckla, förmedla och förvalta kunskap om samhälle, människa och organisationer i en miljö som präglas av öppenhet, tolerans och nyfikenhet. Institutionen för psykologi kombinerar utbildning med forskning och har under senare år varit mycket framgångsrik i konkurrensen om externa forskningsmedel. Centrala forskningsområden är bl.a. arbets- och organisationspsykologi, klinisk psykologi, kognition, neuropsykologi, personlighet- och social psykologi samt utvecklingspsykologi. Många av våra kurser är utvecklade i anslutning till forskningsprojekt och studenterna får möjlighet att ta del av aktuella forskningsrön från lärare som själva är aktiva forskare inom sina respektive områden. Vår utbildningsmiljö är sedan länge starkt internationaliserad. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter från annonsförsäljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsföretag på grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anställningsform Tillsvidare med provanställning Anställningens omfattning Heltid Tillträde 2027-01-01 Löneform Månadslön Antal lediga befattningar 1 Sysselsättningsgrad 100 Ort Lund Län Skåne län Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2686 Kontakt Caroline Hansson, HR-Administratör, caroline.hansson@sam.lu.se Sofia Bunke, Prefekt, +46462221537, sofia.bunke@psy.lu.se Facklig företrädare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-01 Sista ansökningsdag 2026-10-25 Logga in och sök jobbet Dela länkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillgänglighetsredogörelse × Modal title Vi använder cookies för inloggning, förbättrad användarupplevelse, dela-länkar samt i vissa fall marknadsföring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast nödvändiga Läs mer om våra cookies här ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:973191/": {
      "title": "Ekonomiadministratör till medicinska institutionskansliet i Malmö",
      "description": "Ekonomiadministratör till medicinska institutionskansliet i Malmö Logga in och sök jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Ekonomiadministratör till medicinska institutionskansliet i Malmö Logga in och sök jobbet Lunds universitet Medicinska fakulteten Inst för kliniska vetenskaper Malmö Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas återkommande som ett av världens främsta lärosäten. Här finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malmö. Vi förenas i vår strävan att förstå, förklara och förbättra vår värld och människors villkor. Lunds universitet välkomnar sökande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. Jämställdhet, lika villkor och mångfald är grundläggande principer för alla delar av vår verksamhet. Beskrivning av arbetsplatsen Medicinska institutionskansliet i Malmö är ett gemensamt kansli för två av Medicinska fakultetens institutioner vilka är placerade i Malmö; Institutionen för kliniska vetenskaper Malmö och Institutionen för translationell medicin. Här finns patientnära forskningsmiljöer för de forskargrupper som är aktiva vid institutionerna. Dessa har sammanlagt ca 400 anställda, däribland även associerade medarbetare som är anställda inom Region Skåne. Institutionerna bedriver forskning och utbildning, både inom medicinsk grundutbildning och forskarutbildning Kansliets huvudsakliga uppgift är att avlasta kärnverksamheten och möjliggöra forskning och utbildning av hög kvalitet. Kansliet ansvarar för att säkerställa att lärosätet uppfyller både externa krav och lagar samt interna regler och riktlinjer. Arbetet bedrivs med fokus på att använda resurserna effektivt utifrån verksamhetens behov och tillgängliga medel. Kansliet är placerat på Clinical Research Center (CRC) i Malmö och består idag av 11 personer, vilka jobbar inom ekonomi, HR, administration och kommunikation och leds av en administrativ chef. Inom vårt kansli värnar vi om en god arbetsmiljö med respekt och omtanke i våra relationer med varandra och vi arbetar ständigt för att skapa ännu bättre förutsättningar för arbetsglädje, utveckling och delaktighet för alla medarbetare. Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet är en statlig myndighet vilket innebär att du får särskilda förmåner, generös semester och en förmånlig tjänstepension. Vi har även ett flextidsavtal som skapar goda förutsättningar för balans mellan arbete och fritid. Läs mer på universitetets webbplats om att vara anställd vid Lunds universitet Jobba hos oss Arbetsuppgifter och ansvarsområden Som ekonomiadministratör kommer du ha en stor bredd av olika arbetsuppgifter och rollen är omväxlande och självständig. Vi söker dig som uppskattar att arbeta med ekonomiadministration i såväl stort som smått. I rollen som ekonomiadministratör kommer du bland annat vara granskare av reseräkningar samt även upprätta reseräkningar, hantera vårt anläggningsregister inkluderande administration vid årlig inventering, hantera diarieföring, hantera fakturering och rekvirering, ekonomiska avstämningar, arvodering, hantera stipendier samt andra ekonomiadministrativa arbetsuppgifter. Du kommer vara stöd till chefer, forskare och andra medarbetare i ekonomiadministrativa frågor. Dina arbetsuppgifter kan även komma att innefatta andra administrativa arbetsuppgifter som kan förekomma på vårt kansli. I takt med verksamhetens förändrade behov kan tjänstens innehåll utvecklas och förändras över tid. Kvalifikationer För anställningen krävs: Lägst gymnasiekompetens. Flerårig erfarenhet av ekonomiadministrativt arbete såsom bokföring, hantera reskontra, hantera avstämningar. Erfarenhet av att arbeta i olika ekonomisystem. Mycket god förmåga att arbeta självständigt. Mycket god kommunikativ förmåga. God förmåga att uttrycka dig på svenska och engelska i både tal och skrift. God samarbets-, service- och initiativförmåga, noggrann, flexibel, strukturerad och van att arbeta med flera arbetsuppgifter parallellt. God datorvana och erfarenhet av IT-system och verktyg, inklusive Office 365 och olika administrativa system. Meriterande för anställningen är: Tidigare erfarenhet av ekonomiadministrativa och administrativa system inom universitets- och högskolesektorn eller annan offentlig sektor. Övrigt Anställningen är tillsvidareanställning på 100 %, med tillträde 1 januari 2027. Provanställning i sex månader kan komma att tillämpas. Så här söker du Anställningen söks via universitetets rekryteringssystem. Ansökan ska innehålla personligt brev med motivering till varför du är intresserad av anställningen och på vilket sätt anställningen matchar dina meriter. Ansökan ska även innehålla CV samt övrigt som du önskar åberopa (kopior av betyg, uppgifter till referenser, rekommendationsbrev etc.) Universitetet tillämpar individuell lönesättning. Ange gärna löneanspråk i din ansökan. Medicinska fakulteten är ett verksamhetsområde inom Lunds universitet, med ansvar för utbildning och forskning inom medicin, vård och hälsa. Utbildningen sker i nära samverkan med sjukvården och är väl förankrad i fakultetens starka forskningstradition. Fakultetens forskning spänner över ett brett fält inom experimentell grundforskning, patientnära klinisk forskning och hälsovetenskaplig forskning. Medicinska fakulteten, med drygt 1800 anställda och 3000 studenter i Lund, Malmö och Helsingborg, är en kunskapsintensiv mötesplats för studenter, lärare och forskare från hela världen. Institutionen för kliniska vetenskaper i Malmö är en av de sex institutionerna vid Lunds universitets medicinska fakultet. Vi har ett starkt fokus på klinisk och epidemiologisk forskning, och bedriver även en omfattande preklinisk laboratorieforskning. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter från annonsförsäljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsföretag på grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anställningsform Tillsvidare med provanställning Anställningens omfattning Heltid Tillträde 1 januari 2027 Löneform Månadslön Antal lediga befattningar 1 Sysselsättningsgrad 100 Ort Malmö Län Skåne län Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2793 Kontakt Katarina Westrin Sjöberg, Rekryterande chef, +4640391050, katarina.westrin_sjoberg@med.lu.se Sarah Quist, HR-partner, +4640391055, sarah.quist@med.lu.se Facklig företrädare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-01 Sista ansökningsdag 2026-10-16 Logga in och sök jobbet Dela länkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillgänglighetsredogörelse × Modal title Vi använder cookies för inloggning, förbättrad användarupplevelse, dela-länkar samt i vissa fall marknadsföring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast nödvändiga Läs mer om våra cookies här ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:974401/": {
      "title": "Universitetsadjunkt i offentlig rätt",
      "description": "Universitetsadjunkt i offentlig rätt Logga in och sök jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Universitetsadjunkt i offentlig rätt Logga in och sök jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas återkommande som ett av världens främsta lärosäten. Här finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malmö. Vi förenas i vår strävan att förstå, förklara och förbättra vår värld och människors villkor. Lunds universitet välkomnar sökande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. Jämställdhet, lika villkor och mångfald är grundläggande principer för alla delar av vår verksamhet. Lunds universitet är ett fullskaligt och forskningsintensivt universitet, och ingår som enda svenska universitet i de starka internationella nätverken League of European Research Universities (LERU) och Universitas 21 (U21). Lunds universitet har partneruniversitet i närmare 70 länder, och attraherar flest internationella studenter av alla svenska universitet. Juridiska fakulteten kännetecknas av internationalisering, sammanflätning av utbildning och forskning, tvärvetenskap samt nära och gränsöverskridande samverkan med det omgivande samhället. Fakultetens forskningsmiljö och utbildning på forskarnivå präglas av internationalisering, och vid sidan av juristprogrammet erbjuds också flera internationella mastersprogram. Lunds universitet och den Juridiska fakulteten erbjuder en utvecklande och inkluderande arbetsmiljö i den bredare dynamiska vetenskaps- och innovationsregion som Öresundsregionen utgör. Ämne Offentlig rätt Ämnesbeskrivning Offentlig rätt omfattar den del av juridiken som rör maktutövningen i riksdag, regering, kommuner och annan offentlig förvaltning. Till den offentliga rätten räknas framför allt ämnena statsrätt (konstitutionell rätt), allmän förvaltningsrätt inklusive förvaltningsprocessrätt, kommunalrätt samt områden inom speciell förvaltningsrätt. Arbetsuppgifter Arbetsuppgifterna innebär att genom undervisning vidareutveckla en stimulerande utbildningsmiljö. I arbetsuppgifterna ingår undervisning inom ramen för juristprogrammets grundnivå och avancerade nivå. Det kan också ingå undervisning inom ramen för fakultetens distans- och uppdragsutbildningar. Undervisningen omfattar främst föreläsningar, seminarier, uppsatshandledning, kursutveckling och administration samt att utarbeta och spela in videoföreläsningar. Även annan undervisning kan ingå. Därutöver innefattar arbetsuppgifterna att aktivt verka för en pedagogisk utveckling av utbildningen på grund- och avancerad nivå. Undervisningen sker i huvudsak på svenska men engelska kan även förekomma. De ämnesområden som främst aktualiseras är allmän förvaltningsrätt, inklusive förvaltningsprocessrätt, kommunalrätt, statsrätt och miljörätt inklusive speciell fastighetsrätt. Som universitetsadjunkt förväntas du undervisa brett inom i första hand juristprogrammet samt annan utbildningsverksamhet vid fakulteten. Arbetsuppgifterna utförs i nära samarbete med studenter, doktorander, lärare och forskare såväl vid Lunds universitet som vid andra lärosäten samt med andra externa aktörer. Behörighet Behörig att anställas som universitetsadjunkt är den som dels har visat pedagogisk skicklighet, dels har avlagt juristexamen eller på annat inhämtat motsvarande kunskaper samt har annan kompetens som är av betydelse med hänsyn till anställningens ämnesinriktning och de arbetsuppgifter som ingår i anställningen. För universitetsadjunkt gäller som allmänt behörighetskrav att vara lämplig för och ha den förmåga i övrigt som behövs för att väl fullgöra arbetsuppgifterna i den aktuella anställningen. Enligt Lunds universitets anställningsordning måste den sökande även ha genomgått högskolepedagogisk utbildning om minst fem veckor eller på annat sätt ha inhämtat motsvarande kunskaper för att vara behörig. Om det finns särskilda skäl kan den som inte har högskolepedagogisk utbildning om minst fem veckor ändå anses vara behörig. Bedömningsgrunder Som bedömningsgrunder vid anställning av en universitetsadjunkt ska graden av sådan skicklighet som är ett krav för behörighet för anställning gälla. Vid anställning som universitetsadjunkt ska följande utgöra grund för bedömning: Goda och breda ämneskunskaper av relevans för anställningens innehåll och de arbetsuppgifter som ingår God pedagogisk förmåga, vilket innebär god förmåga att bedriva och utveckla undervisning och annan pedagogisk verksamhet på olika nivåer och med varierande undervisningsmetoder Mycket god yrkeserfarenhet eller annan erfarenhet av relevans för anställningen Synnerligen god förmåga att undervisa på svenska eller annat skandinaviskt språk på juristprogrammet är ett krav liksom förmåga att undervisa på engelska Särskild vikt kommer att fästas vid: Stor bredd inom de ämnesområden som förekommer inom juristprogrammet Goda ämneskunskaper i processrätt, miljörätt och fastighetsrätt Omfattande och kvalificerad yrkeserfarenhet som jurist Dokumenterad och aktuell erfarenhet av att undervisa i juridik på grund- och avancerad nivå Vikt kommer att fästas vid: Administrativ och annan skicklighet samt personliga förmågor som är av betydelse för att fullgöra arbetsuppgifterna väl. Nödvändiga personliga förmågor är exempelvis god samarbetsförmåga, självständighet samt att vara initiativtagande och drivande Förmåga att samverka med det omgivande samhället Anvisningar för ansökan Ansökan till anställningen söks elektroniskt via Lunds universitets sökandeportal. Ansökan ska innehålla följande: Personligt brev Kortfattad curriculum vitae (CV) Fullständig publikationslista upp till fem vetenskapliga publikationer kan biläggas ansökan Beskrivning av pedagogiska meriter med bilagor (såsom sammanfattning av den pedagogiska verksamheten, kort pedagogisk självreflektion, pedagogisk meritförteckning) Beskrivning av meriter rörande ledarskap och administration med bilagor (såsom sammanfattning, kort självreflektion och meritförteckning av administrativa erfarenheter och ledningsuppdrag) Beskrivning av meriter rörande samverkan med bilagor (såsom sammanfattning, kort självreflektion och meritförteckning av insatser och åtaganden rörande samverkan) Övriga handlingar som sökanden önskar åberopa Vänligen notera att de handlingar som inkommer eller upprättas med anledning av denna ledigförklarade anställning (såsom ansökningar, sakkunnigutlåtanden och protokoll) som huvudregel är allmänna och därmed offentliga. Detta innebär att handlingarna får (med undantag för sekretessbelagda handlingar) läsas av den som så begär det. Villkor Universitetet tillämpar individuell lönesättning. Ange gärna löneanspråk i din ansökan. Juridiska fakulteten är en av Lunds universitets fyra ursprungliga fakulteter. Vid fakulteten verkar ca 2000 studenter på grundnivå och avancerad nivå och ett 160-tal anställda varav ett 40-tal är doktorander. Mer information om fakulteten finns på vår hemsida www.jur.lu.se Vi undanber oss alla kontakter från annonsförsäljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsföretag på grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anställningsform Tillsvidareanställning Anställningens omfattning Heltid Tillträde 2027-01-01 eller enligt överenskommelse Löneform Månadslön Antal lediga befattningar 1 Sysselsättningsgrad 100 Ort Lund Län Skåne län Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2837 Kontakt Jenny Lindskog, HR-chef, +46462221004, jenny.lindskog@jur.lu.se Ellika Sevelin, Prefekt, 0462221099, ellika.sevelin@jur.lu.se Facklig företrädare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-01 Sista ansökningsdag 2026-11-12 Logga in och sök jobbet Dela länkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillgänglighetsredogörelse × Modal title Vi använder cookies för inloggning, förbättrad användarupplevelse, dela-länkar samt i vissa fall marknadsföring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast nödvändiga Läs mer om våra cookies här ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:968024/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral position in Electrical Engineering focusing on Nanoelectronics and Cryogenic and Ferroelectric materials",
      "description": "Postdoctoral position in Electrical Engineering focusing on Nanoelectronics and Cryogenic and Ferroelectric materials Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral position in Electrical Engineering focusing on Nanoelectronics and Cryogenic and Ferroelectric materials Login and apply Lund University, LTH, Electrical and Information Technology Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The Department of Electrical and Information Technology (EIT) at Lund University, The Faculty of Engineering (LTH), is one of the larger departments with about 120 employees and conducts research and teaching mainly in electrical engineering and computer technology. We are located on LTH's campus in northern Lund. Within the Division of Electromagnetics and Nanoelectronics we develop and study new generations of electronics based on advanced semiconductor technology. In particular, we develop and characterize new generations of electronic and optoelectronic devices based on III-V technology. Part of the effort is related to exploratory material investigations for cryogenic applications. Subject description Ferroelectric materials like HZO show promising properties at cryogenic temperatures with strong polarization and attractive switching characteristics. The interface properties play a critical role but the reduced thermal activation allows different optimization criteria. We will introduce new ALD materials and evaluate their use at the ferroelectric interfaces. The research will be performed in collaboration with researchers within the competence centre ACT and within the strategic research areas in Advanced materials. Work duties The main duties involved in a postdoctoral position is to conduct research. Teaching may also be included, but up to no more than 20% of working hours. The position includes the opportunity for three weeks of training in higher education teaching and learning. The purpose of the position is to develop the independence as a researcher and to create the opportunity of further development. You will be responsible for the investigations of novel interface structures for cryogenic ferroelectric operation. The studies will also include structural characterization at the synchrotron beam lines. Some of the work may be carried out at Brunnshög, close to the large infrastructures MAX IV and ESS. Detailed description of the work duties: Design of experiment and sample preparation. ALD deposition of ferroelectric films. Measurements, data analysis and interpretation. Structural interface characterization. Research within the subject area. Teaching in the first, second and third cycles of studies. Supervision of degree projects and doctoral students. Actively seeking external research funding. Collaboration with industry and wider society. Administration related to the work duties listed above. Qualification requirements Appointment to a postdoctoral position requires that the applicant has a PhD, or an international degree deemed equivalent to a PhD, within the subject of the position. The certificate proving the qualification requirement is met, must be received before the employment decision is made. Priority will be given to candidates who have graduated no more than three years ago before the last day for application. Under special circumstances, the doctoral degree can have been completed earlier. Additional requirements: Documented experience in material deposition techniques. Experience in clean-room processing. Documented experience in structural film characterization, preferable using synchrotron based techniques. Very good oral and written proficiency in English. Good ability to work with others. Good ability to work independently. Assessment criteria This is a career development position primarily focused on research. The position is intended as an initial step in a career, and the assessment of the applicants will primarily be based on their research qualifications and potential as researchers. Particular emphasis will be placed on research skills within the subject. For appointments to a postdoctoral position, the following shall form the assessment criteria: A good ability to develop and conduct high quality research. Teaching skills. Other qualifications: Experience in ALD technology. Consideration will also be given to how the applicant’s experience and skills complement and strengthen ongoing research within the department, and how they stand to contribute to its future development. We offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. Read more on the University website about being a Lund University employee . Further information This is a full-time, fixed-term employment of two years, the start date is as soon as possible by agreement, however no later than April 1, 2027. The period of employment is determined in accordance with the agreement “Avtal om tidsbegränsad anställning som postdoktor” (“Agreement on fixed-term employment as a post-doctoral fellow”). How to apply Applications are to be submitted via the University’s recruitment system. The application should include a CV and a personal letter justifying your interest in the position and how it matches your qualifications. The application should also include a degree certificate or equivalent and any other document to which you would like to draw attention (copies of grade transcripts, details of referees, letters of recommendation, etc.)” We welcome your application! About the Faculty of Engineering LTH is Lund University’s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers – many of whom work in world-leading profile areas – publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create – to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment As soon as possible by agreement, however no later than April 1, 2027 Salary Månadslön Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2649 Contact Lars-Erik Wernersson, Professor, +46462229003, lars-erik.wernersson@eit.lth.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 30.Sep.2026 Last application date 21.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:970808/": {
      "title": "Doctoral student in Astronomy and Astrophysics",
      "description": "Doctoral student in Astronomy and Astrophysics Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral student in Astronomy and Astrophysics Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The Planet Formation Group at the Department of Physics (Division of Astrophysics) at Lund University is seeking a PhD student to work on models of planet formation on a galactic scale. Research within the division encompasses galaxy formation, galactic dynamics and evolution, star formation and dynamics, stellar evolution, stellar spectroscopy and astrometry, planet formation and dynamics, as well as exoplanet atmospheres. Being a doctoral student As a doctoral student, you are both admitted as a student and employed at Lund University. As a doctoral student, you will be trained in a scientific approach. In short, you will be trained to think critically and analytically, to solve problems independently using the right methods, and to develop an awareness of research ethics. In addition, you will have the opportunity to work on projects, to develop your leadership and pedagogical skills. Throughout your studies, you will be guided by supervisors. Doctoral studies end with a thesis and a doctoral degree. More about being a doctoral student at the Faculty of Science at naturvetenskap.se . Allmän studieplan för forskarutbildning Work duties We are seeking a PhD student in theoretical astrophysics. The PhD student will study how planets form at different times and in different regions of our galaxy. The PhD student will also calculate how certain planetesimals are ejected from planetary systems to become free-flying interstellar planetesimals. The PhD project will give astronomers new insight into where interstellar comets came from. Your primary responsibility will be to pursue your doctoral studies, which will mainly consist of conducting research and writing a doctoral thesis. In addition, you will be expected to: Conduct research within the subject area. Publish results in high-quality scientific journals. Present research results at national and international conferences. In addition, you are expected to participate in doctoral courses, seminars and conferenes. In addition to studies, a maximum of 20% of working time may be spent on teaching and other departmental work Qualifications To be eligible for admission and employment as a doctoral student, you must fulfil the requirements below. Admission requirements A person meets the general admission requirements for third-cycle courses and study programmes if the applicant: has been awarded a second-cycle qualification, or has satisfied the requirements for courses comprising at least 240 credits of which at least 60 credits were awarded in the second cycle, or has acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. Specific admission requirements To be admitted to the third-cycle programme in Astronomy and Astrophysics the student must have earned credits in first and second-cycle programmes in which physics, mathematics and/or corresponding engineering subjects have been substantial elements. In addition to 60 credits in basic physics, there is a requirement for at least 60 credits in subjects of relevance to Astronomy and Astrophysics, e.g., courses in astronomy or other physics subjects, or engineering subjects such as space technology and automatic control. The 120 credits must include at least 60 second-cycle credits. Equivalent knowledge acquired through corresponding programmes will be assessed individually. In order to enable interdisciplinary initiatives and important specialisations in certain areas, students with qualifications in subjects other than Astronomy and Astrophysics may be considered for admission. Finally, the student must be judged to have the potential to complete the programme. Additional requirements In order to complete the doctoral programme in question, the following are also required: Strong ability to work independently and to formulate and tackle scientific problems. Good written and oral communication skills. Strong collaborative and teamwork skills. Very good proficiency in English, both spoken and written. Merits Experience in analyzing and working with models of planet formation or galaxy formation Excellent numerical and analytical problem-solving skills, as well as experience with programming languages (e.g. Python and Fortran). Extensive knowledge of galaxy formation and galaxy formation. Selection criteria The selection of eligible applicants will be made taking into account the ability to benefit from the training based on the following criteria: Relevant qualifications and expertise (see the requirements and merit criteria listed above). Demonstrated ability to handle complex research problems and to work both collaboratively and independently, as well as to complete tasks on schedule. Consideration will also be given to strong collaborative skills, motivation, and independence, as well as to how the applicant’s experience and qualifications demonstrate the abilities required to successfully complete doctoral studies. We offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. More about working at Lund University on lu.se. About the employment The employment is a fixed-term employment at full time, starting as agreed. Third cycle studies consist of full-time studies for 4 years. In the case of teaching and other departmental duties, the employment is extended accordingly. Doctoral studentships are regulated in the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), chapter 5, 1-7 §§. More about terms of employment for doctoral students on Lund University’s Staffpages . Other Any other information such as where and when interviews will be held. How to apply The application should be written in English and you must attach to your application: CV and personal letter with a justification of why you are interested in the training place/employment and in what way the research project matches your interests and your educational background. Copies of issued study certificates and/or diplomas. These should prove your basic and special eligibility for the doctoral education subject and show that you have the subject knowledge required for the doctoral education project. Other information that you wish to refer to (copies of grades, information for references, letters of recommendation, etc.). We welcome your application. Within the Faculty of Science research and education is conducted within Astronomy, Biology, Physics, Geosciences, Chemistry, Mathematics, medical radiation physics, physical geography and Environmental Sciences. The Faculty of Science is organized into eight departments, gathered in the northern campus area in Lund. The Faculty of Science has approximately 1900 students, 330 PhD students and 730 employees. The Department of Physics is one of Lund University's largest departments with approximately 400 employees. The department is shared between the Faculty of Science and Faculty of Engineering. At the department there are seven research divisions and a number of major research centra. The research at the department covers a wide range of modern physics. www.fysik.lu.se/en/ We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position First day of employment After agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2727 Contact Anders Johansen, Professor, anders.johansen@fysik.lu.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 29.Sep.2026 Last application date 01.Dec.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:971322/": {
      "title": "Bibliotekarie till Universitetsbiblioteket",
      "description": "Bibliotekarie till Universitetsbiblioteket - Statlig visstidsanställning Logga in och sök jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Bibliotekarie till Universitetsbiblioteket - Statlig visstidsanställning Logga in och sök jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas återkommande som ett av världens främsta lärosäten. Här finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malmö. Vi förenas i vår strävan att förstå, förklara och förbättra vår värld och människors villkor. Lunds universitet välkomnar sökande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. Jämställdhet, lika villkor och mångfald är grundläggande principer för alla delar av vår verksamhet. Kravprofil Avdelning Samlingar ansvarar för universitetsbibliotekets fysiska samlingar, inklusive tillgängliggörande för användarna. Avdelningen hanterar donationsförfrågningar och inköp, samt stöder fakulteternas depåläggning av material. Arbetet utförs både på Universitetsbiblioteket och på våra depåer. På avdelningen arbetar cirka 20 personer, uppdelade i olika team. Team Vardagstryck, där denna tjänst är placerad, hanterar de lagstadgade pliktleveranserna av vardagstryck, som utgör en stor del av våra samlingar. Vardagstryck är material från företag, institutioner, organisationer och föreningar som till exempel reklam, broschyrer, medlemsinformation, personaltidskrifter, årsredovisningar och affischer. Teamet ansvarar för att ordna och tillgängliggöra detta material för användarna. Hos oss arbetar vi för en god arbetsmiljö. Här kan du läsa mer om Universitetsbiblioteket. Arbetsuppgifter och ansvarsområden Universitetsbiblioteket har beviljats medel till ett 2-årigt projekt för att arbeta med ouppordnat material (restantier). Vi söker nu en bibliotekarie för att arbeta med att ordna vardagstryck. Arbetet passar dig som gillar struktur, och vill bidra till att tillgängliggöra detta spännande material. Det kan bli aktuellt med schemalagda pass i någon av våra informationsdiskar, där du möter användarna. Arbetsveckan är fördelad mellan Universitetsbiblioteket Helgonabacken, och UB:s depå för vardagstryck. Periodvis kan arbetet vara fysiskt krävande, med hantering av tungt material. Du arbetar i ett team av kollegor med liknande arbetsuppgifter. Krav för anställningen Examen i biblioteks- och informationsvetenskap eller likvärdig annan utbildning som av arbetsgivaren bedöms som relevant Goda kunskaper om det svenska samhället och det svenska medielandskapet Mycket goda kunskaper i svenska (tal och skrift) Goda kunskaper i engelska (tal och skrift) Meriterande för anställningen B-körkort för manuell växel (för vissa transporter kan det bli aktuellt att köra någon av universitetsbibliotekets bilar) Erfarenhet av arbete i forskningsbibliotek Personliga egenskaper Vi söker dig som: Har ett noggrant och systematiskt arbetssätt Snabbt kan sätta dig in i nya områden och komplexa uppgifter Har god samarbetsförmåga och Kan arbeta självständigt/har ett gott självledarskap. Stor vikt kommer att läggas vid personlig lämplighet. Övrigt Anställningen är en visstidsanställning på 100 procent under 2 år, med tillträde snarast. Lunds universitet är en statlig myndighet vilket innebär att du får särskilda förmåner, generös semester och en förmånlig tjänstepension. Läs mer om att arbeta hos oss på universitetets webbplats. Så här söker du: Anställningen söks via universitetets rekryteringssystem. I ansökan skriver du inget personligt brev. I stället ansöker du genom att bifoga ett CV som beskriver dina meriter för tjänsten, samt genom att besvara ett antal urvalsfrågor kopplade till anställningen. Universitetsbiblioteket vid Lunds universitet är ett tvärvetenskapligt bibliotek med bas i omfattande samlingar av såväl tryckt som elektroniskt material. Biblioteket erbjuder också en studiemiljö med cirka 400 läsplatser. Universitetsbiblioteket har cirka 100 anställda. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter från annonsförsäljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsföretag på grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anställningsform Tidsbegränsad anställning Anställningens omfattning Heltid Tillträde Snarast Löneform Månadslön Antal lediga befattningar 1 Sysselsättningsgrad 100 Ort Lund Län Skåne län Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2747 Kontakt Miriam Björkhem, Avdelningschef, 046-2229810, miriam.bjorkhem@ub.lu.se Facklig företrädare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-09-29 Sista ansökningsdag 2026-10-19 Logga in och sök jobbet Dela länkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillgänglighetsredogörelse × Modal title Vi använder cookies för inloggning, förbättrad användarupplevelse, dela-länkar samt i vissa fall marknadsföring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast nödvändiga Läs mer om våra cookies här ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:972485/": {
      "title": "Ekonom vid Institutionen för energivetenskaper",
      "description": "Ekonom vid Institutionen för energivetenskaper Logga in och sök jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Ekonom vid Institutionen för energivetenskaper Logga in och sök jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas återkommande som ett av världens främsta lärosäten. Här finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malmö. Vi förenas i vår strävan att förstå, förklara och förbättra vår värld och människors villkor. Lunds universitet välkomnar sökande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. Jämställdhet, lika villkor och mångfald är grundläggande principer för alla delar av vår verksamhet. Beskrivning av arbetsplatsen Tjänsten som ekonom är placerad vid Institutionen för energivetenskaper, LTH, Lunds universitet. Vårt uppdrag är att forska och utbilda om hur energisystemen kan utvecklas för en hållbar framtid. Institutionen har en omfattande experimentell verksamhet bland annat bestående av ett av Europas största drivlinelaboratorier med 13 testceller med motorer, bränsleceller och hybrida system, en unik högtrycksrigg för gasturbintestning, samt jetmotorriggar. Institutionen har även omfattande verksamhet med avancerad modellutveckling och simuleringar av olika energisystem och energirelaterade processer. Utbildningsverksamheten är omfattande och vi ser det som ett hedersuppdrag att vara en del av unga människors utveckling till välutbildade och attraktiva medarbetare inom näringsliv och samhälle. Som ekonom ingår du i institutionens administrativa grupp, som svarar för administrativt verksamhetsnära stöd till den undervisande och forskande personalen på institutionen. Tillsammans med den tekniska personalen omfattar det teknisk-/administrativa stödet sju personer, och gruppens arbete och attityd genomsyras av ett genuint servicetänk. En positiv och tillmötesgående stomme, som driver och utvecklar processer för att ge bra, kontinuerlig och effektiv service till ledningen, institutionen och dess medarbetare. Verksamheten i sin helhet är välmående och vi har tillsammans en oerhört spännande framtid inom energiområdet som är så viktig för samhällets utveckling. Vill du vara en del av en verksamhet som bidrar till samhällsutvecklingen och en hållbar framtid? Arbetsuppgifter Vi söker en ekonom som tar ett helhetsansvar för institutionens ekonomiska struktur och rutiner samt deltar i verksamhetsplaneringen. I detta ingår ekonomisk planering och budgetarbete för institutionen som helhet, såväl som enskilda mindre och större forskningsprojekt. Du sköter löpande bokföring och gör ekonomisk uppföljning av helhet och delar, bland annat genom färdigställande och analys av bokslut. Projektstöd till forskarna i alla faser såsom; ansökning, rapportering, uppföljning, samt håller dig informerad om olika bidragsgivares och andra för yrkesrollen relevanta regelverk. Du analyserar verksamheten och dess förutsättningar och gör prognoser på både kort och lång sikt. I anställningen ingår även att ansvara för anläggningsregister och inventering, samt fakturering och kontraktshantering. Vi har internationella medarbetare och kontakter, så engelska används dagligen. Kvalifikationer För tjänsten krävs: ekonomisk utbildning på högskolenivå, gärna civilekonom. god ekonomisk kompetens och erfarenhet gällande ekonomisk planering, bokföring, redovisning och uppföljning/analys. vana vid redovisningssystem och förmåga att ta till sig nya tekniska system. goda kunskaper i Excel på avancerad nivå och i Word. god pedagogisk och kommunikativ förmåga när du förklarar ekonomi för icke-ekonomer. mycket god kunskap i svenska och god engelska, i tal och skrift. Meriterande för tjänsten är: bred erfarenhet från kvalificerat ekonomiarbete. erfarenheter av prognosskapande. kunskap om statliga regelverk inom det ekonomiska området. erfarenhet från ekonomihantering inom offentlig verksamhet eller stora organisationer. kunskap om EU-projekt. Vi lägger stor vikt vid personlig lämplighet. Vi söker en ekonom som är analytisk, pedagogisk, noggrann, strukturerad, serviceinriktad, och som är bra på att samarbeta och ta initiativ, samt har förmåga att se helheter och sammanhang. Vi kommer även att ta hänsyn till hur den sökande genom sin erfarenhet och kompetens bedöms komplettera och stärka institutionen samt bidra till dess framtida utveckling. Villkor Tillsvidareanställning med omfattning 100%. Provanställning kan bli aktuell. Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet är en statlig myndighet vilket innebär att du får särskilda förmåner, generös semester och en förmånlig tjänstepension. Vi har även ett flextidsavtal som skapar goda förutsättningar för balans mellan arbete och fritid. Läs mer på universitetets webbplats om att Jobba hos oss. Så här söker du Ansökan ska innehålla ett personligt brev med motivering till varför du är intresserad av anställningen och på vilket sätt anställningen matchar dina meriter. Ansökan ska även innehålla CV, examensbevis eller motsvarande samt övrigt som du önskar åberopa (kopior av betyg, uppgifter till referenser, rekommendationsbrev etc). Du kommer att få besvara urvalsfrågor i systemet. Om Lunds Tekniska Högskola LTH – Lunds Tekniska Högskola – är en del av Lunds universitet. På LTH utbildar vi människor, bygger kunskap för framtiden och arbetar hårt för att utveckla samhället. Vi skapar utrymme för briljant forskning och inspirerar till kreativ utveckling av teknik, arkitektur och design. Här läser närmare 12 000 studenter. Varje år publicerar våra forskare – varav många verkar inom världsledande profilområden – omkring 100 avhandlingar och 2 000 vetenskapliga rön. En rad forskningsresultat och studentarbeten förädlas till innovationer. Tillsammans utforskar och skapar vi – till nytta för världen. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter från annonsförsäljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsföretag på grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anställningsform Tillsvidareanställning Anställningens omfattning Heltid Tillträde Snarast enligt ök Löneform Månadslön Antal lediga befattningar 1 Sysselsättningsgrad 100 Ort Lund Län Skåne län Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2775 Kontakt Martin Tunér, +46462224050, martin.tuner@energy.lth.se Publicerat 2026-09-29 Sista ansökningsdag 2026-10-22 Logga in och sök jobbet Dela länkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillgänglighetsredogörelse × Modal title Vi använder cookies för inloggning, förbättrad användarupplevelse, dela-länkar samt i vissa fall marknadsföring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast nödvändiga Läs mer om våra cookies här ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:973268/": {
      "title": "Universitetslektor",
      "description": "Universitetslektor Logga in och sök jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Universitetslektor Logga in och sök jobbet Lunds universitet, Samhällsvetenskapliga fakulteten Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas återkommande som ett av världens främsta lärosäten. Här finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malmö. Vi förenas i vår strävan att förstå, förklara och förbättra vår värld och människors villkor. Lunds universitet välkomnar sökande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. Jämställdhet, lika villkor och mångfald är grundläggande principer för alla delar av vår verksamhet. Institutionen för kulturgeografi och ekonomisk geografi är i behov av en tidsbegränsad universitetslektor med en omfattning om 100% under perioden 1 januari 2027 till och med 26 december 2027. Arbetsuppgifter Arbetsuppgifterna omfattar undervisning och handledning i humanekologi. Undervisning och handledning inom kulturgeografi och ekonomisk geografi kan också förekomma. Administrativa uppgifter kan också utgöra en del av arbetsuppgifterna. Undervisning och handledning på både engelska och svenska förekommer. Kvalifikationer För anställningen krävs avlagd doktorsexamen i humanekologi. Anställningen kräver även att den sökande har undervisningserfarenhet inom ämnet humanekologi framför allt från svenskt universitet eller högskola samt dokumenterad förmåga att undervisa på engelska och svenska. En av de viktigaste bedömningsgrunderna utgörs av förmågan att snabbt sätta sig in i och utföra undervisningsuppdraget. Ansökan Ansökan ska innehålla: - CV - Personligt brev - Förteckning över pedagogiska meriter Samhällsvetenskapliga fakulteten vid Lunds universitet är ett av landets ledande kunskapscentra för forskning och utbildning inom samhälls- och beteendevetenskap. Med verksamhet i både Lund och Helsingborg, över 700 anställda och cirka 5 700 helårsstudenter är fakulteten en av Lunds universitets största. Vi erbjuder en kreativ akademisk miljö med engagerade studenter och medarbetare. Vår huvuduppgift är att utveckla, förmedla och förvalta kunskap om samhälle, människa och organisationer i en miljö som präglas av öppenhet, tolerans och nyfikenhet. Institutionen för kulturgeografi och ekonomisk geografi vid Lunds universitet är en forskningsintensiv akademisk enhet inom Samhällsvetenskapliga fakulteten. Den kombinerar långa akademiska traditioner med modern och starkt internationaliserad forskning och utbildning. Institutionen erbjuder ett brett utbud av utbildning på grund-, master- och doktorsnivå, inklusive internationellt inriktade program såsom mastersprogrammet i Human Geography. Institutionen har en mångsidig akademisk personal. Den exakta personalstyrkan varierar, men institutionen har för närvarande 55–60 akademiska och administrativa medarbetare. Institutionen utbildar cirka 400 heltidsstuderande på kandidat- och mastersprogram och har cirka 15 doktorander. Forskningsmiljön är starkt inriktad på extern finansiering och har varit framgångsrik i konkurrensen på nationell och europeisk nivå. Institutionens forsknings- och utbildningsverksamhet har fått mycket positiva omdömen i interna och externa utvärderingar, vilket placerar den bland Lunds universitets ledande disciplinära miljöer. Lunds universitet som helhet presterar framgångsrikt i globala rankningar. Enligt den senaste QS World University Rankings ligger Lunds universitet på plats 72 globalt och uppnår starka positioner på ämnesnivå, bland annat inom områden som rör kulturgeografi och miljövetenskap. Lunds universitet rankas också som nummer 1 i världen inom hållbarhet i samma ranking, vilket återspeglar dess styrkor inom socialt och miljömässigt relevant forskning och utbildning. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter från annonsförsäljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsföretag på grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anställningsform Tidsbegränsad anställning Anställningen avslutas 2027-12-26 Anställningens omfattning Heltid Tillträde Januari 2027 Löneform Månadslön Antal lediga befattningar 1 Sysselsättningsgrad 100% Ort Lund Län Skåne län Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2799 Kontakt Ola Hall, Prefekt, ola.hall@keg.lu.se Natalie Nyman, HR-partner, natalie.nyman@sam.lu.se Facklig företrädare OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 0462229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 0462229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 0462220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-09-29 Sista ansökningsdag 2026-10-20 Logga in och sök jobbet Dela länkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillgänglighetsredogörelse × Modal title Vi använder cookies för inloggning, förbättrad användarupplevelse, dela-länkar samt i vissa fall marknadsföring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast nödvändiga Läs mer om våra cookies här ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:963476/": {
      "title": "Doctoral student in Biomedical Engineering specializing in engineering acoustics",
      "description": "Doctoral student in Biomedical Engineering specializing in engineering acoustics Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral student in Biomedical Engineering specializing in engineering acoustics Login and apply Lund University, Faculty of Engineering, LTH, Dep. of Biomedical Engineering Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The position is based at the Department of Biomedical Engineering and is linked to researchers working in marine biology, medical ultrasound, biomechanics, physics, e-science, and the strategic research area eSSENCE in Lund. The research group you will join conducts research in areas including engineering acoustics, medical ultrasound, acoustic measurement technology, non-destructive testing based on acoustic methods, signal processing, and numerical modelling, with applications in, among other fields, biomedical engineering, civil engineering, and biological systems. The working environment is highly interdisciplinary and is characterized by close collaboration between doctoral students, researchers, and academic staff, often with very different technical and scientific backgrounds and areas of expertise. The group strives to provide an open and inclusive working environment with good access to supervision, knowledge exchange, and broad scientific and interdisciplinary collaborations. More about the strategic research area eSSENCE - on Lund University's website Being a doctoral student As a doctoral student, you are both admitted as a student and employed at Lund University. As a doctoral student, you will be trained in a scientific approach. In short, you will be trained to think critically and analytically, to solve problems independently using the right methods, and to develop an awareness of research ethics. In addition, you will have the opportunity to work on projects, to develop your leadership and pedagogical skills. Throughout your studies, you will be guided by supervisors. Doctoral studies end with a thesis and a doctoral degree. We are looking for a candidate who is curious, focused, and highly motivated by scientific questions. You have a creative and open-minded approach and enjoy combining methods and perspectives from different fields, such as physics, acoustics, computational modelling, and biology. You are driven by a desire to understand complex phenomena and to contribute new knowledge that is relevant to technology and society, as well as to our understanding of biological systems. More about being a doctoral student at LTH - lth.se Work duties You will primarily devote your time to your doctoral studies, which include participation in research projects as well as doctoral-level courses, seminars, and conferences. You will be part of an interdisciplinary research project investigating the physical mechanisms underlying dolphin echolocation. The overall aim of the project is to develop and apply computational models in acoustics and structural mechanics to describe how the short, broadband ultrasonic pulses generated in the dolphin’s head propagate through tissues and other anatomical structures and are thereby shaped into a forward-directed echolocation beam. Particular emphasis will be placed on how variations in acoustic material properties, geometry, and potential reflective or refractive structures influence the direction, frequency-dependent shape, and temporal structure of the beam. The work is interdisciplinary and lies at the interface of engineering acoustics, computational physics, biomedical engineering, and zoology/bioacoustics. The project also includes developing the technical aspects of the results into practically useful concepts for human-made technologies, for example medical applications in diagnostic ultrasound, underwater acoustic sonar systems, or non-destructive testing of civil engineering structures. The work duties include: research on the acoustic properties of relevant tissues and anatomical structures, for example by measuring sound speeds, densities, and attenuation properties, as well as assisting with anatomical CT imaging of the physiology of stranded harbour porpoises and related specimens development of computer-based three-dimensional finite element models (FEM) of acoustic wave propagation in the sound-generating organs of dolphins and surrounding tissues, with the aim of creating a physically accurate so-called digital twin collection and analysis of acoustic, mechanical, and anatomical data from toothed whales development and use of computational and analysis code, with or without machine-learning components, in MATLAB and COMSOL or equivalent environments for model setup, post-processing, signal analysis, visualisation, and comparison between simulations and measurement data collaboration with researchers in, among other fields, physics, marine mammal research, and computational sciences, acting as an interdisciplinary knowledge bridge between different scientific disciplines communication of research results at scientific conferences and through the publication of scientific articles. The duties may also include participation in teaching and other departmental work, up to a maximum of 20% of working hours. Qualifications To be eligible for admission and employment as a doctoral student, you must fulfil the requirements below. Admission requirements A person meets the general admission requirements for third-cycle courses and study programmes if the applicant: has been awarded a second-cycle qualification, or has satisfied the requirements for courses comprising at least 240 credits of which at least 60 credits were awarded in the second cycle, or has acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. A person meets the specific admission requirements for third cycle studies in Biomedical Engineering if the applicant has: at least 45 credits at second-cycle level relevant to the subject area Additional requirements In order to complete the doctoral programme in question, the following are also required: Knowledge and skills relevant to the doctoral project and the subject area (e.g. engineering or theoretical physics, wave propagation, engineering acoustics, programming, modelling, bioacoustics, computational methods, electronics, applied mathematics, zoology, materials physics, etc.). Very good analytical skills, including problem-solving and data analysis. Goal-oriented approach, which may be demonstrated through perseverance and the ability to work methodically, in a structured manner, and with focus. Good ability to work independently and to formulate and tackle research problems. Good collaborative skills (i e manifested as a willingness to share ideas, constructive approach to challenges etc). Very good written and oral communication skills. Very good knowledge of English, spoken and written Other qualifications (advantages) For the doctoral programme in question, the following are considered as other qualifications: Master’s degree in engineering physics or theoretical physics, electrical engineering, mechanical engineering, mathematics, computer engineering, engineering acoustics, or another subject relevant to the research area Knowledge of numerical computational methods and/or FEM-based modelling of physical problems Experience of finite element modelling in acoustics and multiphysics Knowledge of marine mammals, toothed-whale echolocation or other areas of bioacoustics Practical experience of acoustic or measurement systems Practical experience of measurement technology and electronics Programming experience beyond introductory-level courses Experience of working with computing clusters Experience of classical machine-learning or deep-learning-based signal analysis. We offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. More about working at Lund University on Lund University's website About the employment The employment is a fixed-term employment at full time, starting as soon as possible. Third cycle studies at LTH consist of full-time studies for 4 years. In the case of teaching and other departmental duties, the employment is extended accordingly. Doctoral studentships are regulated in the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), chapter 5, 1-7 §§. More about terms of employment for doctoral students on Lund University’s staff pages. Other Job interviews will be held online and on site at the Faculty of Engineering, Lund University, during the autumn semester of 2026. How to apply Applications shall be written in English and include: CV and a cover letter stating the reasons why you are interested in the doctoral programme/employment and in what way the research project corresponds to your interests and educational background. Copies of issued study certificates and/or awarded degree certificates. These must confirm that you meet the general and specific admission requirements for the doctoral programme and show that you have the subject knowledge required for the doctoral programme project. Other documents you wish to be considered (grade transcripts, contact information for your references, letters of recommendation, etc.) We look forward to receiving your application! LTH is Lund University’s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers – many of whom work in world-leading profile areas – publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create – to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position First day of employment As soon as possible, as agreed. Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2501 Contact Josefin Starkhammar, josefin.starkhammar@bme.lth.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 28.Sep.2026 Last application date 09.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:968843/": {
      "title": "PostDoc in Scientific Imaging Data Reduction and Compression",
      "description": "PostDoc in Scientific Imaging Data Reduction and Compression Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) PostDoc in Scientific Imaging Data Reduction and Compression Login and apply Lund University, MAX IV Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. The Scientific Data Group You will join the Scientific Data Group within the Technical Division of MAX IV Laboratory. We develop and operate high-performance data acquisition systems for cutting-edge detectors and provide data processing, visualisation and analysis solutions that enable researchers to rapidly interpret results from X-ray scattering, imaging and spectroscopy experiments. Our systems routinely handle data rates of several GB/s and support large-scale scientific data workflows. To support sustainable data management at next-generation photon science facilities, we are seeking a Postdoctoral Researcher to advance scientific data reduction and compression workflows for tomography and imaging applications in collaboration with European research infrastructures. The Position The rapid growth of data volumes generated by modern imaging experiments is creating significant challenges for data storage, transfer, processing and long-term preservation. Through a collaborative European initiative involving leading photon science facilities, MAX IV is developing sustainable approaches to scientific data reduction and scientifically validated lossy-compression methods for tomography and imaging applications. As a PostDoc you will contribute to the evaluation, development, validation and deployment of advanced data reduction and compression methodologies for large-scale imaging datasets. Working at the interface between scientific computing, image analysis and research infrastructures, you will collaborate closely with scientists, software engineers, beamline scientists and computing specialists across the European photon science community. The project is carried out in close collaboration with leading European photon science facilities through the LEAPS community. The position offers a unique opportunity to engage directly with MAX IV's full-field X-ray imaging and tomography activities. These span the established tomography capabilities at DanMAX and ForMAX, together with the development of TomoWISE, a dedicated next-generation tomography beamline currently under construction. The successful candidate will work closely with scientists and engineers developing future imaging capabilities at MAX IV while collaborating with experts in tomography, scientific computing, data management and research software engineering across Europe. Your work will contribute to practical solutions that significantly reduce data volumes while preserving scientific quality and reproducibility. The project combines scientific research, software development and international collaboration, offering opportunities to influence community-wide best practices for data handling at large-scale research facilities. Activities include benchmarking and validating compression algorithms, developing software tools and workflows, establishing quality metrics and best practices, collaborating with partner facilities, organising workshops and training activities, and disseminating results through publications and presentations. Your primary responsibilities will include Evaluate and benchmark data reduction and lossy-compression methods using representative tomography and imaging datasets from MAX IV and collaborating facilities. Develop software tools, workflows and validation methodologies that support the adoption of compression technologies in scientific environments. Collaborate with beamline scientists to evaluate the impact of data reduction methods on scientific outcomes and data quality. Contribute to community guidelines, best practices and knowledge resources related to scientific data reduction, compression and FAIR data management. Work with researchers and technical experts at European photon science facilities to facilitate knowledge exchange and technology transfer. Support and coordinate project workshops, training activities and dissemination events. Disseminate project outcomes through reports, technical documentation, presentations, workshops, and scientific publications, as appropriate. To be successful in this role you need to have the following qualifications A PhD in Computer Science, Applied Mathematics, Physics, Engineering, Scientific Computing, Image Processing, Data Science, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated experience in scientific programming, scientific software development, or data-intensive computing. Experience with Python and at least one high-performance programming language such as C++, Rust, or Julia. Experience working with large-scale scientific datasets, image processing, computational imaging, tomography data analysis, or data compression. Experience with Linux-based computing environments and modern software development practices, including version control and collaborative software development. Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English. Ability to work effectively in an interdisciplinary and international research environment The following qualifications are considered an advantage Experience with synchrotron, neutron, electron microscopy, medical imaging, or other large-scale imaging facilities. Experience with scientific data formats and technologies such as HDF5, NeXus and Zarr. Knowledge of FAIR data principles and research data management. Experience with high-performance computing, cloud computing, GPU acceleration, or distributed data processing. Experience participating in international scientific collaborations and/or multi-institutional research projects. Eligibility Appointment to the position of postdoc requires that the applicant has a PhD or an international degree deemed equivalent to a PhD, within the subject of the position, completed no more than three years before the application deadline. Under special circumstances the PhD can have been completed previous to the aforementioned three years. Further information This is a full-time, fixed-term employment for two years. A postdoctoral fellow is employed under a period of at least two years and at most three years. The period of employment is determined in accordance with the agreement “Avtal om tidsbegränsad anställning som postdoktor-2022-02-01” (“Agreement on fixed-term employment as a post-doctoral fellow, 2022-02-01”). What we offer When you join our MAX IV team, you enter a world of cutting-edge science. We make the invisible visible by supporting scientists from all over the world, generating scientific results for the benefit of society. We offer you a multicultural work environment with great opportunities for personal development with respect for a healthy work-life balance. Would you like to work in a challenging and supporting environment? Then join us and take the opportunity to make a real difference! For further information, please visit: https://www.lunduniversity.lu.se/about-lund-university/work-lund-university www.sweden.se https://www.maxiv.lu.se/about-us/careers/compensation-benefits/ MAX IV is a Swedish national large-scale research infrastructure hosted by Lund University. It provides scientists from Sweden and abroad, with intense x-rays and state-of-the-art instrumentation for research in areas such as engineering, physics, structural biology, chemistry and nanotechnology. Its 16 beamlines receive up to 2 000 scientists annually, conducting ground-breaking experiments in materials and life sciences using the brilliant X-rays. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment As per agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 % City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2670 Contact Paul Bell, +46706700506, paul.bell@maxiv.lu.se Union representative OFR/S:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds, 046-2229364, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 28.Sep.2026 Last application date 18.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:968981/": {
      "title": "PhD student position in Surgery",
      "description": "PhD student position in Surgery Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) PhD student position in Surgery Login and apply Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Sciences, Lund Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the Workplace Lund University was founded in 1666 and is consistently ranked among the world's leading universities. The University has approximately 47,000 students and more than 8,800 employees in Lund, Helsingborg, and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain, and improve our world and the conditions of humankind. The Faculty of Medicine is one of Lund University's faculties and is responsible for education and research in medicine, nursing, and health sciences. Education is conducted in close collaboration with the healthcare sector and is firmly rooted in the Faculty's strong research tradition. The Faculty's research spans a broad range of areas, including experimental basic research, patient-oriented clinical research, and health sciences research. With more than 1,800 employees and 3,000 students in Lund, Malmö, and Helsingborg, the Faculty of Medicine is a knowledge-intensive environment where students, teachers, and researchers from all over the world meet and collaborate. The Department of Clinical Sciences Lund (IKVL) is one of six departments within the Faculty of Medicine. The department maintains extensive collaborations both within the Faculty and with other parts of the University. IKVL also has well-established collaborations with Skåne University Hospital (SUS), Region Skåne, and external partners in society and industry. These collaborations aim to promote clinical and experimental translational research, development, and education. The research group is now recruiting a doctoral student (full-time, 100%) with a start date of 1 November 2026, or as otherwise agreed. Description of the Doctoral Project and Research Group The doctoral position is based in the Pancreatology Research Group within the Division of Surgery at Lund University. The group's research focuses on pancreatic cancer, one of the most aggressive forms of human malignancy. Pancreatic cancer is often detected at an advanced stage, and effective treatments remain limited. Our strategy combines clinical patient materials with advanced protein research to identify novel biomarkers for earlier diagnosis and treatment response. The research group consists of two research engineers, several full-time and part-time doctoral students, and clinicians affiliated with the group. We value a positive work environment characterized by respect and consideration in our interactions with one another. We continuously strive to create conditions that promote job satisfaction, professional development, and participation for all employees. Duties and Responsibilities The doctoral student will work within a translational research project on pancreatic cancer, focusing on disease biology and prognosis. The project combines data from cancer registries and clinical materials with histopathological analyses and spatial proteomics. The overall aim is to identify novel prognostic and predictive biomarkers and to improve our understanding of pancreatic cancer progression and treatment response. The duties will include: Managing data from cancer registries and clinical databases and integrating these with histopathological and molecular data. Interpreting histopathological findings and spatial proteomics data in relation to tumour characteristics, metastatic patterns, and clinical outcomes. Conducting statistical analyses of prognostic and predictive factors and investigating associations between tumour biology, biomarkers, metastasis, and survival. Compiling and presenting research findings in scientific manuscripts and at national and international conferences. The successful candidate is expected to demonstrate a strong ability and willingness to collaborate with colleagues within the research group. Additional duties related to the position may be assigned. We Offer Lund University is a public authority, which means that employees are entitled to a range of attractive benefits, generous annual leave, and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. We also offer flexible working hours that support a healthy work-life balance. Read more about working at Lund University on the University's website. Work at Lund University Qualifications Applicants must meet the general entry requirements for third-cycle (doctoral) studies. A person meets the general entry requirements if they have: completed a second-cycle degree; completed course requirements of at least 240 higher education credits, of which at least 60 credits are at second-cycle level; or acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way, either in Sweden or abroad. Required Qualifications Previous research experience in pancreatic cancer research is required. Excellent command of spoken and written English. Ability to conduct and document research in a structured and systematic manner. We are looking for a curious, motivated, and highly engaged candidate with a strong interest in translational cancer research. The position involves close collaboration with colleagues, and therefore strong interpersonal and teamwork skills are essential. Meritorious Qualifications A publication record in peer-reviewed journals within the field of pancreatic cancer is considered an asset. Eligibility Applicants must meet the general entry requirements for third cycle (doctoral) studies. A person meets the general entry requirements if they have: completed a second-cycle degree; completed course requirements of at least 240 higher education credits, of which at least 60 credits are at second-cycle level; or acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way, either in Sweden or abroad. Assessment Criteria Regulations concerning employment as a doctoral student are set out in the Swedish Higher Education Ordinance (SFS 1998:80). Only applicants who are admitted to third-cycle studies may be appointed to a doctoral studentship. In the appointment process, primary consideration will be given to the applicant's ability to successfully complete doctoral studies. In addition to pursuing their own doctoral education, the holder of the position may be required to undertake duties related to education, research, and administrative work in accordance with the provisions of the Ordinance. Terms of Employment This is a fixed-term position of four years in accordance with Chapter 5, Section 7 of the Swedish Higher Education Ordinance. How to Apply Applications must be submitted through Lund University's recruitment system. The application should include: A cover letter describing how you meet the qualification requirements and why you are interested in the position. A curriculum vitae (CV). Degree certificates, academic transcripts, and any other relevant supporting documentation. Any additional documents you wish to submit in support of your application. Contact information for at least two professional references. The Faculty of Medicine is a part of Lund University, and is responsible for education and research within medicine and healthcare. Our academic programs are closely linked with the healthcare system and are firmly anchored in the faculty’s strong research tradition. Our research spans a broad field within experimental preclinical research, near-patient clinical research and health sciences research. The Faculty of Medicine, with its 1,800 employees and 2,700 students in Lund and Malmö, is a knowledge-intensive meeting place for students, teachers and researchers from all over the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Employment expires 2030-10-31 First day of employment 2026-09-01 Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2676 Contact Anneli Karlsson, anneli.karlsson@med.lu.se Bobby Tingstedt, tomas.jansson@med.lu.se Daniel Ansari, daniel.ansari@med.lu.se Union representative OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362 SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, kansli@saco-s.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366 Published 28.Sep.2026 Last application date 19.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:973185/": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral fellow in AI-based design of de novo protein biofilm systems",
      "description": "Post-doctoral fellow in AI-based design of de novo protein biofilm systems Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Post-doctoral fellow in AI-based design of de novo protein biofilm systems Login and apply Lunds universitet Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Subject description AI-based protein design and synthetic biology for developing programmable living materials, with a particular focus on the de novo design of proteins biofilm systems. The research combines computational protein design with synthetic biology to develop new molecular functions and mechanisms for controlling the formation, organization, and functional properties of living materials. The work may include development and application of AI-based protein design methods, experimental characterization of designed proteins, microbial engineering, biofilm design, and high-throughput functional screening. We are committed to translating fundamental discoveries into technologies with real-world impact. The lab first spinout company is already funded and operational, with additional translational opportunities under development. This provides a unique environment for researchers interested in pursuing future careers in either academia targeting hard basic research problems or technology development and entrepreneurship. We value community spirit, dedication, and the pursuit of innovative science with the potential to make a meaningful impact on sustainability and future technologies. For more information: https://saragovi.science/ Work duties The main duties involved in a post-doctoral posistion is to conduct research. Teaching may also be included, but up to no more than 20% of working hours. The position shall include the opportunity for three weeks of training in higher education teaching and learning. Detailed description of the work duties, such as: Research within AI-based protein design, synthetic biology, biofilm engineering, and programmable living materials. Development and implementation of computational pipelines for the de novo design of proteins and protein-based systems. Development and implementation of high-throughput experimental approaches for screening and characterization of designed systems. Engineering of microbial systems with de novo biofilms. Teaching in the first, second and third cycles of studies Supervision of degree projects and doctoral students Actively seeking external research funding Collaboration with researchers from different scientific disciplines and with external partners, including industry. Administration related to the work duties listed above Qualification requirements Appointment to a post-doctoral position requires that the applicant has a PhD, or an international degree deemed equivalent to a PhD, within the subject of the position, completed no more than three years before the date of employment decision. Under special circumstances, the doctoral degree can have been completed earlier. Additional requirements: Very good oral and written proficiency in English. A doctoral degree, or equivalent research experience, in a field relevant to the position, such as protein design, computational biology, structural biology, synthetic biology, biotechnology, bioengineering, microbiology, molecular biology, or a closely related field. Assessment criteria and other qualifications This is a career development position primarily focused on research. The position is intended as an initial step in a career, and the assessment of the applicants will primarily be based on their research qualifications and potential as researchers. Particular emphasis will be placed on research skills within the subject. For appointments to a post-doctoral position, the following shall form the assessment criteria: Documented scientific excellence and the quality of the applicant's previous research, including their individual contribution to published or ongoing work. Demonstrated ability to independently formulate scientific questions, solve research problems, and drive research projects forward. Research experience and demonstrated expertise in at least one of the following areas: computational or de novo protein design; synthetic biology; microbial or yeast engineering; biofilm engineering; or high-throughput functional screening. The relevance of the applicant's previous research experience and technical expertise to the development of programmable microbial and biofilm systems. Ability to work effectively in an interdisciplinary research environment combining computational and experimental approaches. Teaching skills. Additional assessment criteria: Research experience spanning two or more of the scientific areas relevant to the project. Experience with AI-based or computational protein design, including modern methods for protein structure prediction, sequence design, or generative protein design. Experience with experimental production and characterization of designed proteins. Experience with genetic engineering of bacteria or yeast and the development of engineered microbial systems. Experience with the engineering, characterization, or functional screening of biofilms. Experience with high-throughput experimentation, automation, screening, or iterative design–build–test–learn workflows. Experience developing or implementing computational pipelines for biological or protein design. A strong publication record relative to career stage, with particular consideration given to evidence of substantial individual contributions to high-quality research. Demonstrated scientific creativity, initiative, and ability to develop new experimental or computational approaches. Experience of interdisciplinary collaboration and the ability to communicate and collaborate effectively with researchers from different scientific backgrounds and with external partners . Consideration will also be given to good collaborative skills, drive and independence, and how the applicant’s experience and skills complement and strengthen ongoing research within the department, and how they stand to contribute to its future development. Terms of employment This is a full-time, fixed-term employment of a maximum of 2 years. The period of employment is determined in accordance with the agreement “Avtal om tidsbegränsad anställning som postdoktor” (“Agreement on fixed-term employment as a post-doctoral fellow”) between Lund University, SACO-S and OFR/S, dated 1st February 2022. Instructions on how to apply Applications shall be written in English and be compiled into a PDF-file containing: résumé/CV, including a list of publications, a general description of past research and future research interests (no more than three pages), contact information of at least two references, copy of the doctoral degree certificate, and other certificates/grades that you wish to be considered. Within the Faculty of Science research and education is conducted within Astronomy, Biology, Physics, Geosciences, Chemistry, Mathematics, medical radiation physics, physical geography and Environmental Sciences. The Faculty of Science is organized into eight departments, gathered in the northern campus area in Lund. The Faculty of Science has approximately 1900 students, 330 PhD students and 730 employees. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment 2027-01-01 or as agreed Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2792 Contact Amijai Saragovi, +46736419771, amijai.saragovi@chem.lu.se Jessica Edwinsson, jessica.edwinsson@chem.lu.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 28.Sep.2026 Last application date 31.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:970477/": {
      "title": "Doctoral student in traffic safety focusing on data analysis and traffic simulation",
      "description": "Doctoral student in traffic safety focusing on data analysis and traffic simulation Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral student in traffic safety focusing on data analysis and traffic simulation Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace Transport and Roads offer a unique and open environment for advanced research on traffic safety and behaviour. The group counts five senior researchers (postdocs and senior lecturers) and two PhD students. On the availability of the group, there is a traffic simulation lab with an advanced driving simulator . The group has several active projects in the field of traffic safety, European and national. As a doctoral student, you will contribute to research intended to improve the understanding and prevention of road crashes and injuries. You will work closely with senior researchers while developing an independent research profile. The position provides opportunities for interdisciplinary and international collaboration, conference participation and research visits where relevant to the project. Being a doctoral student As a doctoral student, you are both admitted as a student and employed at Lund University. As a doctoral student, you will be trained in a scientific approach. In short, you will be trained to think critically and analytically, to solve problems independently using the right methods, and to develop an awareness of research ethics. In addition, you will have the opportunity to work on projects, to develop your leadership and pedagogical skills. Throughout your studies, you will be guided by supervisors. Doctoral studies end with a thesis and a doctoral degree. More about being a doctoral student at LTH on lth.se . Subject and project description The doctoral project concerns the development and application of quantitative methods for traffic-safety analysis. The research will combine empirical crash and traffic data with statistical modelling, machine learning and traffic or driving simulation to study crash occurrence, injury severity and road-user behaviour. Particular attention may be given to heterogeneous effects across road users and environments, the interpretation and validation of predictive models, and the safety effects of infrastructure or policy interventions. The precise research questions and balance between methods will be developed with the doctoral student in relation to the project's data, facilities and collaborations. The work is expected to produce both scientific contributions and knowledge relevant to traffic-safety practice and policy. Work duties You will primarily devote yourself to doctoral studies through research, third-cycle courses, seminars and conferences. You will plan and carry out studies with increasing independence, in collaboration with the supervisory team and project partners. The work duties include: Review and synthesise research on traffic safety, crash analysis, road-user behaviour and relevant modelling methods. Acquire, document, clean and analyse crash, traffic, infrastructure, behavioural or simulation data in accordance with research-ethics and data-management requirements. Develop, implement, compare and validate quantitative models, which may include statistical, econometric, machine-learning and simulation-based approaches. Interpret results in relation to traffic-safety theory, human behaviour and practical decision-making, including uncertainty, bias and limitations. Prepare scientific articles and a doctoral thesis, and present results at seminars, conferences and meetings with project partners. Contribute to the group's collaborative research environment and, where relevant, undertake research visits or field and laboratory work. The duties may also include teaching and other departmental work, up to a maximum of 20% of working hours. Qualifications To be eligible for admission and employment as a doctoral student, you must fulfil the requirements below. Admission requirements A person meets the general admission requirements for third-cycle courses and study programmes if the applicant: has been awarded a second-cycle qualification, or has satisfied the requirements for courses comprising at least 240 credits of which at least 60 credits were awarded in the second cycle, or has acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. A person meets the specific admission requirements for third cycle studies in Technology and Society if the applicant has: at least 30 credits awarded in the second cycle relevant to the subject area. Additional requirements In order to complete the doctoral programme in question, the following are also required: a master's degree, or equivalent, in transportation engineering, civil engineering, traffic engineering, applied statistics, data science, computer science or another field relevant to the project. documented second-cycle coursework or thesis work involving quantitative analysis of transport, traffic-safety, mobility or comparable complex empirical data. experience of using programming languages or statistical computing environments, such as Python, R, MATLAB or an equivalent tool, for data processing and analysis. good ability to work independently, formulate research questions and select appropriate methods. good written and oral communication skills, including the ability to communicate methods and results clearly. good ability to cooperate in interdisciplinary and international research settings. very good command of English, spoken and written. you are structured, analytical and persistent. Other qualifications For the doctoral programme and project, the following are considered advantageous: knowledge of traffic-safety theory, crash and injury analysis, road-user behaviour, transport planning or road-infrastructure safety. experience of advanced quantitative methods, such as regression or discrete-choice models, latent-class or random-parameter methods, machine learning, explainable AI, causal or intervention evaluation. experience of working with large, multi-source or international transport datasets, including data preprocessing, reproducible analysis and model validation. experience of scientific writing, peer-reviewed publication, conference presentation or experience of teaching. experience of collaboration with researchers and stakeholders across disciplines or countries. We offer Lund University is a public authority, and employees receive benefits including generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. The Transport and Roads division offers access to an active traffic-safety research environment, advanced simulation facilities, research seminars and established Swedish and international collaborations. More about working at Lund University on lu.se . About the employment The employment is a fixed-term employment at full time, starting as soon as possible. Third cycle studies at LTH consist of full-time studies for 4 years. In the case of teaching and other departmental duties, the employment is extended accordingly. Doctoral studentships are regulated in the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), chapter 5, 1-7 §§. More about terms of employment for doctoral students on Lund University’s Staff pages . Other We plan to hold interviews at the end of October. How to apply Applications shall be written in English and include: CV and a cover letter stating the reasons why you are interested in the doctoral programme/employment and in what way the research project corresponds to your interests and educational background. Copies of issued study certificates and/or awarded degree certificates. These must confirm that you meet the general and specific admission requirements for the doctoral programme and show that you have the subject knowledge required for the doctoral programme project. Other documents you wish to be considered (grade transcripts, contact information for your references, letters of recommendation, etc.) We welcome your application. LTH is Lund University’s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers – many of whom work in world-leading profile areas – publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create – to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position First day of employment As soon as possible Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2716 Contact Carmelo D'Agostino, associate professor, carmelo.dagostino@tft.lth.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 25.Sep.2026 Last application date 16.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:972280/": {
      "title": "PhD position in Dermatology",
      "description": "PhD position in Dermatology Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) PhD position in Dermatology Login and apply Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Sciences, Lund Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the Workplace The PhD project will be conducted within the field of peptidomics. The research group is based at the Biomedical Centre (BMC), Division of Dermatology and Venereology, Department of Clinical Sciences Lund, Lund University, and conducts translational research on how innate defense mechanisms regulate infection, inflammation, and tissue repair. A particular focus is placed on proteolytically released endogenous peptides and their role in wound healing, as well as on the development of novel peptide-based therapeutic concepts. The research group is led by Professor Artur Schmidtchen. The group consists of approximately seven members, including senior researchers, PhD students, and research staff, with complementary expertise in clinical and translational dermatology, microbiology, immunology, molecular biology, and biochemistry. Research is carried out in close collaboration with clinical departments, BioMS, and experts in proteomics, peptidomics, and bioinformatics at Lund University. The Department of Clinical Sciences Lund is now announcing a PhD position within the doctoral programme subject area Medical Science – Dermatology within the doctoral project “Peptidomics of Wound Fluid Guides the Discovery of Endogenous Peptides.” The position is based at the Faculty of Medicine, Lund University, and is conducted in an international and interdisciplinary research environment. We Offer Lund University is a public authority, which means that you will benefit from special employment benefits, generous annual leave, and an attractive occupational pension scheme. We also offer flexible working hours that support a healthy work-life balance. Read more about working at Lund University on our website: Work at Lund University. Duties and Responsibilities The PhD student will carry out a defined research project focused on identifying and characterizing bioactive endogenous peptides involved in infection, inflammation, and wound healing. The project forms a central part of the group's ongoing research and will be conducted in collaboration with BioMS and experts in proteomics and peptidomics at Lund University. The duties include: Planning and conducting experiments. Developing and optimizing methods for sample preparation, peptide enrichment, and fractionation. Performing LC-MS/MS analyses using both DDA and DIA methodologies. Conducting bioinformatic and statistical analyses of peptidomic datasets to identify peptide patterns, proteolytic signatures, and candidate peptides with potential roles in infection, inflammation, and wound healing. Characterizing selected peptides in microbiological and cell-based assays, both individually and in combination, with regard to antimicrobial and immunomodulatory effects. Documenting, quality assuring, and compiling research results. Presenting and publishing research findings in scientific forums. Participating in research group seminars, collaborations, and other scientific activities. Completing courses and other components required within the doctoral education programme. Qualifications Requirements The successful applicant must have: A Master of Science in Engineering degree in Biotechnology, with specialization in Pharmaceutical Biotechnology or Molecular Biotechnology. Documented experience in basic biochemistry, including SDS-PAGE, LC-MS/MS mass spectrometry (DDA and DIA), and handling of human samples. Knowledge and experience in peptide biology and peptidomics, including analysis of complex datasets using specialized peptidomics tools. Experience in MS data analysis using software such as FragPipe and DIA-NN, as well as basic programming skills in Python. Practical experience in antibacterial assays based on dilution or diffusion methodologies. Excellent proficiency in both Swedish and English, spoken and written. Good collaborative skills combined with a high degree of accuracy and responsibility. Meritorious Qualifications The following qualifications are considered advantageous: Previous experience working with mass spectrometry-based analyses. Experience from project work in international or multicultural environments. Experience in method development and experimental troubleshooting. Experience in combinatorial analyses of antimicrobial peptides. Eligibility Applicants must meet the general entry requirements for third-cycle studies, meaning they must have: Completed a second-cycle degree, or Completed at least 240 credits (ECTS), including at least 60 credits at the second-cycle level, or Acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in another way. Assessment Criteria Provisions regarding employment as a doctoral student are laid down in the Higher Education Ordinance (SFS 1998:80). Only applicants admitted to third-cycle studies may be appointed to a doctoral studentship. When selecting among qualified applicants, particular emphasis will be placed on: Scientific maturity and analytical ability. Motivation, independence, and ability to collaborate. Capacity to successfully complete doctoral education. How the applicant’s background and experience are assessed to contribute to the execution of the project. Terms of Employment The employment is a fixed-term full-time position as a PhD student for four years (48 months), in accordance with Chapter 5, Section 7 of the Swedish Higher Education Ordinance. The planned starting date is 1 December 2026, or as otherwise agreed. The Department of Clinical Sciences Lund is one of six departments within the Faculty of Medicine. The department maintains extensive collaborations both within the faculty and with other units at Lund University. It also has well-established partnerships with Skåne University Hospital (SUS), Region Skåne, and external stakeholders in society and industry. These collaborations support clinical and experimental translational research, development, and education. The Faculty of Medicine is a part of Lund University, and is responsible for education and research within medicine and healthcare. Our academic programs are closely linked with the healthcare system and are firmly anchored in the faculty’s strong research tradition. Our research spans a broad field within experimental preclinical research, near-patient clinical research and health sciences research. The Faculty of Medicine, with its 1,800 employees and 2,700 students in Lund and Malmö, is a knowledge-intensive meeting place for students, teachers and researchers from all over the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Employment expires 2030-11-30 First day of employment 2026-12-01 Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2766 Contact Artur Schmidtchen, professor, 046-2224522, artur.schmidtchen@med.lu.se Jessica Hörngren, HR partner, 073-6361904, jessica.horngren@med.lu.se Union representative OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362 SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, kansli@saco-s.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366 Published 25.Sep.2026 Last application date 16.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:902067/": {
      "title": "Professor of Medical Virology (with the possibility of a combined position)",
      "description": "Professor of Medical Virology (with the possibility of a combined position) Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Professor of Medical Virology (with the possibility of a combined position) Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Employment A permanent position as a professor of medical virology. This post is based in the Department of Translational Medicine (ITM). It may be possible to combine this position with clinical duties. This will be decided at the time of appointment. Duties The role involves conducting research and providing postgraduate training and teaching on the faculty’s programmes in medical virology. Other duties associated with a professorship include administrative work, as well as internal and external positions of trust at a national and international level. Applicants must be prepared to take on leadership responsibilities for research and teaching within the subject area. The successful candidate will carry out their research at Lund University’s Virus Centre (LUVC) . This newly established research centre facilitates experimental virological research and includes a biosafety level 3 laboratory for the study of risk class 3 airborne viruses. LUVC's primary objective is to foster collaboration between researchers, healthcare providers, industry, and the public to enhance our understanding of viral diseases and contribute to the development of new preventive, therapeutic, and diagnostic tools. A key part of the role will be to conduct and develop research that is competitive both nationally and internationally in the field of experimental medical virology, with a view to broadening and strengthening existing research at LUVC . The successful candidate is expected to take up the position of Research Group Leader at ITM. This role involves delegated responsibility for health and safety, finance, and human resources. In the event of a combined position, the role will involve working as part of the medical staff at the Department of Clinical Microbiology at Region Skåne. Responsibilities will include teaching, development work and virological diagnostics. You may also be required to perform other duties. Eligibility A person who has demonstrated both research and teaching expertise shall be qualified for employment as a professor ( Higher Education Ordinance, Chapter 4 Section 3). Unless there are special reasons to the contrary, the applicant must have completed training in higher education pedagogy equivalent to at least five weeks or acquired equivalent knowledge in some other way. If the holder is deemed to have special reasons for not having completed five weeks' training in higher education pedagogy when they take up the post, they must complete the training within two years (see Lund University Appointment Rules ) . In the event of a combined position, applicants must have language skills in Swedish, or another Nordic language (Danish or Norwegian) deemed to be equivalent to Swedish, at a minimum of level C1 according to the Council of Europe’s proficiency scale. For teachers at Lund University, the general eligibility requirement is that they must be suitable for the role and possess the other abilities required to perform their duties effectively. Assessment criteria The applicant must demonstrate excellent academic and teaching skills relevant to the subject. Particular emphasis will be placed on academic ability in the assessment. The applicant’s scientific expertise is demonstrated through up-to-date, pioneering and independent research in experimental medical virology at a high international level. Furthermore, applicants must demonstrate their ability to initiate and lead national and international research collaborations. They must also demonstrate their potential to contribute to the development of experimental medical virology research. Future plans and vision will be taken into account. Relevant and up-to-date experience of translational and/or clinically oriented research and research collaborations would be advantageous. The applicant must demonstrate a track record of publishing high-quality work in reputable international scientific journals and must have secured significant national and international competitive research grants as the principal investigator. They must also demonstrate the ability to initiate and lead national and international research collaborations. The applicant must demonstrate relevant teaching skills in the context of undergraduate, postgraduate and doctoral-level teaching and supervision. This is demonstrated by the ability to plan, implement and lead training, and to develop training modules that incorporate clinical expertise. In addition, great importance will be attached to demonstrated academic leadership and collaboration skills . The ability and potential to lead and develop the organisation are demonstrated through documented evidence of strong leadership qualities, such as positions of trust, leadership training and assessed leadership ability. This may also be demonstrated through experience gained from previous management roles and other administrative skills, such as leadership within interdisciplinary projects, research environments and consortia. Experience of leadership in an international context is an advantage. Leadership skills are also demonstrated through communication skills, the ability to foster staff’s professional development, and the ability to contribute positively to the working environment. Skills relating to participation in organisational development and collaboration, as well as the ability to interact with the wider community, will also be important. This can be demonstrated through experience of communicating research findings and establishing collaborations with researchers from different disciplines and relevant stakeholders outside academia. The ability to disseminate knowledge and contribute to the implementation of research findings in society or clinical practice will be an asset. In the case of a combined position, clinical experience and expertise in the subject area of the post will be taken into account. For teaching staff at Lund University, the general eligibility requirement is that they are suitable for the role and possess the other abilities necessary to perform their duties effectively. When appointing teaching staff, in addition to the provisions set out in The Higher Education Ordinance , Lund University Appointment Rules and The Faculty of Medicine’s general requirements and assessment criteria for appointment as a professor . Further information For furhter information, please contact Head of Department Jan Astermark, phone: +46 70-551 66 19, jan.astermark@med.lu.se or Dean Maria Björkqvist, phone: +46 72-700 71 63, maria.bjorkqvist@med.lu.se Information regarding the application process can be obtained from the recruitment co-ordinator, Eva Nilsson, phone: + 46 46-222 17 89, eva_a.nilsson@med.lu.se The post will be filled following a recommendation from the Medical Staff Appointments Committee. Application procedure Applications for this post must be submitted online via Lund University’s applicant portal Varbi by 26 November 2026 at the latest The application must be submitted in accordance with The Faculty of Medicine’s guidelines for applicants for teaching posts (see List of qualifications for lecturers ). Please note that the application should be written in English. However, academic transcripts and certificates of employment do not need to be translated. The Faculty of Medicine is a part of Lund University, and is responsible for education and research within medicine and healthcare. Our academic programs are closely linked with the healthcare system and are firmly anchored in the faculty’s strong research tradition. Our research spans a broad field within experimental preclinical research, near-patient clinical research and health sciences research. The Faculty of Medicine, with its 1,800 employees and 2,700 students in Lund and Malmö, is a knowledge-intensive meeting place for students, teachers and researchers from all over the world. The Department of Translational Medicine is one of the six departments at the Faculty of Medicine, Lund University. We conduct basic science in a laboratory setting, point-of-care and clinical research as well as carry out epidemiological studies. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time Salary Månadslön Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent Heltid City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/470 Union representative Published 24.Sep.2026 Last application date 26.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:967692/": {
      "title": "Amanuens till avdelningen för Teknisk vattenresurslära",
      "description": "Amanuens till avdelningen för Teknisk vattenresurslära Logga in och sök jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Amanuens till avdelningen för Teknisk vattenresurslära Logga in och sök jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas återkommande som ett av världens främsta lärosäten. Här finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malmö. Vi förenas i vår strävan att förstå, förklara och förbättra vår värld och människors villkor. Lunds universitet välkomnar sökande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. Jämställdhet, lika villkor och mångfald är grundläggande principer för alla delar av vår verksamhet. Beskrivning av arbetsplatsen Anställningen är placerad vid Lunds universitet, Lunds Tekniska Högskola, Institutionen för bygg- och miljöteknologi, avdelningen för teknisk vattenresurslära. Avdelningen bedriver undervisning och forskning kring vattenresurser, hydrologi och hydraulik. Vid avdelningen arbetar cirka 30 personer uppdelade på kategorierna lärare/forskare, doktorander, teknisk-administrativ personal samt studentmedarbetare. Amanuenser utför arbetsuppgifter inom grundutbildning, forskning samt administration. Arbetsplatsen är belägen i V-huset, på LTHs campus i Lund. Arbetsuppgifter Som amanuens kan dina arbetsuppgifter variera och arbetsuppgifterna ska ge en inblick i den akademiska världen på den fakultet där du bedriver studier. Arbetsuppgifterna innefattar: undervisning i form av övningsledare i kursen Vatten (VVRA05) viss medverkan i pågående forskningsprojekt viss administration Kvalifikationer Behörig att anställas som amanuens är den som är antagen till utbildning på grund- eller avancerad nivå vid fakulteten (eller närliggande ämne för de gemensamma institutionerna). Examen får ej vara uttagen. Krav för anställningen är: Pågående heltidsstudier inom V-utbildningen eller motsvarande utbildning som arbetsgivaren bedömer relevant mycket goda kunskaper i svenska och engelska, i tal och skrift God förmåga att samarbeta Självständighet och initiativförmåga Godkänt på alla kurser på V-utbildningens årskurs 1 och 2 eller motsvarande kurser på utbildning som arbetsgivaren bedömer relevant Kursbetyget 5 på kursen VVRA05 Vatten eller motsvarande betyg på kurs som bedöms som relevant av arbetsgivaren Meriterande för anställningen är: Kunskaper inom vattenresursteknik i form av höga kursbetyg Tidigare undervisningserfarenhet Tålamod och förmåga att utrycka sig tydligt Det är viktigt att du har tålamod och förmåga att uttrycka dig tydligt. Du behöver ha god förmåga att samarbeta, men även kunna arbeta självständigt och förmåga att ta egna initiativ. Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet är en statlig myndighet som erbjuder goda anställningsvillkor. Med en anställning som amanuens får du som student en möjlighet att förena studier med arbete för att komplettera dina teoretiska kunskaper med praktisk arbetslivserfarenhet inom akademin. Läs mer på universitets webbplats om att Jobba hos oss . Övrigt Anställningen är tidsbegränsad under perioden 2027-01-18 till 2027-05-30 och avser en omfattning på 10 % av heltid, vilket i genomsnitt motsvarar 4 h i veckan. En anställning som amanuens får vara högst 50% av full arbetstid och får vara tidsbegränsad till högst ett år, sammanlagt max tre år. Anställningen får inte påverka amanuensens studier negativt. Bestämmelser gällande utbildningsanställning som amanuens finns i Högskoleförordningen (SFS 2017:284), 5 kap 8-12 §§. Anställningen omfattas av Arbetstidsavtal för lärare. Så här söker du Ansökan ska innehålla CV och personligt brev med motivering till varför du är intresserad av anställningen och på vilket sätt anställningen matchar dina meriter. Vi ber dig bifoga utdrag från LADOK som intygar din behörighet. Ansökan bör även innehålla övrigt som du önskar åberopa (kopior av betyg, uppgifter till referenser, rekommendationsbrev etc.). Välkommen med din ansökan! LTH – Lunds Tekniska Högskola – är en del av Lunds universitet. På LTH utbildar vi människor, bygger kunskap för framtiden och arbetar hårt för att utveckla samhället. Vi skapar utrymme för briljant forskning och inspirerar till kreativ utveckling av teknik, arkitektur och design. Här läser närmare 12 000 studenter. Varje år publicerar våra forskare – varav många verkar inom världsledande profilområden – omkring 100 avhandlingar och 2 000 vetenskapliga rön. En rad forskningsresultat och studentarbeten förädlas till innovationer. Tillsammans utforskar och skapar vi – till nytta för världen. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter från annonsförsäljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsföretag på grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anställningsform Tidsbegränsad anställning Anställningens omfattning Deltid Tillträde 270118 eller enligt överenskommelse Löneform Månadslön Antal lediga befattningar 1 Sysselsättningsgrad 10% Ort Lund Län Skåne län Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2631 Kontakt Magnus Persson, +46462228990, magnus.persson@tvrl.lth.se Facklig företrädare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-09-24 Sista ansökningsdag 2026-10-21 Logga in och sök jobbet Dela länkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillgänglighetsredogörelse × Modal title Vi använder cookies för inloggning, förbättrad användarupplevelse, dela-länkar samt i vissa fall marknadsföring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast nödvändiga Läs mer om våra cookies här ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:966737/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Computer Science with Focus on Verification and Validation of Large-Scale Autonomous Systems",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Computer Science with Focus on Verification and Validation of Large-Scale Autonomous Systems Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Assistant Professor in Computer Science with Focus on Verification and Validation of Large-Scale Autonomous Systems Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The assistant professor will be working at the Department of Computer Science, in the Software Engineering (SE) division (until recently known as the SERG research group), headed by division head Emelie Engström. SE comprises around 15 people: two professors, two associate professors/senior lecturers, additional lecturers and adjunct staff (some part-time, with ties to industry), one assistant professor and six doctoral students. The division is based in the E-building on LTH's campus in Lund. As the new assistant professor, you will be the division's second assistant professor, working closely with both senior researchers and the doctoral students, tasked with building up and leading the new research track on verification, validation and quality assurance of autonomous systems. SE's research builds on decades of empirical studies of large-scale software development, requirements, testing and quality assurance at industrial scale, with contributions from, among others, Per Runeson, Björn Regnell, Emelie Engström, Elizabeth Bjarnason and Markus Borg. In recent years, this has, among other things, been directed towards autonomous and safety-critical systems. A current example is VerSACE, a Vinnova FFI project (2025–2028) in which Lund University participates together with, among others, Chalmers, KTH and several leading players in the automotive industry and automotive software, on how frequent software updates in self-driving vehicles can be continuously tested, verified and safety-monitored. Supported by the group's established funding channels through the strategic research area ELLIIT and WASP (Wallenberg AI, Autonomous Systems and Software Program), as well as through the network around the NextG2Com competence centre (theme \"Software Platforms and Continuous Engineering\", led by Emma Söderberg in the SDE division and Emelie Engström), there are good prospects for the position to grow into a more long-term research track, with good opportunities for new collaborations. Read more: NextG2Com: https://www.nextg2com.lu.se/ , WASP: https://wasp-sweden.org/ , Elliit: https://elliit.se/ . Assistant professors in SE receive ongoing support in their development towards promotion to senior lecturer. The group holds regular seminars and meetings where research is presented and discussed in a friendly and generous spirit, and members collaborate extensively, both among themselves and with colleagues in other parts of the department. As an assistant professor, we welcome you taking your own initiative for new collaborations, both within and outside the department, and building up your own research direction within this track over time. Subject Computer Science with Focus on Verification and Validation of Large-Scale Autonomous Systems Subject description The position focuses on methods, tools and studies (empirical as well as analytical and design-oriented) for the verification, validation, quality assurance and certification of large-scale, industrial autonomous systems with AI and ML components, for example autonomous vehicles, robotics in industrial operation, and other deployed cyber-physical systems, as well as autonomous systems with no physical counterpart, for example AI agents and automated decision-support systems, seen from a systems perspective. The subject area includes, among other things: Scenario-based and simulation-based testing of autonomous systems. Statistical and data-driven verification under uncertainty and non-determinism. Model-based systems engineering and architecture for autonomous systems. Safety argumentation and assurance cases. Regulatory compliance and requirements management related to, for example, the EU AI Act and relevant safety standards. What these approaches have in common is that they address the behaviour of the whole system in its operational context, including its interaction with the environment, rather than the formal verification of individual ML models or components. The subject thus complements related, more component-level/mathematically oriented ML verification research at LTH, and builds on SE's expertise in empirical and applied software and systems engineering, as well as the department's established collaborations within, among others, NextG2Com, ELLIIT, WASP and the profile area AI and Digitalisation. Work duties Employment as an assistant professor is a tenure track position, which aims for the holder to develop their independence as a researcher and educator. The work duties mainly involve research and teaching. The position includes the opportunity to undertake five weeks of training in teaching and learning in higher education. Work duties include: Research within the subject area. Teaching in the first, second and third cycles of studies. Supervision of degree projects and doctoral students. Actively seeking external research funding. Collaboration with industry and wider society. Administration related to the work duties listed above. Qualification requirements Qualification requirements for employment as an assistant professor are fulfilled by someone who has been awarded a doctorate or has the corresponding research competence. Primary consideration should be given to someone who has been awarded a doctorate or achieved the equivalent competence within seven years of the deadline for application for employment as an assistant professor. However, someone who has been awarded a doctorate or achieved the equivalent expertise at an earlier date may also be considered if there are special grounds. Special grounds are sick leave, parental leave or other similar circumstances. Assessment criteria For appointment to assistant professor, the following shall form the assessment criteria: A good ability to develop and carry out high quality research. Teaching ability. Additional requirements Very good oral and written proficiency in English. Significant documented research experience (e.g. from postdoc or doctoral studies) from another university/institute or relevant experience from industry/public sector. Documented research competence in verification, validation, quality assurance and/or certification of autonomous and/or AI-based systems, or a related area. Documented proficiency in using empirical, analytical, and/or design science methods, as well as the ability to collaborate and work across methodological and knowledge domains. Documented research that is applied to, or grounded in, real, large-scale industrial systems and problems, rather than purely theoretical research lacking such application or grounding. Ability to contribute to a good, inclusive and respectful research and working environment. Collaborative skills, initiative and the ability to solve work tasks independently, as well as a demonstrated interest in leadership. Other qualifications Ability to collaborate in interdisciplinary and international research environments. Ability to establish and develop collaborations, for example with industry, other universities and institutes. Significant documented research experience (e.g. from postdoc or doctoral studies) from another university/institute or relevant experience from industry/public sector. The extent to which the applicant, through their experience and skills, may complement and strengthen ongoing research, undergraduate education, departmental innovation, and how they can contribute to the future development of the department will also be taken into consideration. Terms of employment This is a full-time, fixed-term employment of 6 years. The employment is regulated in accordance with Chapter 4 Section 12a§ HEA. The purpose of the appointment is for the teacher to be given the opportunity to develop research autonomy and acquire the scholarly and teaching qualifications required for eligibility for appointment as a senior lecturer. We offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. Read more on the University website about being a Lund University employee: https://www.lunduniversity.lu.se/about-university/work-lund-university. Instructions on how to apply Applications shall be written in English. Please draw up the application in accordance with LTH’s Academic qualifications portfolio – see link below. Upload the application as PDF-files in the recruitment system. Read more: h ttp://www.lth.se/english/working-at-lth/to-apply-for-academic-positions-at-lth/ We welcome your application! ***************************************************************** Promotion to Senior Lecturer in Computer Science with Focus on Verification and Validation of Large-Scale Autonomous Systems During the period of employment, an assistant professor can apply for promotion to a permanent position as Senior Lecturer if he or she has the required qualifications listed below, and is deemed suitable. An assistant professor can only apply for promotion once. Qualification requirements Appointment to senior lecturer requires that the applicant has: A PhD or corresponding research competence or professional expertise considered important with regard to the subject matter of the post and the work duties it will involve. Demonstrated teaching expertise. Completed five weeks of training in higher education teaching and learning, or acquired equivalent knowledge by other means. Assessment criteria The assessment criteria specify the aspects to be considered, and the level to be achieved, for the assessment criteria to be deemed fulfilled. The following assessment criteria must be fulfilled for appointment to senior lecturer: A good national and international standing as a researcher. The requirement for international experience shall be assessed with consideration to the character and traditions of the subject. Good teaching ability, including a good ability to conduct, develop and lead teaching and other educational activities on different levels and using a variety of teaching methods. An ability to supervise doctoral students to achieve a PhD. An ability to collaborate with wider society and communicate his or her activities. A general ability to lead and develop activities. Additional requirements Good ability to collaborate, independence and drive. Progression in research and teaching expertise. Demonstrated ability to contribute to the research community, for example as a reviewer or organiser of conferences and workshops, and to the department's shared goals. LTH is Lund University’s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers – many of whom work in world-leading profile areas – publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create – to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time First day of employment As soon as possible Salary Monthly Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 % City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2602 Contact Emelie Engström, emelie.engstrom@cs.lth.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2229364,kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362,st@st.lu.se Published 22.Sep.2026 Last application date 16.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:968016/": {
      "title": "Doctoral student in Electrical Engineering focusing on Cybersecurity",
      "description": "Doctoral student in Electrical Engineering focusing on Cybersecurity Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral student in Electrical Engineering focusing on Cybersecurity Login and apply Lund University, LTH, Electrical and Information Technology Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The Division for Secure and Networked Systems within the Department of Electrical and Information Technology works broadly with research within cryptography, computer security, wireless and fixed networks. The division runs several research projects through different research collaboration platforms and arranges workshops and seminar series, making the research at the division visible to larger audiences. Cross-disciplinary projects are formed through our research collaboration platforms and national and international research networks, contributing to a dynamic research environment. We are now looking for a doctoral student to work within cybersecurity and software engineering in a project funded by the Swedish Foundation for Strategic Research, SSF. Being a doctoral student As a doctoral student, you are both admitted as a student and employed at Lund University. As a doctoral student, you will be trained in a scientific approach. In short, you will be trained to think critically and analytically, to solve problems independently using the right methods, and to develop an awareness of research ethics. In addition, you will have the opportunity to work on projects, to develop your leadership and pedagogical skills. Throughout your studies, you will be guided by supervisors. Doctoral studies end with a thesis and a doctoral degree. More about being a doctoral student at LTH on lth.se . Project description You will work in the RESIST project and primarily contribute to the area of ​​protection of distributed AI. RESIST is in collaboration with Linköping University, Örebro University and the research institute RISE and is a multidisciplinary research center that works with the rapidly growing area of ​​developing conditions and techniques to protect future AI-based systems. The center is led by Linköping University with Lund University as a partner. Work duties You will primarily devote yourself to your doctoral programme, which includes participation in research projects as well as third cycle courses, seminars and conferences. The main duties are to conduct research and teaching at the intersection of cyber-security and software engineering. The research focuses on automated principles for analysing program code. This includes how AI models can be used to analyze and correct software to ensure that it does not contain vulnerabilities. For example, it has been shown that AI-generated code often has significant security flaws. In order to use AI-generated code in high-security applications, the code generation process therefore needs to be made much more robust. The duties include evaluating existing techniques from a security perspective and identifying principles for automatic analysis and code correction. Case studies and experimental research are expected to be central research methods in the doctoral project. The duties also include participation in teaching and other departmental work (however, a maximum of 20% of working hours). Qualifications To be eligible for admission and employment as a doctoral student, you must fulfil the requirements below. Admission requirements A person meets the general admission requirements for third-cycle courses and study programmes if the applicant: has been awarded a second-cycle qualification, or has satisfied the requirements for courses comprising at least 240 credits of which at least 60 credits were awarded in the second cycle, or has acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way. A person meets the specific admission requirements for third cycle studies in Electrical Engineering if the applicant has: at least 60 second-cycle credits in subjects of relevance to Electrical Engineering, or an MSc in Engineering in Biomedical Engineering, Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Engineering Mathematics, Nanoengineering, Engineering Physics, or Information and Communication Engineering. Additional requirements In order to complete the doctoral programme in question, the following are also required: Very good software development skills. Experience of working with complex computer and communication systems. Good ability to work independently and to formulate and tackle research problems. Good written and oral communication skills. Good ability to cooperate. Very good knowledge of English, spoken and written. Other qualifications For the doctoral programme in question, the following are considered as other qualifications: Completed courses and/or master thesis work within Computer Security. Documented software engineering skills. Documented software development skills. Documented artificial intelligence technology skills. Documented teaching and communication skills. Industrial experience. We offer Lund University is a public authority, which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave, and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. Read more on the University website about being a Lund University employee Work at Lund University . About the employment The employment is a fixed-term employment at full time, starting as soon as possible by agreement, however no later than May 1, 2027. Third cycle studies at LTH consist of full-time studies for 4 years. In the case of teaching and other departmental duties, the employment is extended accordingly. Doctoral studentships are regulated in the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), chapter 5, 1-7 §§. More about terms of employment for doctoral students on Lund University’s Staffpages . How to apply Applications shall be written in English and include: CV and a cover letter stating the reasons why you are interested in the doctoral programme/employment and in what way the research project corresponds to your interests and educational background. Copies of issued study certificates and/or awarded degree certificates. These must confirm that you meet the general and specific admission requirements for the doctoral programme and show that you have the subject knowledge required for the doctoral programme project. Other documents you wish to be considered (grade transcripts, contact information for your references, letters of recommendation, etc.) We welcome your application. About the Faculty of Engineering LTH is Lund University’s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers – many of whom work in world-leading profile areas – publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create – to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment As soon as possible by agreement, however no later than May 1, 2027 Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2645 Contact Christian Gehrmann, Professor, +46462220000, christian.gehrmann@eit.lth.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 17.Sep.2026 Last application date 23.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:968020/": {
      "title": "Doctoral student in Electrical Engineering focusing on Applied Cryptography and Privacy",
      "description": "Doctoral student in Electrical Engineering focusing on Applied Cryptography and Privacy Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral student in Electrical Engineering focusing on Applied Cryptography and Privacy Login and apply Lund University, LTH, Electrical and Information Technology Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The Secure and Networked Systems Division within the Department of Electrical and Information Technology works broadly with research within Cryptography, Computer Security, Wireless and Fixed Networks. The security group within the Division has around 20 members. The main research directions are Cryptography, Privacy and System Security for Connected Systems. The division runs several research projects through different large research collaboration platforms and arranges extensive workshops and seminar series, making the research at the division visible to larger audiences. Cross-disciplinary projects are formed through our research collaboration platforms and national and international research networks, contributing to a dynamic research environment. Being a doctoral student As a doctoral student, you are both admitted as a student and employed at Lund University. As a doctoral student, you will be trained in a scientific approach. In short, you will be trained to think critically and analytically, to solve problems independently using the right methods and to develop an awareness of research ethics. In addition, you will have the opportunity to work on projects, to develop your leadership and pedagogical skills. Throughout your studies, you will be guided by supervisors. Doctoral studies end with a thesis and a doctoral degree. More about being a doctoral student at LTH on lth.se . Subject and project description Through the Wallenberg AI, Autonomous Systems and Software Program (WASP) we now offer a new doctoral student position in the field of Applied Cryptography and Privacy. WASP is Sweden’s largest individual research program ever, a major national initiative for strategically motivated basic research, education and faculty recruitment. The program addresses research on artificial intelligence and autonomous systems acting in collaboration with humans, adapting to their environment through sensors, information and knowledge, and forming intelligent systems-of-systems. More about WASP (wasp-sweden.org). The primary duties of the doctoral student positions are to perform research and teaching within the Applied Cryptography and Privacy area. The research is devoted to the broader area of privacy-preserving communication and computation outsourcing. Communication over the internet is susceptible to surveillance and censorship. Privacy preserving communication techniques (e.g., Tor, Nym, Snowflake) allow users to circumvent such surveillance and censorship. The research scope would include designing, analysing and implementing such systems; additionally, studying different attacks and countermeasures are expected to be part of the research method. Privacy-preserving computation outsourcing allows users to outsource computation tasks to a cloud server without revealing to the server anything about the user data or even what kind of computations the user is performing. There are different techniques for such privacy-preserving computation outsourcing such as Trusted Execution Environment (e.g., Intel SGX) and Fully Homomorphic Encryption (TFHE, BGV). Furthermore, the specific functions/tasks can be subject to attacks, and identifying attacks and countermeasures is expected to be studied. The research method will be a combination of system studies, design, and experimental research. Work duties You will primarily devote yourself to your doctoral programme, which includes participation in research projects as well as third cycle courses, seminars and conferences. The work duties include: Research in applied cryptography and privacy. Contributing to research projects. Taking doctoral students courses. The duties also include participation in teaching and other departmental work (however, a maximum of 20% of working hours). Qualifications To be eligible for admission and employment as a doctoral student, you must fulfil the requirements below. Admission requirements A person meets the general admission requirements for third-cycle courses and study programmes if the applicant: has been awarded a second-cycle qualification, or has satisfied the requirements for courses comprising at least 240 credits of which at least 60 credits were awarded in the second cycle, or has acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. A person meets the specific admission requirements for third cycle studies in Electrical Engineering if the applicant has: at least 60 second-cycle credits in subjects of relevance to Electrical Engineering, or a MSc in Engineering in Biomedical Engineering, Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Engineering Mathematics, Nanoengineering, Engineering Physics, or Information and Communication Engineering. Additional requirements In order to complete the doctoral programme in question, the following are also required: Good programming skills. Good ability to work independently and to formulate and tackle research problems. Good written and oral communication skills. Good ability to cooperate. Very good knowledge of English, spoken and written. Other qualifications For the doctoral programme in question, the following are considered as other qualifications: Completed courses and/or master thesis work within Computer Security and/or Cryptology. Industrial experience. Documented software development skills. Documented teaching and communication skills. We offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. More about working at Lund University on lu.se . About the employment The employment is a fixed-term employment at full time, starting as soon as possible by agreement, however no later than May 1, 2027. Third cycle studies at LTH consist of full-time studies for 4 years. In the case of teaching and other departmental duties, the employment is extended accordingly. Doctoral studentships are regulated in the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), chapter 5, 1-7 §§. More about terms of employment for doctoral students on Lund University’s Staffpages . How to apply Applications shall be written in English and include: CV and a cover letter stating the reasons why you are interested in the doctoral programme/ employment and in what way the research project corresponds to your interests and educational background. Copies of issued study certificates and/or awarded degree certificates. These must confirm that you meet the general and specific admission requirements for the doctoral programme and show that you have the subject knowledge required for the doctoral programme project. Other documents you wish to be considered (grade transcripts, contact information for your references, letters of recommendation, etc.) We welcome your application. About the Faculty of Engineering LTH is Lund University’s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers – many of whom work in world-leading profile areas – publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create – to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment As soon as possible by agreement, however no later than May 1, 2027 Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2647 Contact Debajyoti Das, Associate senior lecturer, +46462220000, debajyoti.das@eit.lth.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 17.Sep.2026 Last application date 23.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:966816/": {
      "title": "Universitetslektor i processrätt",
      "description": "Universitetslektor i processrätt Logga in och sök jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Universitetslektor i processrätt Logga in och sök jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas återkommande som ett av världens främsta lärosäten. Här finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malmö. Vi förenas i vår strävan att förstå, förklara och förbättra vår värld och människors villkor. Lunds universitet välkomnar sökande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. Jämställdhet, lika villkor och mångfald är grundläggande principer för alla delar av vår verksamhet. Lunds universitet är ett fullskaligt och forskningsintensivt universitet, och ingår som enda svenska universitet i de starka internationella nätverken League of European Research Universities (LERU) och Universitas 21 (U21). Lunds universitet har partneruniversitet i närmare 70 länder, och attraherar flest internationella studenter av alla svenska universitet. Juridiska fakulteten kännetecknas av internationalisering, sammanflätning av utbildning och forskning, tvärvetenskap samt nära och gränsöverskridande samverkan med det omgivande samhället. Fakultetens forskningsmiljö och utbildning på forskarnivå präglas av internationalisering, och vid sidan av juristprogrammet erbjuds också flera internationella mastersprogram. Lunds universitet och den Juridiska fakulteten erbjuder en utvecklande och inkluderande arbetsmiljö i den bredare dynamiska vetenskaps- och innovationsregion som Öresundsregionen utgör. Ämne Processrätt med särskild inriktning mot civilprocess Ämnesbeskrivning Ämnet processrätt omfattar främst förfaranden i tvistemål, brottmål och förvaltningsmål vid allmänna domstolar, allmänna förvaltningsdomstolar och specialdomstolar samt förfarandet vid exekutiv myndighet. Ämnet omfattar också medling, förlikningsförhandlingar, skiljeförfaranden och andra alternativa privaträttsliga rättsskipningsförfaranden. Ämnet processrätt begränsar sig i stort till att avse i Sverige gällande rätt, vare sig denna har ett nationellt, nordiskt, europeiskt eller ett vidare internationellt ursprung. Arbetsuppgifter Arbetsuppgifterna omfattar ett särskilt ansvar för undervisning och examination i främst svensk processrätt inom ramen för juristprogrammet med särskild betoning på civilprocessrätt. I arbetsuppgifterna ingår att undervisa på juristprogrammets grund- och fördjupningskursnivå, att handleda och examinera examensarbeten, samt att handleda doktorander. Därutöver ingår handledning och examination av uppsatser inom kursen Rättsvetenskaplig uppsats på juristprogrammets sjätte termin. Även annan undervisning kan ingå. Därutöver innefattar arbetsuppgifterna att aktivt verka för en pedagogisk utveckling av utbildningen på alla nivåer. Undervisningen sker i första hand på svenska men även undervisning på engelska kan förekomma. I arbetsuppgifterna ingår vidare att genom undervisning, handledning och samarbete med lärare, forskare, doktorander och studenter samt samverkan med det omgivande samhället vidmakthålla och vidareutveckla en stimulerande forsknings- och utbildningsmiljö. Till dessa arbetsuppgifter hör särskilt att aktivt bedriva forskning och medverka till en utveckling av forskningsmiljön i processrätt. Fakultetens forskare och lärare förväntas bidra till en levande forskningsmiljö och fakultetens övriga verksamhet och i huvudsak bedriva arbetet på arbetsplatsen. Behörighet Behörig att anställas som universitetslektor är den som dels har visat pedagogisk skicklighet, dels har avlagt juris doktorsexamen eller utländsk examen som bedöms motsvara en juris doktorsexamen eller har uppnått motsvarande vetenskaplig kompetens eller någon annan yrkesskicklighet som är av betydelse med hänsyn till anställningens ämnesinnehåll och de arbetsuppgifter som ska ingå i anställningen. För universitetslektor gäller som allmänt behörighetskrav att vara lämplig för och ha den förmåga i övrigt som behövs för att väl fullgöra arbetsuppgifterna i den aktuella anställningen. Enligt Lunds universitets anställningsordning måste den sökande även ha genomgått högskolepedagogisk utbildning om minst fem veckor eller på annat sätt ha inhämtat motsvarande kunskaper för att vara behörig. Om det finns särskilda skäl kan den som inte har högskolepedagogisk utbildning om minst fem veckor ändå anses vara behörig. Bedömningsgrunder Som bedömningsgrunder vid anställning av en universitetslektor ska graden av sådan skicklighet som är ett krav för behörighet för anställning gälla. Prövningen av den pedagogiska skickligheten ska ägnas lika stor omsorg som prövningen av andra behörighetsgrundande förhållanden. Vid anställning som universitetslektor ska följande utgöra grund för bedömning: God nationell och internationell nivå som forskare, där kravet på internationell meritering ska bedömas med hänsyn till ämnets karaktär och tradition God pedagogisk förmåga, vilket innebär god förmåga att bedriva, utveckla och leda undervisning och annan pedagogisk verksamhet på olika nivåer och med varierande undervisningsmetoder Förmåga att delta i handledning av doktorander i studier till doktorsexamen Förmåga att samverka med det omgivande samhället och att informera om sin verksamhet Förmåga i övrigt att leda och utveckla verksamhet Förmåga att undervisa på svenska eller annat skandinaviskt språk på juristprogrammet är ett krav liksom förmåga att undervisa på engelska Dokumenterad erfarenhet av undervisning inom svensk civilprocessrätt Särskild vikt kommer att fästas vid: Goda ämneskunskaper i svensk civilprocessrätt Erfarenhet av kursansvar på grund- och/eller avancerad nivå Kreativitet och visad innovativ förmåga avseende utveckling av kurser, lärandemoment och läromedel Vikt kommer också att fästas vid i processrätt: Bred ämnesmässig kompetens Dokumenterad förmåga att formulera forskningsansökningar om externa medel Dokumenterade internationella forsknings- och undervisningserfarenheter, exempelvis i form av publikationer, forsknings- och undervisningsvistelser i utlandet, forskningssamarbeten och konferenspresentationer Anvisningar för ansökan Ansökan till anställningen söks elektroniskt via Lunds universitets sökandeportal. Kompletteringar i form av inbundna publikationer/motsvarande, skickas i tre exemplar till: Juridiska fakulteten vid Lunds universitet, att: Helena Josefsson, Box 207, 221 00 Lund. Ansökan ska utformas i enlighet med följande mall (för akademisk meritportfölj, innehållande beskrivningar av meriter, se länk) och innehålla följande: Personligt brev Kortfattad curriculum vitae (CV) Beskrivning av vetenskapliga meriter med bilagor (såsom sammanfattning av forskningen, forskningsprofil, forskningsverksamhet inkl. nationella och internationella meriter, forskningserfarenheter och meriter) Fullständig publikationslista Förteckning över doktorsavhandlingen och de övriga 5 vetenskapliga arbeten som sökanden önskar åberopa. De åberopade 6 publikationerna ska biläggas ansökan. DOI-kod för varje publikation ska anges om sådan finns. Beskrivning av pedagogiska meriter med bilagor (såsom sammanfattning av den pedagogiska verksamheten, kort pedagogisk självreflektion, pedagogisk meritförteckning) Beskrivning av meriter rörande ledarskap och administration med bilagor (såsom sammanfattning, kort självreflektion och meritförteckning av administrativa erfarenheter och ledningsuppdrag) Beskrivning av meriter rörande samverkan med bilagor (såsom sammanfattning, kort självreflektion och meritförteckning av insatser och åtaganden rörande samverkan) Övriga handlingar som sökanden önskar åberopa Vänligen notera att de handlingar som inkommer eller upprättas med anledning av denna ledigförklarade anställning (såsom ansökningar, sakkunnigutlåtanden och protokoll) som huvudregel är allmänna och därmed offentliga. Detta innebär att handlingarna får (med undantag för sekretessbelagda handlingar) läsas av den som så begär det. Villkor Universitetet tillämpar individuell lönesättning. Ange gärna löneanspråk i din ansökan. Lunds universitet välkomnar sökande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. Vi ser jämställdhet och mångfald som en styrka och tillgång. Välkommen med din ansökan! Juridiska fakulteten är en av Lunds universitets fyra ursprungliga fakulteter. Vid fakulteten verkar ca 2000 studenter på grundnivå och avancerad nivå och ett 160-tal anställda varav ett 40-tal är doktorander. Mer information om fakulteten finns på vår hemsida www.jur.lu.se Vi undanber oss alla kontakter från annonsförsäljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsföretag på grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anställningsform Tillsvidareanställning Anställningens omfattning Heltid Tillträde 2027-06-01 eller enligt överenskommelse Löneform Månadslön Antal lediga befattningar 1 Sysselsättningsgrad 100 Ort Lund Län Skåne län Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2605 Kontakt Ellika Sevelin, Prefekt, 0462221099, ellika.sevelin@jur.lu.se Helena Josefsson, Kanslichef, 046-2221095, helena.josefsson@jur.lu.se Facklig företrädare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-09-15 Sista ansökningsdag 2026-11-15 Logga in och sök jobbet Dela länkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillgänglighetsredogörelse × Modal title Vi använder cookies för inloggning, förbättrad användarupplevelse, dela-länkar samt i vissa fall marknadsföring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast nödvändiga Läs mer om våra cookies här ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:964482/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Polymer Technology with a focus on Polymer Chemistry",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Polymer Technology with a focus on Polymer Chemistry Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Assistant Professor in Polymer Technology with a focus on Polymer Chemistry Login and apply Lund University, LTH, Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Description of the workplace The Department of Chemistry at Lund University, Faculty of Engineering, invites applications for a position as Assistant Professor in Polymer technology with focus on polymer chemistry. Placed at the Centre for Analysis and Synthesis (CAS) at the Department of Chemistry, the recruited Assistant Professor will be supported by funding of a PhD student. The Department of Chemistry conducts research across all core areas of chemistry with a broad theme of research in support of a sustainable society. Focus areas include the environment, renewable resources, energy and health. Of special relevance are molecular design and synthesis, and understanding of the interplay between structure and properties, chemical and physical processes, and application performance. Advanced characterization of material properties by, e.g., electron microscopy and X-ray characterization (in particular at the synchrotron MAX IV) is also a focal area of the Department. Current research within polymer technology at CAS is mainly directed towards polymers for energy and the environment, including polymeric materials for energy storage and conversion, and sustainable biobased polymers. We synthesize and characterize new monomers, polymer structures, and materials to establish fundamental structure-property relationships relevant for specific application areas. In our work we emphasize a creative environment characterized by scientific excellence, diversity, generosity and freedom. We are now expanding and need to further strengthen our capacity and competence in polymer chemistry. In this context, the successful candidate may develop new synthetic pathways to meet demanding polymer properties for specific application areas. The choice of research approach, application area, etc., will be determined by the research interests of the candidate. Combinations of experimental techniques and theory are most welcome. The position therefore offers an excellent opportunity to develop an independent research programme at the interface of polymer chemistry, material science and sustainability, supported by a strong research environment and dedicated PhD-student funding. Subject Polymer Technology with a focus on Polymer Chemistry . Subject description Deep knowledge in polymer technology and polymer chemistry is crucial for the development, production, application and recyclability of the next generation of efficient and environmentally benign polymeric materials. Polymer technology is an interdisciplinary subject including the chemistry and physics of polymers, polymers from renewable resources, processing and use of polymer materials, and degradation and environmental aspects of polymer materials. Polymer chemistry comprises polymerisations and chemical modifications of polymers, combined with polymer characterisation to determine fundamental structure-property relationships. Work duties Employment as an assistant professor is a tenure track position, which aims for the holder to develop their independence as a researcher and educator. The work duties mainly involve research and teaching. The position includes the opportunity to undertake five weeks of training in teaching and learning in higher education. Work duties include: Research within the subject area. Teaching in the first, second and third cycles of studies. Supervision of degree projects and doctoral students. Actively seeking external research funding. Collaboration with industry and wider society. Administration related to the work duties listed above. Qualification requirements Qualification requirements for employment as an assistant professor are fulfilled by someone who has been awarded a doctorate or has the corresponding research competence. Primary consideration should be given to someone who has been awarded a doctorate or achieved the equivalent competence within seven years of the deadline for application for employment as an assistant professor. However, someone who has been awarded a doctorate or achieved the equivalent expertise at an earlier date may also be considered if there are special grounds. Special grounds are sick leave, parental leave or other similar circumstances. Assessment criteria For appointment to assistant professor, the following shall form the assessment criteria: A good ability to develop and carry out high-quality research. Teaching ability. Additional requirements Very good oral and written proficiency in English. Extensive documented experience within polymer chemistry, including the synthesis and characterization of structure and fundamental properties of polymers. Experience of postdoctoral research in a research environment other than the university at which the applicant obtained their PhD degree A submitted research plan (1500-2000 words) that can form the basis for external funding Collaborative skills, initiative and the ability to solve work tasks independently, as well as a demonstrated interest in leadership. Other qualifications Documented ability to acquire competitive external research funding. As part of the application, the applicant is to submit a research plan (1500-2000 words) clearly describing the research that will be conducted during the employment within the topic of Polymer Chemistry . The plan should also describe how the applicant’s research could complement and reinforce research at the Department of Chemistry. The quality of the research plan shall be given substantial weight in the selection of candidates. Terms of employment This is a full-time, fixed-term employment of 6 years. The employment is regulated in accordance with Chapter 4 Section 12a§ HEA. The purpose of the appointment is for the teacher to be given the opportunity to develop research autonomy and acquire the scholarly and teaching qualifications required for eligibility for appointment as a senior lecturer. We offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. Read more on the University website about being a Lund University employee: https://www.lunduniversity.lu.se/about-university/work-lund-university. Instructions on how to apply Applications shall be written in English. Please draw up the application in accordance with LTH’s Academic qualifications portfolio – see link below. Upload the application as PDF-files in the recruitment system. Read more: http://www.lth.se/english/working-at-lth/to-apply-for-academic-positions-at-lth/ We welcome your application! ***************************************************************** Promotion to Senior Lecturer in Polymer Technology with a focus on Polymer Chemistry During the period of employment, an assistant professor can apply for promotion to a permanent position as Senior Lecturer if he or she has the required qualifications listed below, and is deemed suitable. An assistant professor can only apply for promotion once. Qualification requirements Appointment to senior lecturer requires that the applicant has: A PhD or corresponding research competence or professional expertise considered important with regard to the subject matter of the post and the work duties it will involve. Demonstrated teaching expertise. Completed five weeks of training in higher education teaching and learning, or acquired equivalent knowledge by other means. Assessment criteria The assessment criteria specify the aspects to be considered, and the level to be achieved, for the assessment criteria to be deemed fulfilled. The following assessment criteria must be fulfilled for appointment to senior lecturer: A good national and international standing as a researcher. The requirement for international experience shall be assessed with consideration to the character and traditions of the subject. Good teaching ability, including a good ability to conduct, develop and lead teaching and other educational activities on different levels and using a variety of teaching methods. An ability to supervise doctoral students to achieve a PhD. An ability to collaborate with wider society and communicate his or her activities. A general ability to lead and develop activities. Additional requirements Demonstrated scientific independence, shown among other things by several publications published without their previous supervisors or mentors, where the applicant has clearly had a leading (PI) role. Good ability to collaborate, independence and drive. Sufficient knowledge of Swedish to carry out administrative and educational tasks that require an understanding of Swedish. Progression in research and teaching expertise. Ability to actively, independently, and successfully seek external funding as main applicant. This means that the applicant has received multi-year research grants from large national or international funders such as ERC, Wallenberg Foundations, Swedish Research Council, Formas, Swedish Energy Agency, etc. If the applicant has not received such funding as main applicant, they must be able to show very good evaluations from the application process. LTH is Lund University’s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers – many of whom work in world-leading profile areas – publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create – to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time First day of employment As soon as possible Salary Monthly Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 % City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2526 Contact Ola Wendt, +46462228153, ola.wendt@chem.lu.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2229364, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 09.Sep.2026 Last application date 03.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:930481/": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer in technical GIS",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer in technical GIS Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Senior Lecturer in technical GIS Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Research and education at the Department of Earth and Environmental Sciences (MGeo) addresses fundamental and applied questions on the Earth’s past, present and future climate and environment, including people’s interactions with the natural world and consequences for human wellbeing. MGeo advances and deploys cutting-edge methods, models and technologies in environmental science, quaternary sciences, bedrock geology, paleontology, physical geography, biodiversity and ecosystem science, remote sensing, Geographic Information Science (GIS), and computational science for health and environment, to study processes spanning from the microscopic to the planetary, across all time scales. Lund University welcomes applicants with different backgrounds and experiences. Gender equality, equal opportunities and diversity are fundamental principles in all parts of the University’s activities. Find more reasons why Lund University and the Faculty of Science are right for you here and here , and learn more about what it is like to Working in Lund , Moving to Lund and Living in Lund . Research and education at the Department of Earth and Environmental Sciences (MGeo) address fundamental and applied questions on the Earth’s past, present and future climate and environment, including people’s interactions with the natural world and consequences for human wellbeing. MGeo advances and deploys cutting-edge methods, models and technologies in environmental science, quaternary sciences, bedrock geology, paleontology, physical geography, biodiversity and ecosystem science, remote sensing, Geographic Information Science (GIS), and computational science for health and environment, to study processes spanning from the microscopic to the planetary, across all time scales. Job description The successful candidate is expected to contribute to the department’s core activities in research, teaching and collaboration, as well as, where appropriate, academic leadership roles. The post involves research in geographic information science, with an emphasis on the technical aspects of GIS. The successful candidate is expected to actively seek and secure external research funding, publish in peer-reviewed scientific journals, and contribute to the development of the department’s research environment, including interdisciplinary collaborations. The duties also include teaching at undergraduate and postgraduate levels in geographic information science (GIS), with a particular focus on technically oriented courses such as geographic databases, Web GIS, GIS algorithms and data structures, geospatial artificial intelligence (GeoAI), and the collection and analysis of 3D geodata. The position includes course coordination, course development and participation in pedagogical development within the subject area. Within the framework of outreach, the successful candidate is expected to engage with the wider community, including public authorities, industry and other societal stakeholders, and to contribute to the application of GIS and geospatial technologies in relevant societal areas. The duties may also include participation in departmental and faculty-wide administrative and management-related tasks, such as committee work, programme development and coordination assignments. The allocation of time between research, teaching, outreach and administrative duties follows the faculty’s working hours model, under which teaching normally accounts for approximately 25–35% of a full-time position, with the remaining time divided between research, outreach and other duties. The content, distribution and scope of the duties may change over time in line with the development of the organisation, strategic priorities and external conditions. To support the establishment of a research group, resources equivalent to a PhD student position will be attached to the post. Qualification requirements A person is qualified to be employed as a senior lecturer if they have demonstrated teaching expertise and been awarded a PhD in subject matter of relevance to the position, or equivalent research expertise, in accordance with the Higher Education Ordinance, Chapter 4 Section 4. For this position, applicants must hold a PhD in Geographic Information Systems, Geographic Information Science, Geoinformatics, Engineering Surveying, Computer Science, Information Systems, or a related or equivalent subject area. The position requires at least five weeks’ training in teaching and learning in higher education or corresponding knowledge that has been obtained in some other way. An exception to this requirement may be made in special cases. Applicants who do not possess training in teaching and learning in higher education are to undergo such training within two years of taking up the position. Teaching staff at Lund University are required to be suitable for the position and to have the general ability to fulfil their work duties well. Assessment criteria The requirements for the position are: The applicant must demonstrate a strong academic background in the technical aspects of geographic information science (GIS). Academic competence must be evidenced by publications in reputable, peer-reviewed scientific journals. The applicant must demonstrate a proven ability to successfully secure external research funding in a competitive environment, as well as experience of leading their own research projects. The applicant must demonstrate documented experience of teaching at advanced level in GIS, particularly in areas such as geographic databases, web GIS, GIS algorithms and data structures, geospatial artificial intelligence (GeoAI), and the collection and analysis of 3D geodata. The applicant must have experience of teaching at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels. The applicant must demonstrate experience of supervising undergraduates and PhD students. The applicant must demonstrate a strong ability to engage with the wider community, including experience of applying GIS and geospatial technologies in areas such as the environment and climate, urban planning, health and epidemiology, and disaster management, preferably in collaboration with public sector bodies, industry or other societal stakeholders. The applicant must have a very good command of spoken and written English. The applicant must have experience of research and/or teaching outside Lund University. The applicant must have very good collaborative skills and well-developed communication skills. Merits for the position are: Experience and knowledge of geospatial artificial intelligence (GeoAI) and/or digital twins. Leadership skills, including experience of leading research projects or research teams. Proven experience of interdisciplinary collaboration. Experience of developing innovative teaching methods in GIS. Active participation in international research and education networks. Good command of Swedish, both spoken and written. Experience of distance learning at undergraduate and/or postgraduate level. Personal qualities The applicant should demonstrate creativity, strong drive and the ability to familiarise themselves with new fields of research. The ability to share knowledge and contribute to a collegial and collaborative academic environment is of great importance. The applicant must have the ability to interact effectively with research, teaching and administrative staff, both internally and externally, including stakeholders in academia, industry and the public sector. Further considerations As much attention will be given to the assessment of teaching expertise as to the assessment of research expertise. When appointing teaching staff, Lund University’s Appointment Rules apply, in addition to the provisions set out in the Higher Education Ordinance. For a non-Swedish speaking staff members, language level B2* must be achieved in Swedish within three years. *Common European Framework of Reference for Language, CEFR. What we offer Lund University is a public authority which means that you receive special benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension. Read more on the University website about working with us. Design and content of the application We recommend you write your application in English, as it may be reviewed by international external experts. The application is to be completed according to the Faculty of Science’s application instructions for teaching positions . Upload the application to the recruitment system as PDF files. Please note that it is very important that you follow the application instructions. An application that is incomplete will be rejected. Within the Faculty of Science research and education is conducted within Astronomy, Biology, Physics, Geosciences, Chemistry, Mathematics, medical radiation physics, physical geography and Environmental Sciences. The Faculty of Science is organized into eight departments, gathered in the northern campus area in Lund. The Faculty of Science has approximately 1900 students, 330 PhD students and 730 employees. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time First day of employment As soon as possible Salary Monthly Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/1439 Contact Ali Mansourian Ali Mansourian, Professor, ali.mansourian@mgeo.lu.se Ying Pan, Recruitment Coordinator, +46462228917, ying.pan@science.lu.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 08.Sep.2026 Last application date 04.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:961545/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Student in Automatic Control with focus on Datacenter Control",
      "description": "Doctoral Student in Automatic Control with focus on Datacenter Control Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral Student in Automatic Control with focus on Datacenter Control Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Doctoral student in Automatic Control with focus on Datacenter Control Lund University, The Faculty of Engineering, Department Description of the workplace Automatic Control is an exciting and broad subject, covering both advanced mathematics and hands-on engineering. Historically, it has been instrumental in many areas, from the early development of telecommunications to the space race. Today, driven by the need to engineer ever larger systems, Automatic Control is more relevant than ever. The department of Automatic control has a stimulating and international environment with PhD students, postdocs, and teachers coming from all corners of the world. Research and teaching are conducted in an open and progressive atmosphere with collaborations both within academia and with industry, nationally as well as internationally. A PhD degree from the Department of Automatic control gives you the perfect base for an exciting career, be it in academia or industry. Lund University and the Department of Automatic Control welcome applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences. We regard equality and diversity as a strength and an asset. For more information on being a doctoral student at the department, please have a look at our research videos: Research | Department of Automatic Control (lth.se). Being a doctoral student As a doctoral student, you are both admitted as a student and employed at Lund University. As a doctoral student, you will be trained in a scientific approach. In short, you will be trained to think critically and analytically, to solve problems independently using the right methods, and to develop an awareness of research ethics. In addition, you will have the opportunity to work on projects, to develop your leadership and pedagogical skills. Throughout your studies, you will be guided by supervisors. Doctoral studies end with a thesis and a doctoral degree. More about being a doctoral student at LTH on lth.se. https://www.lth.se/english/study-at-lth/phd-studies/ AEGIS — Adaptive Grid-Interactive Edge Datacenter Fleets is a European Marie Skłodowska-Curie Action (MSCA) research and training network. It is funded by the EU and trains 15 PhD students from 2026 to 2030. The main host for this position is Department of Automatic Control at Lund University. As part of the program you will spend two 3-months visits with partners in the network: École Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne (Switzerland) and Elisa (Finland). Marie Skłodowska-Curie fellowships are among the most respected PhD positions in Europe. The position is only open to applicants that have not lived, studied, or worked in Sweden for more than 12 months in the 36 months before applying. More information about the project is available at the website https://aegis-dn.eu Subject and project description The AEGIS project sits where two fast-growing fields meet: datacentres and AI infrastructure on one side, energy and power systems on the other. Few people today can work across both, so the skills you build here are scarce and in high demand. Specifically there is a gap between a high-level goal like “cut carbon now” and the low-level controls of a site’s cooling, batteries, and compute hardware. In this project you close that gap. You will build a control layer that takes “intents” and translates them into a coordinated set of actions across the site’s physical assets. The models close the loop and tune themselves online using both classical control, AI, and reinforcement learning. In the project you will work on: Designing an intent language that captures carbon, flexibility, and cost. Breaking high-level intents down into control actions. Tuning power-performance and thermal models online. What you will deliver: Control software that turns intents into commands, with measured latency. Practical control systems using real-world data from experiments. A telemetry system that reports headroom and runs without breaking service-level limits in test scenarios. Work duties You will primarily devote yourself to your doctoral programme, which includes participation in research projects as well as third cycle courses, seminars and conferences. The PhD position consists of three main aspects, and the work duties include: research project, including authoring papers and traveling to conferences, seminars etc. postgraduate courses, given locally, nationally and internationally (90 ECTS credits) teaching (no more than 20%), including lab supervision and exam responsibilities. This part may also include departmental services, such as working with equality and diversity, arranging events etc Qualifications To be eligible for admission and employment as a doctoral student, you must fulfil the requirements below. Admission requirements A person meets the general admission requirements for third-cycle courses and study programmes if the applicant: has been awarded a second-cycle qualification, or has satisfied the requirements for courses comprising at least 240 credits of which at least 60 credits were awarded in the second cycle, or has acquired substantial equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. A person meets the specific admission requirements for third cycle studies in Automatic Control if the applicant has: knowledge corresponding to course FRTF05 (previously FRT010) Automatic Control, Basic Course and a second cycle specialisation of relevance to the subject, and an MSc in engineering or corresponding qualification The standard MSCA eligibility criteria also apply: No doctoral degree. At the date of recruitment you must not yet hold a PhD. Mobility rule. You must not have lived or done your main activity (work or studies) in Sweden for more than 12 months in the 36 months just before you are recruited. Short stays such as holidays do not count. Additional requirements In order to complete the doctoral programme in question, the following are also required: Very good oral and written proficiency in English. Good language-analytical ability. Curiosity about research and teaching in general, and motivation for the particular research project. Creativity with good ability for cooperation and networking. Good ability to work independently and to formulate and tackle research problems. Good written and oral communication skills. Strong mathematical knowledge as demonstrated through university transcripts. Other qualifications (advantages) For the doctoral programme in question, the following are considered as other qualifications: Strong foundations in Machine learning and reinformement learning. Cloud computing and cloud technology. Low-level programming and Linux kernel experience. are meriting. Consideration will be given to good collaborative skills, drive and independence, and how the applicant,through experience and skills, is deemed to have the abilities necessary for successfully completing the third cycle programme. We offer Lund University is a public authority which means that employees get particular benefits, generous annual leave and an advantageous occupational pension scheme. More about working at Lund University on lu.se. https://www.lunduniversity.lu.se/about-university/work-lund-university About the employment The employment is a fixed-term employment at full time, starting as soon as possible or March 1, 2027, at the latest. Third cycle studies at LTH consist of full-time studies for 4 years. In the case of teaching and other departmental duties, the employment is extended accordingly. Doctoral studentships are regulated in the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), chapter 5, 1-7 §§. More about terms of employment for doctoral students on Lund University’s Staffpages. https://www.staff.lu.se/research-and-education/research-support/doctoral-education/terms-employment-doctoral-students Other We intend to offer employment to 1 PhD student. A doctoral student will receive a competitive monthly salary of 35 900 SEK with yearly raise. Those applicants who will be called for interview, might be asked to perform a small test to demonstrate basic competence. How to apply Applications shall be written in English and include: CV and a cover letter stating the reasons why you are interested in the doctoral programme/employment and in what way the research project corresponds to your interests and educational background. Copies of issued study certificates and/or awarded degree certificates. These must confirm that you meet the general and specific admission requirements for the doctoral programme and show that you have the subject knowledge required for the doctoral programme project. Other documents you wish to be considered (grade transcripts, contact information for your references, letters of recommendation, etc.) We welcome your application. LTH is Lund University’s Faculty of Engineering. At LTH we educate people, build knowledge for the future and work hard for the development of society. We create space for brilliant research and inspire creative advancements in technology, architecture and design. We have nearly 12,000 students. Every year, our researchers – many of whom work in world-leading profile areas – publish around 100 theses and 2 000 scientific findings. In addition, a number of research results and degree projects are transformed into innovations. Together we explore and create – to benefit the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2448 Contact Johan Eker, +46462228780, johan.eker@control.lth.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 08.Sep.2026 Last application date 23.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:943541/": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer in Experimental Medical Science",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer in Experimental Medical Science Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Senior Lecturer in Experimental Medical Science Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Employment This is permanent employment as a senior lecturer in experimental medical science, with placement at either the Department of Experimental Medical Science (EMV) or the Department of Laboratory Medicine (ILM). The department to which the employment is attached will be decided upon appointment. Duties The main responsibilities will be to lead and develop undergraduate and second cycle education in experimental medicine. The successful candidate will therefore be expected to be prepared to take on key leadership roles at course or program level within the Medical Programme or Biomedicine Programmes. The position also involves teaching and evaluation within the Biomedicine Programmes and/or the first cycle of the Medical Programme (semesters 1-5) using various forms of active learning. As a guideline, teaching, educational management and educational development work is expected to account for approximately 70% of the time over time. Tasks related to third cycle studies may also be included. The teaching role is therefore the main focus of employment. In addition to teaching, the position involves active research in experimental medicine. The position also includes the responsibilities normally associated with the position of Senior Lecturer, such as administrative duties and internal and external elected offices at the national and international levels. Other duties may also be required. Eligibility A person is eligible for employment as a senior lecturer under Chapter 4, Section 4 of the Higher Education Ordinance if he/she has demonstrated teaching ability and has either a doctoral degree or equivalent academic or other professional competence relevant to the subject matter of the employment and the duties to be performed in the position. The applicant must have completed a course in higher education pedagogy lasting at least five weeks. Should the appointee be assessed to have valid reasons for not having completed a five-week course in higher education pedagogy upon taking up the position, they must complete such a course within two years of taking up the position (see Lund University’s Staff Regulations ). Language proficiency equivalent to at least level C2 in Swedish, as per the Council of Europe’s proficiency scale, is a requirement for employment. For teaching staff members at Lund University, the general requirements are that they are suitable for the role and possess the other abilities necessary to carry out their duties effectively. l Assessment criteria The applicant must have demonstrated teaching, academic, and administrative competence relevant to the discipline; particular emphasis will be placed on teaching competence during the review process. The applicant must demonstrate teaching expertise relevant to the subject area, both in teaching and in supervision at undergraduate, postgraduate and doctoral levels. This is demonstrated by a proven ability to deliver teaching and summative assessment through various forms of active learning, in accordance with the Faculty of Medicine’s educational plan. The ability to lead and develop university-level education at first- and second cycle level is advantageous. The candidate’s own development work in higher education pedagogy or research projects is also advantageous. In addition, the applicant must demonstrate research expertise by conducting his/her own current research. Research expertise is demonstrated by publications in international scientific journals, competitive grants, and experience in national and international research collaborations. In addition, research expertise is demonstrated by relevant research programs and the potential for long-term career development. The candidate must demonstrate strong leadership skills and the ability to work collaboratively and externally with the broader community. When employing teaching staff, in addition to the consequences of the Higher Education Ordinance , Lund University’s Staff Regulations and the Faculty of Medicine’s general requirements and assessment criteria for Senior Lecturer shall apply. Further information For further information, please contact Dean Maria Björkqvist, tel. +46 72 700 71 63, maria.bjorkqvist@med.lu.se or Head of Department Karolin Hansén Nord, tel. +46 70 283 1827, karolin.hansen_nord@med.lu.se or Head of Department Tomas Deierborg, tel. +46 70 970 8212, tomas.deierborg@med.lu.se Further information on the application process can be obtained from the recruitment coordinator, Eva A Nilsson, tel. +46 46 222 17 89, eva_a.nilsson@med.lu.se The employment will be filled following a recommendation from the Medical Academic Appointment Board. Application procedure Applications for this employment must be submitted online via Lund University’s application portal by 27 November 2026 at the latest. Applications must be submitted in accordance with the Faculty of Medicine's guidelines for applicants for faculty positions (see \"Summary of Qualifications and CV\"). The university applies a system of individual salary-setting. Please state your salary expectations in your application. Lund University welcomes applicants from a variety of backgrounds and with a range of experiences. We regard gender equality and diversity as a strength and an asset. We look forward to receiving your application! The Faculty of Medicine is a part of Lund University, and is responsible for education and research within medicine and healthcare. Our academic programs are closely linked with the healthcare system and are firmly anchored in the faculty’s strong research tradition. Our research spans a broad field within experimental preclinical research, near-patient clinical research and health sciences research. The Faculty of Medicine, with its 1,800 employees and 2,700 students in Lund and Malmö, is a knowledge-intensive meeting place for students, teachers and researchers from all over the world. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time First day of employment Enligt överenskommelse Salary Månadslön Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/1950 Contact Maria Björkqvist, Dekan, maria.bjorkqvist@med.lu.se Karolin Hansén Nord, Prefekt ILM, karolin.hansen_nord@med.lu.se Tomas Deierborg, Prefekt EMV, tomas.deierborg@med.lu.se Eva Nilsson, Rekryteringskoordinator, eva_a.nilsson@med.lu.se Union representative SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 03.Sep.2026 Last application date 27.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:902060/": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer in Gynaecology combined with a position as Specialist Physician/Consultant",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer in Gynaecology combined with a position as Specialist Physician/Consultant Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Senior Lecturer in Gynaecology combined with a position as Specialist Physician/Consultant Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. Anställning Anställningen är placerad vid Institutionen för kliniska vetenskaper i Malmö. Den kliniska tjänstgöringen sker vid Kvinnokliniken, Skånes universitetssjukhus. Arbetsuppgifter Anställningen utlyses för att säkerställa grundutbildningens behov inom ämnet obstetrik och  gynekologi. Den huvudsakliga arbetsuppgiften är att leda och driva utbildningen inom obstetrik och gynekologi i Malmö samt vara en av tre ämneansvariga inom läkarprogrammet. Innehavaren ska dessutom vara beredd att ta på sig ytterligare ledningsuppdrag inom ämnet på läkarprogrammet, liksom andra utbildningsuppdrag på grund- och avancerad nivå vid Medicinska fakultetens utbildningsprogram samt inom forskarutbildningen. Utöver utbildningsuppdraget ingår att bedriva forskning inom obstetrik och gynekologi samt att medverka i forskarutbildningen. Innehavaren förväntas också vara beredd att bistå ledningsgruppen i utbildningsfrågor och medverka till strategisk utveckling av både utbildning och forskning inom ämnesområdet. Anställningen innefattar även arbetsuppgifter som normalt är förknippade med en tjänst som universitetslektor, såsom administration samt interna och externa förtroendeuppdrag på nationell och internationell nivå. I anställningen ingår självständig klinisk tjänstgöring inklusive jourtjänstgöring. Även andra arbetsuppgifter kan förekomma. Behörighet Behörig att anställas som lektor enligt Högskoleförordningen 4 kap 4 § är den som dels har visat pedagogisk skicklighet, dels har avlagt doktorsexamen eller har motsvarande vetenskaplig kompetens eller någon annan yrkesskicklighet som är av betydelse med hänsyn till anställningens ämnesinnehåll och de arbetsuppgifter som ska ingå i anställningen. Enligt Lunds universitets anställningsordning måste den sökande ha genomgått högskolepedagogisk utbildning om minst fem veckor eller på annat sätt ha inhämtat motsvarande kunskaper för att vara behörig, om det inte föreligger särskilda skäl. I den händelse att innehavaren bedöms ha särskilda skäl för att inte ha genomgått fem veckors högskolepedagogisk utbildning vid tillträdet av tjänsten, ska innehavaren genomföra sådan utbildning inom två år från tillträdet. Då arbetsuppgifterna innebär att leda och utveckla samt att undervisa inom grundutbildningen på främst läkarprogrammet, är svensk eller nordisk läkarlegitimation och specialistkompetens i obstetrik och gynekologi samt mycket goda kunskaper i svenska ett krav vid tillträdet. Språkkunskap i svenska lägst nivå C2 enligt Europarådets nivåskala är ett krav för anställningen. För lärare vid Lunds universitet gäller som allmänt behörighetskrav att vara lämplig för och ha den förmåga i övrigt som behövs för att fullgöra arbetsuppgifterna väl. Bedömningsgrunder Den sökande ska ha visat pedagogisk, vetenskaplig, administrativ och klinisk skicklighet av betydelse för ämnet och vid bedömningen kommer särskild vikt att tillmätas den pedagogiska skickligheten. Den sökande ska uppvisa pedagogisk skicklighet av relevans för ämnesområdet såväl inom utbildning som inom handledning på grund-, avancerad- och forskarutbildningsnivå. Detta visas genom en god förmåga att planera, leda, utveckla, driva och genomföra utbildning samt förmåga att omsätta klinisk kompetens i utbildningsmoment. Förmåga att leda universitetsutbildning på grund- och avancerad nivå kommer att vara särskilt meriterande. Vidare ska den sökande uppvisa vetenskaplig skicklighet genom att bedriva egen aktuell forskning på hög nationell eller internationell nivå. Vetenskaplig skicklighet visas genom publikationer i internationella vetenskapliga tidskrifter, anslag erhållna i konkurrens samt erfarenhet av nationellt och internationellt forskningssamarbete. Vidare visas vetenskaplig skicklighet genom forskningsprogram av relevans för ämnet och förutsättningar för långsiktig karriärutveckling. Den sökande ska visa god förmåga till ledarskap, samarbete och samverkan med det omgivande samhället. Vid anställning av lärare gäller, utöver vad som följer av Högskoleförordningen, Lunds universitets anställningsordning samt Medicinska fakultetens allmänna kravprofil och bedömningsgrunder vid anställning: https://www.medicin.lu.se/medicinska-fakulteten-vid-lunds-universitet/jobba-hos-oss/instruktioner-sokande-till-lararanstallningar Övrig information Upplysningar lämnas av prefekt Patrik Midlöv, tel. +46 73 079 13 63, patrik.midlov@med.lu.se och av dekan Maria Björkqvist, tel +46 72 700 71 63, maria.bjorkqvist@med.lu.se Upplysningar om ansökningsförfarande lämnas av rekryteringskoordinator Robert Norrman tel. +46 46 222 44 10, robert.norrman@med.lu.se Anställningen tillsätts efter förslag från Medicinska lärarförslagsnämnden. Ansökningsförfarande Anställningen söks elektroniskt via Lunds universitets sökandeportal senast 2026-11-01. Ansökan redovisas enligt Medicinska fakultetens anvisningar för sökande till läraranställning (se https://www.medicin.lu.se/medicinska-fakulteten-vid-lunds-universitet/jobba-hos-oss/instruktioner-sokande-till-lararanstallningar under rubrik Meritsammanställning och CV). Universitetet tillämpar individuell lönesättning. Ange gärna löneanspråk i din ansökan. Lunds universitet välkomnar sökande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. Vi ser jämställdhet och mångfald som en styrka och tillgång. Välkommen med din ansökan! The Faculty of Medicine is a part of Lund University, and is responsible for education and research within medicine and healthcare. Our academic programs are closely linked with the healthcare system and are firmly anchored in the faculty’s strong research tradition. Our research spans a broad field within experimental preclinical research, near-patient clinical research and health sciences research. The Faculty of Medicine, with its 1,800 employees and 2,700 students in Lund and Malmö, is a knowledge-intensive meeting place for students, teachers and researchers from all over the world. The Department of Clinical Sciences, Malmö is one of the six departments at the Faculty of Medicine, Lund University. We have a strong focus on clinical and epidemiological research and also conduct an extensive preclinical laboratory research. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time First day of employment In accordance with the agreed terms Salary Monthly payment Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Malmö County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/468 Contact Patrik Midlöv, Head of Department, +4640391363, patrik.midlov@med.lu.se Maria Björkqvist, Dean, +46727007163, maria.bjorkqvist@med.lu.se Robert Norrman, Recruitment officer, +46462224410, robert.norrman@med.lu.se Union representative OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, kansli@saco-s.lu.se, kansli@saco-s.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 01.Sep.2026 Last application date 01.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:975187/": {
      "title": "Vikariat som studievägledare",
      "description": "Vikariat som studievägledare Logga in och sök jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Vikariat som studievägledare Logga in och sök jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas återkommande som ett av världens främsta lärosäten. Här finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malmö. Vi förenas i vår strävan att förstå, förklara och förbättra vår värld och människors villkor. Lunds universitet välkomnar sökande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. Jämställdhet, lika villkor och mångfald är grundläggande principer för alla delar av vår verksamhet. Institutionen för kommunikation söker nu en studievägledare för ett vikariat. Läs mer om Lunds universitet och Institutionen för kommunikation här: Start | Institutionen för kommunikation Beskrivning av arbetsplatsen Institutionen för kommunikation finns på tre orter, Lund, Helsingborg och Malmö. Din placering kommer till största delen att vara på Campus Helsingborg. Någon arbetsdag per vecka arbetar du i Lund. Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet är en statlig myndighet vilket innebär att du får särskilda förmåner, generös semester och en förmånlig tjänstepension. Vi har även ett flextidsavtal som skapar goda förutsättningar för balans mellan arbete och fritid. Vi erbjuder en varierad och studentnära roll i en akademisk miljö och kollegialt samarbete med andra studievägledare och administratörer. Läs mer på universitetets webbplats om att vara anställd hos oss . Arbetsuppgifter och ansvarsområden Som studievägledare vid Institutionen för kommunikation förväntas du säkerställa en professionell studievägledning med hög kvalitet på såväl vägledning som bemötande av våra studenter. I rollen kommer du bland annat att ha uppgifter som: mottagning av presumtiva och nuvarande studenter vägledning av program och kursval studieadministration studieuppföljning karriärvägledning bereda studentärenden ta fram intyg och information till studenter I uppgifterna ingår även marknadsföring av kurser och program. Du kommer också att delta i olika nätverk och grupper tillsammans med andra studievägledare inom Lunds universitet. Även andra arbetsuppgifter kan komma att ingå. Kvalifikationer Vi söker dig som har: Erfarenhet av studievägledning vid universitet eller högskola. Akademisk examen inom studie- och karriärvägledning eller annan universitets- eller högskoleutbildning som arbetsgivaren bedömer som likvärdig. Förmåga att arbeta självständigt, strukturerat och med hög grad av ansvarstagande. Du tar ansvar för dina uppgifter och driver dina processer vidare. God initiativförmåga och ett lösningsorienterat arbetssätt. Hög noggrannhet och god administrativ förmåga. Ett lyhört, serviceinriktat och utåtriktat förhållningssätt. Mycket god kommunikativ förmåga, såväl muntligt som skriftligt. Mycket goda kunskaper i svenska och engelska, både i tal och skrift. Det är meriterande om du dessutom: har erfarenhet av arbete i Ladok, NyA, Canvas och W3D3 har kunskap om Lunds universitet Övrigt Anställningen är ett vikariat från och med januari 2027 till och med 30e juni 2027. Anställningens omfattning är 75% - 100%. Så här söker du Anställningen söks via universitets rekryteringssystem och din ansökan ska innehålla CV och ett personligt brev med motivering på vilket sätt dina meriter överensstämmer med uppställda krav. Bifoga examensbevis eller motsvarande samt övriga handlingar som du önskar åberopa (kopior av betyg, kontaktuppgifter till referenser, rekommendationsbrev etc.). Välkommen med din ansökan! Universitetet tillämpar individuell lönesättning. Ange gärna löneanspråk i din ansökan. Samhällsvetenskapliga fakulteten vid Lunds universitet är ett av landets ledande kunskapscentra för forskning och utbildning inom samhälls- och beteendevetenskap. Med verksamhet i både Lund och Helsingborg, över 700 anställda och cirka 5 700 helårsstudenter är fakulteten en av Lunds universitets största. Vi erbjuder en kreativ akademisk miljö med engagerade studenter och medarbetare. Vår huvuduppgift är att utveckla, förmedla och förvalta kunskap om samhälle, människa och organisationer i en miljö som präglas av öppenhet, tolerans och nyfikenhet. Institutionen för kommunikation erbjuder en internationell, interdisciplinär och dynamisk miljö för utbildning och forskning inom journalistik, strategisk kommunikation samt medie- och kommunikationsvetenskap. Våra utbildningar kombinerar teoretiska insikter med praktiska färdigheter för att rusta studenter för arbetslivet och vidare studier. Vi arbetar nära mediebranschen, civilsamhället, företag och offentlig sektor för att ge studenter och forskare möjlighet att bidra till och dra nytta av verksamhet utanför akademin. Våra forskare studerar kommunikations- och medielandskapets utveckling på lokal, nationell och global nivå. De utforskar och analyserar kritiskt hur kommunikation och digitala medieteknologier påverkar organisationer, politik, samhälle och kultur. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter från annonsförsäljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsföretag på grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anställningsform Tidsbegränsad anställning Anställningens omfattning Heltid/Deltid Löneform Månadslön Antal lediga befattningar 1 Sysselsättningsgrad 75-100 Ort Helsingborg Län Skåne län Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2859 Kontakt Tobias Linné, Prefekt, tobias.linne@iko.lu.se Emelie Larenhjelm, HR-administratör, emelie.larenhjelm@sam.lu.se Facklig företrädare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-16 Sista ansökningsdag 2026-10-30 Logga in och sök jobbet Dela länkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillgänglighetsredogörelse × Modal title Vi använder cookies för inloggning, förbättrad användarupplevelse, dela-länkar samt i vissa fall marknadsföring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast nödvändiga Läs mer om våra cookies här ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:976668/": {
      "title": "Serviceassistent vid BMC",
      "description": "Serviceassistent vid BMC Logga in och sök jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Serviceassistent vid BMC Logga in och sök jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas återkommande som ett av världens främsta lärosäten. Här finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malmö. Vi förenas i vår strävan att förstå, förklara och förbättra vår värld och människors villkor. Lunds universitet välkomnar sökande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. Jämställdhet, lika villkor och mångfald är grundläggande principer för alla delar av vår verksamhet. Verksamhetsstöd är Medicinska fakultetens gemensamma support- och serviceorganisation. Vi ger samordnat och behovsanpassat stöd till fakultetens verksamheter inom flera olika områden – och bidrar till en väl fungerande vardag för forskning, utbildning och administration. Verksamhetsstöd omfattar fem verksamhetsområden: Bibliotek, Lokalservice , Lokalplanering, IT samt Universitetsveterinären. Här finns även en stab och ett HMS-team som samordnar fakultetens arbete med hälsa, miljö och säkerhet. Avdelningen för Lokalservice ansvarar för teknik och service på BMC (Lund) och CRC (Malmö).  Avdelningens uppdrag är att verkställa underhåll, fastighetsskötsel samt leverans av fastställda tjänster mot fakultetens egna verksamheter (t ex kansli och institutioner). Avdelningen arbetar även med förebyggande och avhjälpande underhåll, och tar inom sitt ansvarsområde emot felanmälningar och beställningar från verksamheten. Inom Verksamhetsstöd värnar vi om en god arbetsmiljö med respekt och omtanke i relationerna med varandra. Vi söker nu en serviceassistent till avdelningen Lokalservice med placering på BMC i Lund. Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet är en statlig myndighet vilket innebär att du får särskilda förmåner, generös semester och en förmånlig tjänstepension. Läs mer på universitetets webbplats \"https://www.lu.se/om-universitetet/jobba-hos-oss\" om att vara anställd hos oss. Arbetsuppgifter Som serviceassistent kommer du i huvudsak att arbeta med: bokning och möblering av möteslokaler / lokaler, postsortering och utdelning av post, vid behov vara backup / extra resurs till receptionen. Även andra arbetsuppgifter som är relevanta för den verksamhet som bedrivs inom Lokalservice kan förekomma. Arbetsuppgifterna kan medföra tunga lyft. Arbetet som serviceassistent innebär kontakter med olika delar av verksamheten och sker till stor del i samarbete med vår övriga serviceorganisation. Kvalifikationer Krav: genomförd gymnasieutbildning med godkänt resultat (betyg), erfarenhet av serviceinriktat arbete, datorvana och god erfarenhet av arbete med MS Office (Word, Excel och Outlook), goda språkkunskaper i svenska och engelska, körkort B - för manuellt växlad bil. Meriterande: erfarenhet av receptions- och konferensarbete erfarenhet av arbete med stödsystem; till exempel TimeEdit, Salto och Serix, Stor vikt kommer att läggas vid personliga egenskaper. Arbetsuppgifterna förutsätter att du har gott ordningssinne, samordnings- och samarbetsförmåga. Det är viktigt att du har en väl utvecklad servicekänsla samt en professionell och positiv framtoning. Vi ser gärna att du tar dig an dina arbetsuppgifter på ett ansvarsfullt sätt och har en stark vilja att främja en god teamkänsla Övrigt anställningen innebär att du förväntas bära tilldelad arbetsklädsel, vid behov kan tjänstgöring i Malmö vara aktuellt, provanställning kommer att tillämpas, startdatum enligt överenskommelse, vid erbjudande om anställning kommer berörd sökande att behöva bekräfta sin identitet via pass / nationellt id-kort. Avdelningen strävar efter en mer jämställd arbetsplats varpå vi gärna ser att både kvinnor och män söker anställningen. Medicinska fakulteten är ett verksamhetsområde inom Lunds universitet, med ansvar för utbildning och forskning inom medicin, vård och hälsa. Utbildningen sker i nära samverkan med sjukvården och är väl förankrad i fakultetens starka forskningstradition. Fakultetens forskning spänner över ett brett fält inom experimentell grundforskning, patientnära klinisk forskning och hälsovetenskaplig forskning. Medicinska fakulteten, med drygt 1800 anställda och 3000 studenter i Lund, Malmö och Helsingborg, är en kunskapsintensiv mötesplats för studenter, lärare och forskare från hela världen. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter från annonsförsäljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsföretag på grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anställningsform Tillsvidareanställning Anställningens omfattning Heltid Tillträde Snarast eller efter överenskommelse Löneform Månadslön Antal lediga befattningar 1 Sysselsättningsgrad 100 Ort Lund Län Skåne län Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2897 Kontakt Joel Johansson, Avdelningschef, +4640391109, joel.johansson@med.lu.se Jeffrey Armstrong, HR-specialist, +46462227103, jeffrey.armstrong@med.lu.se Facklig företrädare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-16 Sista ansökningsdag 2026-10-25 Logga in och sök jobbet Dela länkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillgänglighetsredogörelse × Modal title Vi använder cookies för inloggning, förbättrad användarupplevelse, dela-länkar samt i vissa fall marknadsföring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast nödvändiga Läs mer om våra cookies här ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:977396/": {
      "title": "Postdoc experienced in electrochemistry research",
      "description": "Postdoc experienced in electrochemistry research Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoc experienced in electrochemistry research Login and apply Lund University, MAX IV, Beamline Office Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. MAX IV is looking for a Postdoc experienced in electrochemistry research. The focus will be to document experimental designs and procedures that give reliable and reproducible results, transferrable between research facilities in Europe. Two to three reaction cells based on the most promising designs will be developed and tested at major European synchrotrons. All results (CAD models, performance data, and procedures) will be published in an open data base for the benefit of the European research community. Your team At MAX IV, you will work in the Support Labs team which is part of the Beamline Office group. The Support Labs team is involved in support for sample preparation, installation and maintenance of sample environments, as well as detector support for beamlines. In addition, the team operates ten chemistry and instrumentation labs across MAX IV. This project was granted funding from the EU organisation LEAPS, consisting of all major synchrotron radiation sources in Europe. The motivation for the project comes from academia and industry that seeks standardisation of electrochemical experiments and technical solutions to ensure reproducible and accurate results from all facilities. The project is called SEEQuality and includes close collaboration with a postdoc at ESRF/CEA (France) and an engineer at HZB (Germany). Your main work tasks will be Plan and partake in the development of an expert advisory board in electrochemistry. The board will guide in selecting the best technical solutions. Jointly with ESRF/CEA and HZB review the best designs for electrochemistry experiments, and documenting these in the open database Wayforlight. Take part in the development of electrochemical reaction cells (demonstrators) in collaboration with ESRF/CEA and HZB. Take part in the in the initial testing of the reaction cells and collect data to be published in the Wayforlight database. Take part in a Round-robin test of the developed reaction cells at different synchrotron facilities. To be successful in this role you need to have the following qualifications PhD in physics, chemistry, or engineering. Demonstrated experience with electrochemistry research at synchrotron radiation sources or similar large research infrastructures. You are interested in interdisciplinary work in collaboration with research groups of very diverse backgrounds as well as engineers and technicians Good command of the English language, good communication and team working skills. Below are seen as merits Demonstrated experience in the development of electrochemical reaction cells. Experience in analysis of data from electrochemical research. Experience with documentation and certification of instrumentation for laboratory experiments. Experience with instrumentation used in synchrotron X-ray based research. As a person you have a demonstrated ability to work independently, as well as having the ability to cooperate with different teams and functions. Eligibility Appointment to the position of postdoc requires that the applicant has a PhD or an international degree deemed equivalent to a PhD, within the subject of the position, completed no more than three years before the application deadline. Under special circumstances the PhD can have been completed previous to the aforementioned three years. Further information This is a full-time, fixed-term employment for 2 years. A postdoctoral fellow is employed under a period of at least two years and at most three years. The period of employment is determined in accordance with the agreement “Avtal om tidsbegränsad anställning som postdoktor-2022-02-01” (“Agreement on fixed-term employment as a post-doctoral fellow, 2022-02-01”) What we offer When you join our MAX IV team, you step into a world of cutting-edge science. We make the invisible visible by supporting scientists from all over the world and enabling scientific results for the benefit of society. We offer a multicultural work environment with opportunities for professional development and a healthy work-life balance. Would you like to work in a challenging and supportive environment and contribute directly to the reliable operation of one of the world's most advanced synchrotron facilities? Then join us and take the opportunity to make a real difference. For further information, please visit: https://www.lunduniversity.lu.se/about-lund-university/work-lund-university https://www.sweden.se https://www.maxiv.lu.se/about-us/careers/compensation-benefits/ Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences. We regard gender equality and diversity as a strength and an asset. MAX IV is a Swedish national large-scale research infrastructure hosted by Lund University. It provides scientists from Sweden and abroad, with intense x-rays and state-of-the-art instrumentation for research in areas such as engineering, physics, structural biology, chemistry and nanotechnology. Its 16 beamlines receive up to 2 000 scientists annually, conducting ground-breaking experiments in materials and life sciences using the brilliant X-rays. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment As per agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2912 Contact Johan Adell, +46708323357, johan.adell@maxiv.lu.se Stefan Carlson, +46733439550, stefan.carlson@maxiv.lu.se Union representative OFR/S:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds, 046-2229364, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 16.Oct.2026 Last application date 08.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:977402/": {
      "title": "RF Technician",
      "description": "RF Technician Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) RF Technician Login and apply Lund University, MAX IV, Accelerator Division Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. MAX IV is looking for a RF Technician to join the RF Group. Your team The RF Group at MAX IV is responsible for the operation, maintenance and development of several high-power radio-frequency systems that are essential for the MAX IV accelerators. The systems include pulsed S-band RF systems as well as continuous-wave VHF/UHF systems, together with associated high-voltage modulators, diagnostics, instrumentation and control systems. Would you like to work hands-on with advanced accelerator technology at one of the brightest light sources in the world? About the role You will work with the operation, maintenance, repair and installation of RF, electronic and high-voltage equipment used throughout the MAX IV accelerator facility. The position has a strong practical focus and involves troubleshooting, repairing, modifying and maintaining specialised technical equipment. The work includes electronics, electrical systems, cabling and, where needed, basic mechanical fabrication and modification of parts. You will work closely with RF engineers and other technical staff to ensure high reliability and availability of the accelerator RF systems. MAX IV is preparing for MAX 4 U , a major upgrade of the 3 GeV storage ring. As part of the RF Group, you will have the opportunity to contribute to the technical work associated with this upgrade, including installation, modification and commissioning of RF-related equipment. Your main work tasks will be Maintenance, troubleshooting and repair of RF, electronic and high-voltage equipment. Maintenance and repair of high-voltage modulators. Electrical and electronic assembly work. Precision soldering and repair of electronic equipment and circuit boards. Manufacturing, installation and repair of cables and cable assemblies. Installation and modification of RF equipment, electronics and associated infrastructure. Preventive maintenance and inspection of technical systems. Documentation of maintenance, repairs and technical modifications. Participation in fault finding and corrective maintenance during accelerator operation. Collaboration with RF engineers in system upgrades, improvements and new installations. Participate in technical installations, modifications and commissioning activities related to future accelerator upgrades, including MAX 4 U . To be successful in this role you need to have the following qualifications Relevant technical education in electronics, electrical engineering, RF technology or a related technical field, or equivalent professional experience. Good practical skills in electronics and electrical work. Experience with soldering and assembly of electronic equipment. Ability to read and understand electrical schematics and technical documentation. Experience in troubleshooting and repairing electrical or electronic equipment. A structured and safety-conscious way of working. Good command of spoken and written English. Good communication and teamwork skills. Experience with high-voltage equipment. Experience with high-power electronics. Experience with cable manufacturing, connectors and RF cabling. Experience in the fields below is considered a merit RF systems or RF equipment. Pulsed power systems or modulators. Industrial electronics. Electrical cabinets and installations. Measurement equipment such as oscilloscopes, multimeters and signal generators. Mechanical workshop skills, such as using a milling machine, drill press and other common workshop tools. Basic mechanical fabrication, modification and fitting of components. Maintenance of complex scientific, industrial or accelerator equipment. Experience from accelerator facilities or synchrotron light sources is an advantage, but not a requirement. About you We are looking for someone who enjoys practical technical work and takes pride in solving problems and keeping complex equipment operational. You are systematic, thorough and safety-conscious, and you are comfortable working both independently and together with engineers and technicians. You are curious and willing to learn new systems and technologies, and you enjoy turning technical problems into practical solutions. What we offer When you join our MAX IV team, you step into a world of cutting-edge science. We make the invisible visible by supporting scientists from all over the world and enabling scientific results for the benefit of society. We offer a multicultural work environment with opportunities for professional development and a healthy work-life balance. Would you like to work in a challenging and supportive environment and contribute directly to the reliable operation of one of the world's most advanced synchrotron facilities? Then join us and take the opportunity to make a real difference. For further information, please visit: https://www.lunduniversity.lu.se/about-lund-university/work-lund-university https://www.sweden.se https://www.maxiv.lu.se/about-us/careers/compensation-benefits/ Probationary period may apply. On-call services may apply. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences. We regard gender equality and diversity as a strength and an asset. MAX IV is a Swedish national large-scale research infrastructure hosted by Lund University. It provides scientists from Sweden and abroad, with intense x-rays and state-of-the-art instrumentation for research in areas such as engineering, physics, structural biology, chemistry and nanotechnology. Its 16 beamlines receive up to 2 000 scientists annually, conducting ground-breaking experiments in materials and life sciences using the brilliant X-rays. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Permanent position – (starting with a temporary contract) Contract type Full time First day of employment As per agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2913 Contact Robert Lindvall, gruppchef, +46462221598, robert.lindvall@maxiv.lu.se Union representative OFR/S:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds, 046-2229364, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Published 16.Oct.2026 Last application date 01.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:978489/": {
      "title": "PhD in Sociology of Law",
      "description": "PhD in Sociology of Law – Islamic Ethics and Governance in Central Asia Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) PhD in Sociology of Law – Islamic Ethics and Governance in Central Asia Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. PhD Position in Sociology of Post-Imperial Islamic Legal Cultures – Islamic Ethics and Administrative Reform in Central Asia Project description This doctoral project investigates how Islamic ethical principles influence legal and governance reforms in Uzbekistan and Kazakhstan. The doctoral candidate will examine whether religiously informed governance practices and legal strategies strengthen accountability, public trust, and institutional effectiveness, or whether they primarily serve as tools of political legitimation. The project engages with emerging scholarship on Islamic public administration, Islamic legal culture and governance traditions. To read more about the MINARET project please see: https://www.norca.lu.se/minaret https://www.soclaw.lu.se/en/article/major-eu-grant-lund-led-phd-programme-islamic-legal-cultures Tasks and responsibilities As a doctoral student, you will be admitted to doctoral studies in sociology of law and employed at Lund University. You will: Conduct independent research within the scope of the project. Undertake multi-sited fieldwork in Central Asia (Kazakhstan and Uzbekistan) and two mandatory secondments (one academic, one non-academic) abroad. Participate in training events, workshops, and conferences organized by the MINARET Doctoral Network. Collaborate with international supervisors and peers. Contribute to departmental activities, including teaching and seminars (up to 20% of working hours). If selected for the position, you will join NORCA – Nordic Central Asian Studies ( www.norca.lu.se ) research environment at the Sociology of Law Department, led by Rustamjon Urinboyev who will also serve as your principal supervisor. You will be given sufficient time, guidance, and resources to develop your individual research project, aligned with the overall MINARET project's aims. Doctoral Programme in Sociology of Law The doctoral programme in sociology of law comprises 240 credits (equivalent to four years of full-time study) and concludes with a public defence of the doctoral thesis. You will primarily engage in doctoral studies and work on your dissertation within the field of sociology of law. You will also actively participate in the department’s research environment. In addition to research, the position may include teaching and administrative duties, up to a maximum of 20% of the working time. The working language is primarily English, but you are expected to acquire basic knowledge of Swedish during the employment period. More information about the doctoral programme is available at: https://www.soclaw.lu.se/en/research/doctoral-studies/phd-handbook General Requirements The requirements for admission to third cycle courses and study programs (in accordance with HF, Chapter 7, Section 35) are that the applicant; meets the general and specific entry requirements that the higher education institution may have laid down, and is considered in other respects to have the ability required to benefit from the course or study program. A person meets the general entry requirements for third cycle courses and study programmes if he or she: has been awarded a second cycle qualification prior to the employment decision, has satisfied the requirements for courses comprising at least 240 credits of which at least 60 credits were awarded in the second cycle, or has acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. Specific Requirements A completed degree at the advanced level in Sociology of Law or another subject deemed relevant by the employer. Doctoral candidates cannot have been awarded a doctoral degree and/or completed more than four years of full-time equivalent research experience. In line with the eligibility criteria and on Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Networks programme, doctoral candidates must not have resided or carried out their main activity (i.e. work, studies) in the hosting country for more than 12 months in the 3 years immediately before the recruitment date. For further information on eligibility criteria and on Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Networks in general, please refer to: Doctoral Networks - Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions . A minimum of 240 credits, of which at least 60 must be at the advanced level. At least 30 credits in Sociology of Law or a related subject at the advanced level, including a thesis of at least 15 credits. Excellent ability to express yourself in spoken and written English. Strong motivation and ability to work independently under pressure. Good collaboration and communication skills. Merits Knowledge of legal sociology, Islamic public administration, Islamic legal culture and governance traditions. Experience with qualitative research methods and fieldwork. Self-motivated, perseverant, and strong writing skills. Collaborative and independent working style. Knowledge of Central Asian legal and political contexts is an asset. What we offer A full-time, fixed-term employment for four years. Competitive employment package. Joint supervision and intersectoral placements. Comprehensive training in research methods, ethics, Open Science, and transferable skills. Assessment Criteria Regulations for employment as a doctoral student can be found in the Higher Education Ordinance . Only those admitted to third-cycle studies may be appointed to a doctoral position. In the recruitment process, primary consideration will be given to the applicant’s ability to benefit from the doctoral programme. The research plan, as well as previous theses and published material in Sociology of Law or related subjects within social sciences or law, are important documents for assessing this ability. In addition to pursuing their own doctoral studies, the incumbent may be required to perform duties related to education, research, and administration in accordance with specific provisions in the Higher Education Ordinance . Excellent ability to express oneself in speech and writing is of great importance. As doctoral studies in Sociology of Law are highly demanding, the candidate must be strongly motivated and able to work independently under pressure. Good collaboration and communication skills are also required, as well as strong proficiency in English, both spoken and written. Application The application must include: A cover letter in English (max 1,000 words), including a brief presentation of yourself and your qualifications, as well as a short description of why you are interested in the doctoral programme in Sociology of Law at the Sociology of Law Department, Lund University. A thesis corresponding to at least 15 credits at the advanced level in Sociology of Law or a subject deemed equivalent/relevant, and other relevant publications. If the thesis is written in a language other than Swedish, Danish, Norwegian, or English, a summary of max 1,000 words must be included, outlining the methodology, theory, results/analysis. A CV in English demonstrating eligibility for doctoral studies in Sociology of Law. Degree certificates and transcripts in English. A research proposal of no more than 13,000 characters (including spaces and references), written in English. Please ensure that your proposed research aligns closely with the focus of the PhD project, Islamic Ethics and Administrative Reform in Central Asia . General guidelines for preparing a research plan can be found here: https://www.soclaw.lu.se/en/sites/soclaw.lu.se.en/files/ras_phd_research_plan.pdf Names and contact details of two referees. A writing sample (e.g., master’s thesis or published paper) that demonstrates the applicant’s research and writing skills. Any other documents the applicant wishes to submit in support of the application. Applicants will be assessed based on the above criteria, and top-ranked candidates will be invited for an interview. Gender equality must always be considered. In cases of equal qualifications, the underrepresented gender within the subject at Lund University shall be prioritized, unless valid reasons suggest otherwise. Employment Type The position is full-time (100%) for four years, starting in September 2027. You are required to work on-site in Lund, Sweden. Employment is governed by the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), Chapter 5. Additional Information For questions regarding the MINARET Doctoral Networks Programme and PhD project, please contact Dr. Rustamjon Urinboyev at rustamjon.urinboyev@soclaw.lu.se , Principal Investigator of the MINARET Doctoral Networks programme. For questions about the doctoral programme in sociology of law, please contact Ida Nafstad at ida.nafstad@soclaw.lu.se . For questions about the recruitment process, please contact Ellen Karlsson at ellen.karlsson@sam.lu.se . The Faculty of Social Sciences at Lund University is one of the leading education and research institutions in Sweden and operates both in Lund and Helsingborg. Sociology of law at Lund University is a subject within Social sciences focusing on the relationship between law and society, such as the tension between the formal legislation of the government and the informal emergence of norms in civil society, among other contexts. Research is conducted in fields such as gender and discrimination, AI and machine learning, children's rights, welfare, legal cultures, corruption, migration, financial security and crime. The department offers courses at all levels. The department also runs the bachelor's program in criminology in collaboration with the Department of Sociology. The Sociology of Law Department is keen to engage in cross-disciplinary collaboration and has good contacts with professionals and public authorities. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment 2027-09-01 Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2939 Contact Rustamjon Urinboyev, Associate professor, rustamjon.urinboyev@soclaw.lu.se Ida Nafstad, Associate professor, ida.nafstad@soclaw.lu.se Ellen Karlsson, HR partner, ellen.karlsson@sam.lu.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 16.Oct.2026 Last application date 31.Jan.2027 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:979730/": {
      "title": "Bibliotekarie till Juridiska fakultetens bibliotek",
      "description": "Bibliotekarie till Juridiska fakultetens bibliotek Logga in och sök jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Bibliotekarie till Juridiska fakultetens bibliotek Logga in och sök jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas återkommande som ett av världens främsta lärosäten. Här finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malmö. Vi förenas i vår strävan att förstå, förklara och förbättra vår värld och människors villkor. Lunds universitet välkomnar sökande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. Jämställdhet, lika villkor och mångfald är grundläggande principer för alla delar av vår verksamhet. Juridiska fakultetens bibliotek utgör en del av biblioteksverksamheten vid Lunds universitet som består av Universitetsbiblioteket och åtta fakultetsbibliotek. Biblioteket är ett av Nordens största juridiska bibliotek och är även ett Europeiskt dokumentationscentrum. Vår verksamhet är väl integrerad i Juridiska fakultetens forsknings- och utbildningsprocesser. Vi förser fakultetens forskare, lärare och studenter med ämnesanpassat biblioteksstöd, och tillhandahåller även service till Lunds universitet och till allmänheten. Juridiska fakultetens bibliotek söker en vikarie för vårterminen. Du kommer att ingå i ett team av inkluderande och välkomnande kollegor som bidrar med sin kompetens i en kreativ akademisk miljö med engagerade medarbetare och studenter. För mer information om biblioteket se: https://www.jur.lu.se/bibliotek Vi erbjuder Lunds universitet är en statlig myndighet vilket innebär att du får särskilda förmåner, generös semester och en förmånlig tjänstepension. Vi har även ett flextidsavtal som skapar goda förutsättningar för balans mellan arbete och fritid. Läs mer på universitetets webbplats om att jobba hos oss Arbetsuppgifter Anställningen är ett vikariat med fokus på mediehantering och användarstöd där du i ditt arbete både samarbetar med kollegor och fördjupar dig självständigt. Kanske har du lagt grunden inom yrket och är redo att ta nästa steg i rollen som bibliotekarie, eller vill du byta inriktning och testa arbete med ämnesfördjupning inom akademin? Då kan detta vara ett perfekt tillfälle för dig. Juridiska biblioteket är i inledningsskedet av ett stort gallringsprojekt som ska säkerställa samlingarnas relevans och användbarhet, och samtidigt upprätta rutiner för konsekvent gallring och ett hållbart samlingsarbete på sikt. Med stöd i riktlinjer och manualer kommer du att få vara med och lägga grunden för det praktiska arbetet med systematisk gallring. Arbetsuppgifterna i vikariatet har fokus på mediehantering och användarstöd. Gallring i magasin och på öppna hyllor liksom tjänstgöring i bibliotekets informationsdisk ingår. Övriga allmänt förekommande arbetsuppgifter på ett akademiskt bibliotek kan tillkomma. Kvalifikationer Krav för anställningen är: Akademisk examen i biblioteks- och informationsvetenskap, eller motsvarande som arbetsgivaren bedömer likvärdigt Mycket goda kunskaper i svenska och engelska i tal och skrift Du måste vara kvalitetsmedveten, serviceinriktad, ha en välutvecklad samarbetsförmåga samt ta självständigt ansvar för dina arbetsuppgifter och ditt lärande. Meriterande för anställningen är: Erfarenhet av arbete vid universitets- eller högskolebibliotek Erfarenhet av gallringsarbete Erfarenhet av arbete i informationsdisk Vi vill även att du har helhetsperspektiv och förmåga att prioritera. Vi lägger stor vikt vid personlig lämplighet samt hur du genom din erfarenhet och kompetens bedöms komplettera och stärka verksamheten vid Juridiska fakultetens bibliotek. Villkor Anställningen är ett vikariat på 100% under 6 månader med startdatum 2027-01-07 eller enligt överenskommelse, som längst till och med 2027-06-30. Intervjuer är planerade till vecka 47. Så här söker du Anställningen söks via universitetets rekryteringssystem. Ansökan ska innehålla personligt brev med motivering till varför du är intresserad av anställningen och på vilket sätt anställningen matchar dina meriter. Ansökan ska även innehålla CV, examensbevis eller motsvarande samt övrigt som du önskar åberopa (kopior av betyg, uppgifter till referenser etc.) Juridiska fakulteten är en av Lunds universitets fyra ursprungliga fakulteter. Vid fakulteten verkar ca 2000 studenter på grundnivå och avancerad nivå och ett 160-tal anställda varav ett 40-tal är doktorander. Mer information om fakulteten finns på vår hemsida www.jur.lu.se Vi undanber oss alla kontakter från annonsförsäljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsföretag på grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anställningsform Tidsbegränsad anställning Anställningen avslutas 2027-06-30 Anställningens omfattning Heltid Tillträde 2027-01-07 eller enligt överenskommelse Löneform Månadslön Antal lediga befattningar 1 Sysselsättningsgrad 100 Ort Lund Län Skåne län Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2978 Kontakt Catarina Carlsson, Bibliotekschef, +46462221096, catarina.carlsson@jur.lu.se Facklig företrädare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-16 Sista ansökningsdag 2026-11-09 Logga in och sök jobbet Dela länkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillgänglighetsredogörelse × Modal title Vi använder cookies för inloggning, förbättrad användarupplevelse, dela-länkar samt i vissa fall marknadsföring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast nödvändiga Läs mer om våra cookies här ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:979777/": {
      "title": "Grafisk produktionsmedarbetare till Media-Tryck",
      "description": "Grafisk produktionsmedarbetare till Media-Tryck Logga in och sök jobbet Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Grafisk produktionsmedarbetare till Media-Tryck Logga in och sök jobbet Lunds universitet Lunds universitet grundades 1666 och rankas återkommande som ett av världens främsta lärosäten. Här finns omkring 46 000 studenter och 8 500 medarbetare i Lund, Helsingborg och Malmö. Vi förenas i vår strävan att förstå, förklara och förbättra vår värld och människors villkor. Lunds universitet välkomnar sökande med olika bakgrund och erfarenheter. Jämställdhet, lika villkor och mångfald är grundläggande principer för alla delar av vår verksamhet. Vill du arbeta praktiskt med grafisk produktion i en verksamhet där kvalitet, samarbete och leverans står i centrum? Som produktionsmedarbetare på Media-Tryck blir du en viktig del av ett gemensamt produktionsteam som hjälper Lunds universitets verksamheter från färdigt produktionsunderlag till färdig produkt. Här får du ett varierat arbete med modern produktionsutrustning, tydliga deadlines och stort ansvar för att uppdragen blir rätt utförda och levererade i tid. Välkommen till LU Service och Media-Tryck LU Service erbjuder tjänster och produkter till hela universitetet inom bland annat lokalservice, reception, konferens, post och grafisk produktion. Media-Tryck är universitetets interna leverantör av grafiska tjänster och arbetar med hela processen – från idé och original till tryck, efterbehandling, distribution och leverans. Verksamheten kombinerar service, produktion och rådgivning och har ett stort fokus på kvalitet, leverans och utveckling. Om rollen Som produktionsmedarbetare arbetar du brett genom flera delar av produktionen. Du planerar och prioriterar ditt arbete utifrån inkommande uppdrag och deadlines och säkerställer tillsammans med kollegorna att produktionen håller rätt kvalitet och använder verksamhetens resurser effektivt. Rollen är inte knuten till en enskild maskin. Arbetsuppgifterna varierar, och du förväntas hjälpa till där behovet för tillfället är störst. Arbetsuppgifter Digital tryckproduktion, stor- och småformatsproduktion. Efterbehandling. Kontroll av produktionsunderlag inför produktion. Kvalitetskontroll av producerat material. Enklare felsökning, underhåll och löpande tillsyn av produktionsutrustning. Planering och prioritering av det egna arbetet utifrån uppdrag och deadlines. Att tillsammans med kollegorna bidra till ordning, struktur och ett effektivt produktionsflöde. Kvalifikationer För att vara aktuell för anställningen ska du ha: Erfarenhet av arbete inom grafisk produktion, tryckproduktion eller annan jämförbar produktionsmiljö. Erfarenhet av att arbeta med maskiner och produktionsutrustning. God digital vana och förmåga att arbeta i olika system. Förmåga att förstå och följa produktionsinstruktioner och arbetsflöden. God förmåga att kommunicera på svenska och engelska i tal och skrift. Meriterande Det är meriterande om du har erfarenhet av ett eller flera av följande områden: Digital tryckproduktion. Storformatsproduktion med monteringserfarenhet. Efterbehandling. Produktions- eller ordersystem inom grafisk verksamhet. Grundläggande kunskaper inom prepress och hantering av PDF-filer för tryckproduktion. Vem är du? Du arbetar systematiskt och noggrant och kan hålla ordning och kvalitet även när flera uppdrag pågår samtidigt. Du är flexibel och kan växla mellan arbetsuppgifter, maskiner och olika typer av produktion. Eftersom vi arbetar som ett gemensamt team behöver du ha god samarbetsförmåga, ta ansvar för helheten och bidra där behovet finns. Du har en praktisk problemlösningsförmåga, uppmärksammar problem i tid och vet när du behöver ta hjälp. Du är nyfiken på att lära dig nya maskiner, produktionsmetoder och arbetssätt. I kontakten med kunder och kollegor är du professionell, lyhörd och lösningsorienterad. Du tar reda på behov, ger tydlig återkoppling och följer upp det ni har kommit överens om. Vi kommer att lägga stor vikt vid personlig lämplighet och hur din erfarenhet och dina egenskaper kompletterar teamet. Vi erbjuder Ett varierat och praktiskt arbete i en unik universitetsmiljö. Möjlighet att utveckla din kompetens inom flera delar av grafisk produktion. Engagerade kollegor och ett arbetssätt där vi hjälper varandra och tar gemensamt ansvar för leveransen. Generös semester, friskvårdsförmåner, förmånlig tjänstepension och andra statliga anställningsvillkor. Läs mer om hur det är att jobba hos oss på universitetets hemsida, länk nedan. Jobba hos oss | Lunds universitet Övrigt Anställningen är en tillsvidareanställning på 100 %, med tillträde snarast enligt överenskommelse. Provanställning i 6 månader kan komma att tillämpas. Lönespannet för tjänsten är 30 000 - 37 000 kr. Universitetet tillämpar individuell lönesättning. Ange gärna löneanspråk i din ansökan. LU Service är en sektion inom universitetets gemensamma förvaltning och erbjuder såväl tjänster som produkter till universitetets verksamheter: bl.a. lokalvård, vaktmästeri, reception, tryckeri, post, parkering, universitetsbutik, konferens och bostäder. LU Service har ca 240 medarbetare. Vi undanber oss alla kontakter från annonsförsäljare, rekryterings- och bemanningsföretag på grund av statliga upphandlingsregler. Anställningsform Tillsvidareanställning Anställningens omfattning Heltid Tillträde 2026-12-01 eller enligt överenskommelse Löneform Månadslön Antal lediga befattningar 1 Sysselsättningsgrad 100 Ort Lund Län Skåne län Land Sverige Referensnummer PA2026/2979 Kontakt Mikael Olofsson, Avdelningschef, mikael.olofsson@service.lu.se Facklig företrädare SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se Publicerat 2026-10-16 Sista ansökningsdag 2026-10-30 Logga in och sök jobbet Dela länkar Tillbaka till lediga jobb Grade Varbi Recruit rekryteringsverktyg Cookies Villkor Dataskyddspolicy Tillgänglighetsredogörelse × Modal title Vi använder cookies för inloggning, förbättrad användarupplevelse, dela-länkar samt i vissa fall marknadsföring och insamling av statistik. Acceptera alla cookies Acceptera endast nödvändiga Läs mer om våra cookies här ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:980150/": {
      "title": "PhD in Sociology of Law",
      "description": "PhD in Sociology of Law – Women's Legal Agency in Central Asia and MENA Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) PhD in Sociology of Law – Women's Legal Agency in Central Asia and MENA Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. PhD Position in Sociology of Post-Imperial Islamic Legal Cultures – Women's Legal Agency Across Post-Imperial Islamic Societies in Central Asia, the Middle East, and North Africa Project description This doctoral project explores how women in Tunisia, Lebanon, and Uzbekistan use both Islamic and secular legal frameworks to claim rights, challenge discrimination, and expand access to justice. The doctoral candidate will analyse legal mobilisation, constitutional reform, and women’s agency as drivers of social and political transformation in post-imperial Islamic societies. To read more about the MINARET project please see: https://www.norca.lu.se/minaret https://www.soclaw.lu.se/en/article/major-eu-grant-lund-led-phd-programme-islamic-legal-cultures Tasks and responsibilities As a doctoral student, you will be admitted to doctoral studies in sociology of law and employed at Lund University. You will: Conduct independent research within the scope of the project. Undertake multi-sited fieldwork in Central Asia, the Middle East and North Africa (Uzbekistan, Lebanon and Tunisia) and two mandatory secondments (one academic, one non-academic) abroad. Participate in training events, workshops, and conferences organized by the MINARET Doctoral Network. Collaborate with international supervisors and peers. Contribute to departmental activities, including teaching and seminars (up to 20% of working hours). If selected for the position, you will join NORCA – Nordic Central Asian Studies ( www.norca.lu.se ) research environment at the Sociology of Law Department, led by Rustamjon Urinboyev who will also serve as your principal supervisor. You will be given sufficient time, guidance, and resources to develop your individual research project, aligned with the overall MINARET project's aims. Doctoral Programme in Sociology of Law The doctoral programme in sociology of law comprises 240 credits (equivalent to four years of full-time study) and concludes with a public defence of the doctoral thesis. You will primarily engage in doctoral studies and work on your dissertation within the field of sociology of law. You will also actively participate in the department’s research environment. In addition to research, the position may include teaching and administrative duties, up to a maximum of 20% of the working time. The working language is primarily English, but you are expected to acquire basic knowledge of Swedish during the employment period. More information about the doctoral programme is available at: https://www.soclaw.lu.se/en/research/doctoral-studies/phd-handbook General Requirements The requirements for admission to third cycle courses and study programs (in accordance with HF, Chapter 7, Section 35) are that the applicant; meets the general and specific entry requirements that the higher education institution may have laid down, and is considered in other respects to have the ability required to benefit from the course or study program. A person meets the general entry requirements for third cycle courses and study programmes if he or she: has been awarded a second cycle qualification prior to the employment decision, has satisfied the requirements for courses comprising at least 240 credits of which at least 60 credits were awarded in the second cycle, or has acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. Specific Requirements A completed degree at the advanced level in Sociology of Law or another subject deemed relevant by the employer. Doctoral candidates cannot have been awarded a doctoral degree and/or completed more than four years of full-time equivalent research experience. In line with the eligibility criteria and on Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Networks programme, doctoral candidates must not have resided or carried out their main activity (i.e. work, studies) in the hosting country for more than 12 months in the 3 years immediately before the recruitment date. For further information on eligibility criteria and on Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Networks in general, please refer to: Doctoral Networks - Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions . A minimum of 240 credits, of which at least 60 must be at the advanced level. At least 30 credits in Sociology of Law or a related subject at the advanced level, including a thesis of at least 15 credits. Excellent ability to express yourself in spoken and written English. Strong motivation and ability to work independently under pressure. Good collaboration and communication skills. Merits Knowledge of legal sociology, Islamic legal cultures, Islam and gender studies, and legal mobilization scholarship is an asset. Experience with qualitative research methods and fieldwork. Self-motivated, perseverant, and strong writing skills. Collaborative and independent working style. Knowledge of the legal and political contexts of Central Asia, the Middle East and North Africa (MENA) is considered an asset. What we offer A full-time, fixed-term employment for four years. Competitive employment package. Joint supervision and intersectoral placements. Comprehensive training in research methods, ethics, Open Science, and transferable skills. Assessment Criteria Regulations for employment as a doctoral student can be found in the Higher Education Ordinance . Only those admitted to third-cycle studies may be appointed to a doctoral position. In the recruitment process, primary consideration will be given to the applicant’s ability to benefit from the doctoral programme. The research plan, as well as previous theses and published material in Sociology of Law or related subjects within social sciences or law, are important documents for assessing this ability. In addition to pursuing their own doctoral studies, the incumbent may be required to perform duties related to education, research, and administration in accordance with specific provisions in the Higher Education Ordinance . Excellent ability to express oneself in speech and writing is of great importance. As doctoral studies in Sociology of Law are highly demanding, the candidate must be strongly motivated and able to work independently under pressure. Good collaboration and communication skills are also required, as well as strong proficiency in English, both spoken and written. Application The application must include: A cover letter in English (max 1,000 words), including a brief presentation of yourself and your qualifications, as well as a short description of why you are interested in the doctoral programme in Sociology of Law at the Sociology of Law Department, Lund University. A thesis corresponding to at least 15 credits at the advanced level in Sociology of Law or a subject deemed equivalent/relevant, and other relevant publications. If the thesis is written in a language other than Swedish, Danish, Norwegian, or English, a summary of max 1,000 words must be included, outlining the methodology, theory, results/analysis. A CV in English demonstrating eligibility for doctoral studies in Sociology of Law. Degree certificates and transcripts in English. A research proposal of no more than 13,000 characters (including spaces and references), written in English. Please ensure that your proposed research aligns closely with the focus of the PhD project, Women's Legal Agency Across Post-Imperial Islamic Societies in Central Asia, the Middle East, and North Africa . General guidelines for preparing a research plan can be found here: https://www.soclaw.lu.se/en/sites/soclaw.lu.se.en/files/ras_phd_research_plan.pdf Names and contact details of two referees. A writing sample (e.g., master’s thesis or published paper) that demonstrates the applicant’s research and writing skills. Any other documents the applicant wishes to submit in support of the application. Applicants will be assessed based on the above criteria, and top-ranked candidates will be invited for an interview. Gender equality must always be considered. In cases of equal qualifications, the underrepresented gender within the subject at Lund University shall be prioritized, unless valid reasons suggest otherwise. Employment Type The position is full-time (100%) for four years, starting in September 2027. You are required to work on-site in Lund, Sweden. Employment is governed by the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), Chapter 5. Additional Information For questions regarding the MINARET Doctoral Networks Programme and PhD project, please contact Dr. Rustamjon Urinboyev at rustamjon.urinboyev@soclaw.lu.se , Principal Investigator of the MINARET Doctoral Networks programme. For questions about the doctoral programme in sociology of law, please contact Ida Nafstad at ida.nafstad@soclaw.lu.se . For questions about the recruitment process, please contact Ellen Karlsson at ellen.karlsson@sam.lu.se . The Faculty of Social Sciences at Lund University is one of the leading education and research institutions in Sweden and operates both in Lund and Helsingborg. Sociology of law at Lund University is a subject within Social sciences focusing on the relationship between law and society, such as the tension between the formal legislation of the government and the informal emergence of norms in civil society, among other contexts. Research is conducted in fields such as gender and discrimination, AI and machine learning, children's rights, welfare, legal cultures, corruption, migration, financial security and crime. The department offers courses at all levels. The department also runs the bachelor's program in criminology in collaboration with the Department of Sociology. The Sociology of Law Department is keen to engage in cross-disciplinary collaboration and has good contacts with professionals and public authorities. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment 2027-09-01 Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2991 Contact Rustamjon Urinboyev, Associate professor, rustamjon.urinboyev@soclaw.lu.se Ida Nafstad, Associate professor, ida.nafstad@soclaw.lu.se Ellen Karlsson, HR partner, ellen.karlsson@sam.lu.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 16.Oct.2026 Last application date 31.Jan.2027 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://lu.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:980246/": {
      "title": "PhD in Sociology of Law",
      "description": "PhD in Sociology of Law – Securitisation of Religion in Hybrid Regimes Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) PhD in Sociology of Law – Securitisation of Religion in Hybrid Regimes Login and apply Lund University Lund University was founded in 1666 and is repeatedly ranked among the world’s top universities. The University has around 46 000 students and 8 500 staff based in Lund, Helsingborg and Malmö. We are united in our efforts to understand, explain and improve our world and the human condition. Lund University welcomes applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences.  We regard equality, equal opportunities and diversity as a strength and an asset. PhD Position in Sociology of Post-Imperial Islamic Legal Cultures – Securitisation of Religion in Hybrid Regimes: Insights from Central Asia and North Africa Project description This doctoral project investigates how governments in Uzbekistan and Egypt mobilise religious narratives to justify security policies and governance strategies. The doctoral candidate will analyse how religion becomes embedded within state security frameworks and assess the implications of these processes for citizenship, constitutional legitimacy, and state-society relations in hybrid political regimes. To read more about the MINARET project please see: https://www.norca.lu.se/minaret https://www.soclaw.lu.se/en/article/major-eu-grant-lund-led-phd-programme-islamic-legal-cultures Tasks and responsibilities As a doctoral student, you will be admitted to doctoral studies in sociology of law and employed at Lund University. You will: Conduct independent research within the scope of the project. Undertake multi-sited fieldwork in Central Asia and North Africa (Uzbekistan and Egypt) and two mandatory secondments (one academic, one non-academic) abroad. Participate in training events, workshops, and conferences organized by the MINARET Doctoral Network. Collaborate with international supervisors and peers. Contribute to departmental activities, including teaching and seminars (up to 20% of working hours). If selected for the position, you will join NORCA – Nordic Central Asian Studies ( www.norca.lu.se ) research environment at the Sociology of Law Department, led by Rustamjon Urinboyev who will also serve as your principal supervisor. You will be given sufficient time, guidance, and resources to develop your individual research project, aligned with the overall MINARET project's aims. Doctoral Programme in Sociology of Law The doctoral programme in sociology of law comprises 240 credits (equivalent to four years of full-time study) and concludes with a public defence of the doctoral thesis. You will primarily engage in doctoral studies and work on your dissertation within the field of sociology of law. You will also actively participate in the department’s research environment. In addition to research, the position may include teaching and administrative duties, up to a maximum of 20% of the working time. The working language is primarily English, but you are expected to acquire basic knowledge of Swedish during the employment period. More information about the doctoral programme is available at: https://www.soclaw.lu.se/en/research/doctoral-studies/phd-handbook General Requirements The requirements for admission to third cycle courses and study programs (in accordance with HF, Chapter 7, Section 35) are that the applicant; meets the general and specific entry requirements that the higher education institution may have laid down, and is considered in other respects to have the ability required to benefit from the course or study program. A person meets the general entry requirements for third cycle courses and study programmes if he or she: has been awarded a second cycle qualification prior to the employment decision, has satisfied the requirements for courses comprising at least 240 credits of which at least 60 credits were awarded in the second cycle, or has acquired substantially equivalent knowledge in some other way in Sweden or abroad. Specific Requirements A completed degree at the advanced level in Sociology of Law or another subject deemed relevant by the employer. Doctoral candidates cannot have been awarded a doctoral degree and/or completed more than four years of full-time equivalent research experience. In line with the eligibility criteria and on Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Networks programme, doctoral candidates must not have resided or carried out their main activity (i.e. work, studies) in the hosting country for more than 12 months in the 3 years immediately before the recruitment date. For further information on eligibility criteria and on Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Networks in general, please refer to: Doctoral Networks - Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions . A minimum of 240 credits, of which at least 60 must be at the advanced level. At least 30 credits in Sociology of Law or a related subject at the advanced level, including a thesis of at least 15 credits. Excellent ability to express yourself in spoken and written English. Strong motivation and ability to work independently under pressure. Good collaboration and communication skills. Merits Knowledge of legal sociology, Islamic legal culture, security studies and hybrid and authoritarian governance literature. Experience with qualitative research methods and fieldwork. Self-motivated, perseverant, and strong writing skills. Collaborative and independent working style. Knowledge of the legal and political contexts of Central Asia, the Middle East and North Africa (MENA) is considered an asset. What we offer A full-time, fixed-term employment for four years. Competitive employment package. Joint supervision and intersectoral placements. Comprehensive training in research methods, ethics, Open Science, and transferable skills. Assessment Criteria Regulations for employment as a doctoral student can be found in the Higher Education Ordinance . Only those admitted to third-cycle studies may be appointed to a doctoral position. In the recruitment process, primary consideration will be given to the applicant’s ability to benefit from the doctoral programme. The research plan, as well as previous theses and published material in Sociology of Law or related subjects within social sciences or law, are important documents for assessing this ability. In addition to pursuing their own doctoral studies, the incumbent may be required to perform duties related to education, research, and administration in accordance with specific provisions in the Higher Education Ordinance . Excellent ability to express oneself in speech and writing is of great importance. As doctoral studies in Sociology of Law are highly demanding, the candidate must be strongly motivated and able to work independently under pressure. Good collaboration and communication skills are also required, as well as strong proficiency in English, both spoken and written. Application The application must include: A cover letter in English (max 1,000 words), including a brief presentation of yourself and your qualifications, as well as a short description of why you are interested in the doctoral programme in Sociology of Law at the Sociology of Law Department, Lund University. A thesis corresponding to at least 15 credits at the advanced level in Sociology of Law or a subject deemed equivalent/relevant, and other relevant publications. If the thesis is written in a language other than Swedish, Danish, Norwegian, or English, a summary of max 1,000 words must be included, outlining the methodology, theory, results/analysis. A CV in English demonstrating eligibility for doctoral studies in Sociology of Law. Degree certificates and transcripts in English. A research proposal of no more than 13,000 characters (including spaces and references), written in English. Please ensure that your proposed research aligns closely with the focus of the PhD project, Securitisation of Religion in Hybrid Regimes: Insights from Central Asia and North Africa . General guidelines for preparing a research plan can be found here: https://www.soclaw.lu.se/en/sites/soclaw.lu.se.en/files/ras_phd_research_plan.pdf Names and contact details of two referees. A writing sample (e.g., master’s thesis or published paper) that demonstrates the applicant’s research and writing skills. Any other documents the applicant wishes to submit in support of the application. Applicants will be assessed based on the above criteria, and top-ranked candidates will be invited for an interview. Gender equality must always be considered. In cases of equal qualifications, the underrepresented gender within the subject at Lund University shall be prioritized, unless valid reasons suggest otherwise. Employment Type The position is full-time (100%) for four years, starting in September 2027. You are required to work on-site in Lund, Sweden. Employment is governed by the Higher Education Ordinance (1993:100), Chapter 5. Additional Information For questions regarding the MINARET Doctoral Networks Programme and PhD project, please contact Dr. Rustamjon Urinboyev at rustamjon.urinboyev@soclaw.lu.se , Principal Investigator of the MINARET Doctoral Networks programme. For questions about the doctoral programme in sociology of law, please contact Ida Nafstad at ida.nafstad@soclaw.lu.se . For questions about the recruitment process, please contact Ellen Karlsson at ellen.karlsson@sam.lu.se . The Faculty of Social Sciences at Lund University is one of the leading education and research institutions in Sweden and operates both in Lund and Helsingborg. Sociology of law at Lund University is a subject within Social sciences focusing on the relationship between law and society, such as the tension between the formal legislation of the government and the informal emergence of norms in civil society, among other contexts. Research is conducted in fields such as gender and discrimination, AI and machine learning, children's rights, welfare, legal cultures, corruption, migration, financial security and crime. The department offers courses at all levels. The department also runs the bachelor's program in criminology in collaboration with the Department of Sociology. The Sociology of Law Department is keen to engage in cross-disciplinary collaboration and has good contacts with professionals and public authorities. We kindly decline all sales and marketing contacts. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment 2027-09-01 Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Lund County Skåne län Country Sweden Reference number PA2026/2993 Contact Rustamjon Urinboyev, Associate professor, rustamjon.urinboyev@soclaw.lu.se Ida Nafstad, Associate professor, ida.nafstad@soclaw.lu.se Ellen Karlsson, HR partner, ellen.karlsson@sam.lu.se Union representative SACO:Saco-s-rådet vid Lunds universitet, 046-2220000, kansli@saco-s.lu.se OFR/ST:Fackförbundet ST:s kansli, 046-2229362, st@st.lu.se SEKO: Seko Civil, 046-2229366, sekocivil@seko.lu.se Published 16.Oct.2026 Last application date 31.Jan.2027 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
